 Vi\'f1\'ebup\'e4da \'c7r\'e9 \'c7r\'e9mad Bhaktisiddh\'e4nta Sarasvat\'e9 Gosv\'e4m\'e9 Prabhup\'e4da, by whose order I am engaged in this herculean task of writing commentary on the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  as the Bhaktivedanta purports. By his grace we have finished three cantos already, and we are just trying to begin the Fourth Canto. By his divine grace let us offer our respectful obeisances unto Lord Caitanya, who began this K\'e5
\'f1\'eba consciousness movement of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  five hundred years ago, and through His grace let us offer our obeisances to the six Gosv\'e4m\'e9s, and then let us offer our obeisances to R
\'e4dh\'e4 and K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the spiritual couple who enjoy eternally in V\'e5nd\'e4vana with Their cowherd boys and damsels in Vrajabh\'fcmi. Let us also offer our respectful obeisances to all the devotees and eternal servitors of the Supreme Lord.

\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In this Fourth Canto of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  there are thirty-one chapters, and all these chapters describe the secondary creation by Brahm\'e4
 and the Manus. The real creation is done by the Supreme Lord Himself by agitating His material energy, and then, by His order, Brahma, t
he first living creature in the universe, attempts to create the different planetary systems and their inhabitants, expanding the population through his progeny, like Manu and other progenitors of living entities, who work perpetually under the order of t
he Supreme Lord. In the First Chapter of this Fourth Canto there are descriptions of the three daughters of Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu and their descendants. The next six chapters describe the sacrifice performed by King Dak\'f1
a and how it was spoiled. Thereafter the activities of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Dhruva are described in five chapters. Then, in eleven chapters, the activities of King P\'e5
thu are described, and the next eight chapters are devoted to the activities of the Pracetas Kings.
\par As described in the first verse of this chapter, Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu had three daughters, named \'c4k\'fcti, Devah\'fcti and Pras\'fcti. Of these three daughters, one daughter, Devah\'fc
ti, has already been described, along with her husband, Kardama Muni, and her son, Kapila Muni. In this chapter the descendants of the first daughter, \'c4k\'fcti, will specifically be described. Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu was the son of Brahm\'e4. Brahm\'e4
 had many other sons, but Manu's name is specifically mentioned first because he was a great devotee of the Lord. In this verse there is also the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ca,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 indicating that besides the three daughters mentioned, Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu also had two sons.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.1.2
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 TEXT 2
