\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 rucaye}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash unto the great sage Ruci; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 pr\'e4d\'e4t}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash handed over; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 api}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash although; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 bhr\'e4t\'e5mat\'e9m}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash daughter having a brother; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 n\'e5pa\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash the King; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 putrik\'e4}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash 
get the resultant son; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 dharmam}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash religious rites; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 \'e4\'e7ritya}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash taking shelter; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 \'e7atar\'fcp\'e4}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash 
by the wife of Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 anumodita\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash being sanctioned.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\b\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid11288628 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11288628 \'c4k\'fc
ti had two brothers, but in spite of her brothers, King Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu handed her over to Praj\'e4pati Ruci on the condition that the son born of her be returned to him as his son. This he did in consultation with his wife, \'c7atar\'fcp\'e4.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Sometimes a sonless person offers his daughter to a husband on the condition that his grandson be returned to him to be adopted as his son and inherit his property. This is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 putrik\'e4-dharma,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 which means that by execution of religious rituals one gets a son, although he is sonless by his own wife. But here we see extraordinary behavior in Manu, for in spite of his having two sons, he handed over his first daughter to Praj\'e4
pati Ruci on the condition that the son born of his daughter be returned to him as his son. \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kur comments in this connection that King Manu knew that the Supreme Personality of Godhead would take birth in the womb of \'c4k\'fcti; therefore, in spite of having two sons, he wanted the particular son born of \'c4k\'fc
ti because he was ambitious to have the Supreme Personality of Godhead appear as his son and grandson. Manu is the lawgiver of mankind, and since he personally executed the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 putrik\'e4-dharma,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 it is to be accepted that such a system can be adopted by mankind also. Thus, even though one has a son, if he wants to have a particular son from his daughter, he can give his daughter in charity on that condition. That is the opinion of \'c7r\'e9la J
\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.1.3
