 is very significant. Ruci was a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and he executed the brahminical duties very rigidly. As stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 the brahminical qualifications are control of the senses, control of the
 mind, cleanliness within and without, development of spiritual and material knowledge, simplicity, truthfulness, faith in the Supreme Personality of Godhead, etc. There are many qualities which indicate a brahminical personality, and it is understood tha
t Ruci followed all the brahminical principles rigidly. Therefore he is specifically mentioned as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma-varcasv\'e9.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  One who is born of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  father but does not act as a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is called, in Vedic language, a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma-bandhu,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and is calculated to be on 
the level of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and women. Thus in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  we find that }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Mah\'e4bh\'e4rata}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 was specifically compiled by Vy\'e4sadeva for }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 str\'e9-\'e7\'fcdra-brahma-bandhu.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Str\'e9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means women, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdra}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  means the lower class of civilized human society, and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma-bandhu}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means persons who are born in the families of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  but do not follow the rules and regulations carefully. All of these three classes are called less intelligent; they have no access to the study of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 which are specifically meant for persons who have acquired
 the brahminical qualifications. This restriction is based not upon any sectarian distinction but upon qualification. The Vedic literatures cannot be understood unless one has developed the brahminical qualifications. It is regrettable, therefore, that pe
rsons who have no brahminical qualifications and have never been trained under a bona fide spiritual master nevertheless comment on Vedic literatures like the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and other }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Pur\'e4\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  for they cannot deliver their real message. Ruci was considered a first-class }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba;}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  therefore he is mentioned here as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma-varcasv\'e9,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  one who had full prowess in brahminical strength.
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid11288628 
