ecause of this his son-in-law, Ruci, might be sorry. Thus when he heard that a daughter was born along with the boy, he was very glad. Ruci, according to his promise, returned his male child to Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu and decided to keep the daughter, whose name was Dak\'f1i\'eb\'e4. One of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's names is Yaj\'efa because He is the master of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The name Yaj\'efa comes from }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaju\'f1\'e4\'e0 pati\'f9;}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Yajur-veda}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  there are different ritualistic prescriptions for performing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efas,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  and the beneficiary of all such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'ebu. Therefore it is stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 , }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'eba\'f9:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  one should act, but one should perform one's prescribed duties only for the sake of Yaj\'efa, or Vi\'f1\'eb
u. If one does not act for the satisfaction of the Supreme Personality
 of Godhead, or if one does not perform devotional service, then there will be reactions to all his activities. It does not matter if the reaction is good or bad; if our activities are not dovetailed with the desire of the Supreme Lord, or if we do not ac
t in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, then we shall be responsible for the results of all our activities. There is always a reaction to every kind of action, but if actions are performed for Yaj\'efa, there is no reaction. Thus if one acts for Yaj\'ef
a, or the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one is not entangled in the material condition, for it is mentioned in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and also in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and the Vedic rituals are all meant for understanding the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba. From the very beginning one should try to act in K\'e5\'f1
\'eba consciousness; that will free one from the reactions of material activities.
