a-brahma-sambhav\'e4n.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c4tma}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means the Supersoul, or Vi\'f1\'ebu, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e9\'e7a}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means Lord \'c7iva, and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means the four-headed Lord Brahm\'e4. The three sons born of Anas\'fcy\'e4\emdash Datt\'e4treya, Durv\'e4s\'e4 and Soma\emdash were born as partial representations of these three demigods. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c4tma}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is not in the category of the demigods or living entities because He is Vi\'f1\'ebu; therefore He is described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vibhinn\'e4\'e0\'e7a-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  The Supersoul or Vi\'f1\'ebu, is the seed-giving father of all living entities, including Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva. Another meaning of the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4tma}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 may be accepted in this way: the principle who is the Supersoul in every }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4tma,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or, one may say, the soul of everyone, became manifested as Datt\'e4treya, because the word }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 a\'e0\'e7a,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  part and parcel, is used here.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 the individual souls are also described as parts of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, or Supersoul, so why not accept that Datt\'e4treya was one of those parts? Lord \'c7iva and Lord Brahm\'e4
 are also described here as parts, so why not accept all of them as ordinary individual souls? The answer is that the manifestations of Vi\'f1\'ebu and those of the ordinary living entities are certainly all parts and parcels of the Supreme Lord,
 and no one is equal to Him, but among the parts and parcels there are different categories. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Var\'e4ha Pur\'e4\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is nicely explained that some of the parts are }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sv\'e4\'e0\'e7a}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and some are }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vibhinn\'e4\'e0\'e7a.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vibhinn\'e4\'e0\'e7a}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  parts are called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 j\'e9vas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sv\'e4\'e0\'e7a}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  parts are in the Vi\'f1\'ebu category. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 j\'e9va}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 category, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vibhinn\'e4\'e0\'e7a}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  parts and parcels, there are also gradations. That is explained in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vi\'f1\'ebu Pur\'e4\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 where it is clearly stated that the individual parts and parcels who can travel to any part of the Lord's creation, are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sarva-gata}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 and are suffering the pangs of material existence. They are subject to be freed from the coverings of ignorance under material existence according to different levels of work and under different influences of the modes of material
 nature. For example, the sufferings of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 j\'e9vas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  who are situated in the mode of goodness are less than those of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 j\'e9vas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 situated in the mode of ignorance. Pure K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, is the birthright of all living entities because every living entity is part an
d parcel of the Supreme Lord. The consciousness of the Lord is also in the part and parcel, and according to the proportion to which that consciousness is cleared of material dirt, the living entities are differently situated. In the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the liv
ing entities of different gradations are compared to candles or lamps with different candle power. For example, some electric bulbs have the power of one thousand candles, some have the power of 500 candles, some the power of 100 candles, some fifty candl
