kness of the mode of ignorance, such as unclean drunkards who do not regularly bathe. Lord \'c7
iva is so kind that he gives shelter to such creatures and gradually elevates them to spiritual consciousness. Although it is very difficult to raise such creatures to spiritual understanding, Lord \'c7
iva takes charge of them, and therefore, as stated in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord \'c7
iva is all-auspicious. Thus by his association even such fallen souls can be elevated. Sometimes it is seen that great personalities meet with fallen 
