 are no longer interested in understanding the nature of the Supreme Brahman, although a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means one who has attained knowledge about Brahman. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Ved\'e4
nta-s\'fctra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  also it is stated, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ath\'e4to brahma jij\'ef\'e4s\'e4:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 this human form of life is meant for realization of the Supreme Brahman or Absolute Truth, or, in other words, human life is meant for one's elevation to the post of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Unfortunately the modern }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or so-called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 who come in originally brahminical families, have left their own occupational duties, but they do not allow others to occupy the posts of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The qualifications for }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are described in the scriptures, in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and all other Vedic literatures. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is not a hereditary title or position. If someone from a non-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  family (for example, one born in a family of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ) tries to become a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  by being properly qualified under the instruction of a bona fide spiritual master, these so-called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  will object. Such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  being cursed by Nand\'e9\'e7vara, are actually in a position where they h
ave no discrimination between eatables and noneatables and simply live to maintain the perishable material body and its family. Such fallen conditioned souls are not worthy to be called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  but in Kali-yuga they claim to be }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and if a perso
n actually tries to attain the brahminical qualifications, they try to hinder his progress. This is the situation in the present age. Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu condemned this principle very strongly. During His conversation with R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4
ya, He said that regardless of whether a person is born in a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  family or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 family, regardless of whether he is a householder or a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sanny\'e4s\'e9,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  if he knows the science of K\'e5\'f1\'eba he must be a spiritual master. He had many so-called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
\'e7\'fcdra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  disciples like Harid\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura and R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya. Even the Gosv\'e4m\'e9s, who were principal students of Lord Caitanya, were also ostracized from }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  society, but Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, by His grace, made them first-class Vai\'f1\'ebavas.
\par 
