\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, has claimed that He is the father of all living entities, regardless of form. There are 8,400,000 different species of life forms, and Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a claims that He is the father of all. Because the living entities are parts and parcels of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, they are all sons of the Lord, and for their benefit, because they are hovering under the impression that they can lord it 
over material nature, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are given to them for their guidance. Therefore the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 apauru\'f1eya,}
{\cf1\insrsid11288628  for they are not written by any man or demigod, including the first living creature, Brahm\'e4. Brahm\'e4 is not the creator or author of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  
He is also one of the living beings in this material world; therefore he does not have the power to write or speak the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 independently. Every living entity within this material world is subject to four deficiencies: he commits mistakes, he accepts one thing for another, he cheats, and he has imperfect senses. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 however, are not written by any living creature within this material world. Therefore they are said to be }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 apauru\'f1eya.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  No one can trace out the history of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  Of course, modern human civilization has no chronological history of the world or the universe, and it cannot present actual historical facts older than 3,000 years. But no one has traced out when the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  were written, because they were never written by any living being with
in this material world. All other systems of knowledge are defective because they have been written or spoken by men or demigods who are products of this material creation, but }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is }
{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 apauru\'f1eya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  for it was not spoken by any human being or any demigod of this material creation; it was spoken by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, who is beyond the material creation. That is accepted by such stalwart scholars as \'c7a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya, not to speak of other }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  such as R\'e4m\'e4nuj\'e4c\'e4rya and Madhv\'e4c\'e4
rya. \'c7a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya has accepted that N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba and K\'e5\'f1\'eba are transcendental, and in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  also Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba has established, }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhavo matta\'f9 sarva\'e0 pravartate:}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 "I am the origin of everything; everything has emanated from Me." This material creation, including Brahm\'e4 and 
\'c7iva and all the demigods, has been created by Him, for everything has emanated from Him. He also says that (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ) the purpose of all the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is to understand Him. He is the original }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 veda-vit,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or knower of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Ved\'e4nta, }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ved\'e4nta-k\'e5t,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or compiler of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Brahm\'e4 is not the compiler of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid1910093 
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In the beginning of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is established, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 tene brahma h\'e5d\'e4:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the Supreme Absolute Truth, the Personality of Godhead, instructed Brahm\'e4 in the Vedic knowledge through hi
s heart. Therefore the evidence that Vedic knowledge is free from the defects of mistakes, illusions, cheating and imperfection is that it is spoken by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Jan\'e4
rdana, and has thus been followed from time immemorial, beginning from Brahm\'e4. The Vedic religion or the principles of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 have been followed by the highly cultured population of India since time immemorial; no one can trace out the history of Vedic religion. Therefore it is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 san\'e4tana,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and any blasphemy against the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is calculated to be atheism. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7etu,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 which means bridge. If one wants to attain his spiritual existence, one has to cross an ocean of nescience. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are the bridge to cross such a great ocean. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  describe how to divide the human race into four divisions according to quality and working capacity. This is a very scientific system, and it is also }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 san\'e4tana,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 for no one can trace out its history, and it has no dissolution. No one can stop the system of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 var\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4\'e7rama,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or the castes and divisions. For example, whether or not one accepts the name }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 there is a class in society which is known as the intelligent class and which is interested in spiritual understanding and philosophy. Similarly, there is a class of
 men who are interested in administration and in ruling others. In the Vedic system these martially spirited men are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriyas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Similarly, everywhere there is a class of men who are interested in economic development, business, industry and moneymaking; they are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 And there is another class who are neither intelligent nor martially spirited nor endowed with the capacity for economic development but who simply can serve others. They are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdras,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or the laborer class. This system is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 san\'e4tana}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 \emdash it comes from time immemorial, and it will continue in the same way. There is no power in the world which can stop it. Therefore, since this }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 san\'e4tana-dharma}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  system is eternal, one can elevate himself to the highest standard of spiritual life by following the Vedic principles.
\par It is stated that formerly the sages followed this system; therefore to follow the Vedic system is to follow the standard etiquette of society. But the followers of Lord \'c7iva, who are drunkards, who are addicted to intoxicant
s and sex life, who do not bathe and who smoke }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 g\'e4\'efj\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 are against all human etiquette. The conclusion is that persons who rebel against the Vedic principles are themselves the evidence that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 are authoritative because by not following the Vedic principles they become like animals. Such animalistic persons are themselves evidence of the supremacy of the Vedic regulations.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.2.32
