\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 The living entity is constitutionally pure. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Asa\'ec
go hy }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 tm}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ya\'e0 puru\'f1a\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  In the 
Vedic literature it is said that the soul is always pure and uncontaminated by material attachment. The identification of the body with the soul is due to misunderstanding. As soon as one is fully K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious it is to be understood that he is in his pure, original constitutional position. This state of existence is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7uddha-sattva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 which means that it is transcendental to the material qualities. Since this }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7uddha-sattva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  existence is under the direct action of the internal potency, in this state the
 activities of material consciousness stop. For example, when iron is put into a fire, it becomes warm, and when it is red-hot, although it is iron, it acts like fire. Similarly, when copper is surcharged with electricity, its action as copper stops; it a
cts as electricity. It is also confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  that anyone who engages in unadulterated devotional service to the Lord is at once elevated to the position of pure Brahman:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 m\'e4\'e0 ca yo 'vyabhic\'e4re\'eba bhakti-yogena sevate\line sa gu\'eb\'e4
n samat\'e9tyait\'e4n brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate\line }{\cs337\i0\cf1\insrsid11288628  (}{\cs337\i0\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid4929533 Bg. }{\i0\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid4929533 14.26}{\i0\cf1\insrsid11288628 )
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 Therefore }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7uddha-sattva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 as described in this verse, is the transcendental position, which is technically called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Vasudeva is also the name of the person from whom K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a appears. This verse explains that the pure state is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  because in that state }{\i\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid4929533 V\'e4sudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is revealed without any covering. To execute unadulterated devotional service, therefore, one must follow the rules and regulations of devotional service without desir
e to gain material profit by fruitive activities or mental speculation.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 
In pure devotional service one simply serves the Supreme Personality of Godhead as a matter of duty, without reason and without being impeded by material conditions. That is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7uddha-sattva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  because in that stage the Supreme Person, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is revealed in the heart of the devotee. \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9 has very nicely described this }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7uddha-sattva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  in his }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavat-sandarbha.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He explains that }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 a\'f1\'f6ottara-\'e7ata}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  (108) is added to the name of the spiritual master to indicate one who is situated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7uddha-sattva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or in the transcendental state of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is also used for other purposes. For example, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
vasudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  also means one who is everywhere or all-pervading. The sun is also called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva-\'e7abditam.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 may be utilized for different purposes, but whatever purpose we adopt, V\'e4sudeva means the all-pervading or localized Supreme Personality of Godhead. In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is also stated, }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 V\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid4929533 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid4929533 Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid4929533 7.19)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Factual realization is to understand V\'e4sudeva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and surrender unto Him. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vasudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is the field where V\'e4
sudeva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is revealed. When one is free from the contamination of material nature and is situated in pure K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, or in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  state, V\'e4
sudeva, the Supreme Person, is revealed. This state is also called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 kaivalya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  which means pure consciousness. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 J\'ef\'e4na\'e0 s\'e4ttvika\'e0 kaivalyam.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  When one is situated in pure, transcendental knowledge, one is situated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 kaivalya.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Therefore }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vasudeva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  also means }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 kaivalya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  a word which is generally used by impersonalists. Impersonal }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 kaivalya}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is not the last stage of realization, but in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 kaivalya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  when
 one understands the Supreme Personality of Godhead, then he is successful. In that pure state, by hearing, chanting, remembering, etc., because of the development of knowledge of the science of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, one can understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead. All these activities are under the guidance of the internal energy of the Supreme Lord. The action of the internal potency is also described in this verse as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ap\'e4v
\'e5ta\'f9,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  free from any covering. Because the Supreme Personality of Godhead, His name, His form,
 His quality, His paraphernalia, etc., are beyond material nature, being transcendental, it is not possible to understand any one of them with the materialistic senses. When the senses are purified by the discharge of pure devotional service (}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 h\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'eba h\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a-sevana\'e0 bhaktir ucyate}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ), the pure senses can see K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a without covering. Now one may inquire that since factually the devotee has the same material existential body, how is it possible that the same materialistic eyes become purified by devotional ser
vice? The example, as stated by Lord Caitanya, is that devotional service cleanses the mirror of the mind. In a clean mirror one can see his face very distinctly. Similarly, simply by cleansing the mirror of the mind one can have a clear conception of the
 Supreme Personality of Godhead. It is stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, abhy\'e4sa-yoga-yuktena.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  By executing one's prescribed duties in devotional service, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 cetas\'e4 n\'e4
nyag\'e4min\'e4 }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid12541577 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 8}{\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid12541577 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 8}{\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid12541577 )}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or simply by hearing about God and chanting about Him, if one's mind is always engaged in chanting and hearing and is not allowed to go elsewhere, one can realize the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As confirmed by Lord Caitanya, by the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bhakti-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  process, beginning from hearing and chanting, one can cleanse the heart and mind, and thus one can clearly see the face of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par Lord \'c7iva said that since his heart was always filled with the conception of V\'e4sudeva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, because of His presence within his mind and heart, he was always offering obeisances unto Him. In other words, Lord \'c7
iva is always in trance, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sam\'e4dhi.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  This }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sam\'e4dhi}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is not under the control of the devotee; it is under the control of V\'e4
sudeva, for the entire internal energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead acts un
der His order. Of course, the material energy also acts by His order, but His direct will is specifically executed through the spiritual energy. Thus by His spiritual energy He reveals Himself. It is stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9
t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 , }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sambhav\'e4my \'e4tma-m\'e4yay\'e4 }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid12541577 (Bg.}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid12541577  }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 4.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid12541577 6)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c4tma-m\'e4yay\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 means internal potency. By His sweet will He reveals Himself by His internal potency, being satisfied by the transcendental loving service of the devotee. The devotee never commands, "My dear Lord, please come here so that I can see You." It
 is not the position of the devotee to command the Supreme Personality of Godhead to come before him or to dance before him. There are many so-called devotees who command the Lord to come before them dancing. The Lord, however, is not subject to anyone's 
command, but if He is satisfied by one's pure devotional activities, He reveals Himself. Therefore a meaningful word in this verse is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 adhok\'f1aja,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 for it indicates that the activities of our material senses will fail to realize the Supreme Personality of Godh
ead. One cannot realize the Supreme Personality of Godhead simply by the attempt of his speculative mind, but if one desires he can subdue all the material activities of his senses, and by manifesting His spiritual energy the Lord can reveal Himself to th
e pure devotee. When the Supreme Personality of Godhead reveals Himself to the pure devotee, the devotee has no other duty than to offer Him respectful obeisances. The Absolute Truth reveals Himself to the devotee in His form. He is not formless. V\'e4
sudeva is not formless because it is stated in this verse that as soon as the Lord reveals Himself, the devotee offers his obeisances. Obeisances are offered to a person, not to anything impersonal. One should not accept the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d}{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid4021091 \'e9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  interpretation that V\'e4sudeva is impersonal. As stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 prapadyate,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  one surrenders. One surrenders to a person, not to impersonal nonduality. Whenever there is a question of surrendering or offering obeisances, there must be an object of surrender or obeisances.
\par 
