u, who is called Yaj\'efe\'e7a because He is the enjoyer of the fruits of all sacrifice. }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  also confirms this fact. The Lord says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj
\'efa-tapas\'e4m }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 (Bg. 5.29)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He is the actual beneficiary of all sacrifices. Not knowing this fact, less intel
ligent men offer sacrifices for some material benefit. To derive personal material benefit for sense gratification is the reason persons like Dak\'f1
a and his followers perform sacrifices. Such sacrifices are condemned here as a labor of love without actual profit. This is confirmed in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 One may prosecute the Vedic injunctions of offering sacrifices and other fruitive activities, but if by such activities one does not develop attraction for Vi\'f1\'ebu, they are useless labors. One who has developed love for Vi\'f1\'eb
u must develop love and respect for Vi\'f1\'ebu's devotees. Lord \'c7iva is considered the foremost personality amongst the Vai\'f1\'ebavas. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vai\'f1\'ebav\'e4n\'e4\'e0 yath\'e4 \'e7ambhu\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Thus when Sat\'e9 saw that her father was performing great sacrifices but had no respect for the greatest devotee, Lord \'c7iva, she was very angry. This is fitting; when Vi\'f1\'ebu or a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava is insulted, one should be angry. Lord Caitanya, who always preached nonviolence, meekness and humility, also became angry when Nity\'e4nanda was offended by Jag\'e4i and M\'e4dh\'e4i, and He wanted to kill them. When Vi\'f1\'ebu or a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava is blasphemed or dishonored, one should be very angry. Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 krodha bhakta-dve\'f1i jane.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 We have anger, and that anger can be a great quality when directed against a person who is envious of the Supreme Personality of Godhead or His devotee. One should not be tolerant when a person is offensive towards Vi\'f1\'ebu or a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava. The anger of Sat\'e9 towards her father was not objectionable, for although he was her father, still he was trying to insult the greatest Vai\'f1\'ebava. Thus Sat\'e9's anger against her father was quite applaudable.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.4.11
