 (Bg. 9.29) the Lord says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 samo'ha\'e0 sarva-bh\'fcte\'f1u:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  "I am equal to all living entities." Similarly, Lord \'c7
iva is a qualitative incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, so he has almost the same qualities as Him. Therefore he is equal to everyone; no one is his enemy
, and no one is his friend, but one who is envious by nature can become the enemy of Lord \'c7iva. Therefore Sat\'e9 accused her father, "No one but you could be envious of Lord \'c7iva or be his enemy." There were other sages and learned }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  present, but they were not envious of Lord \'c7iva, although they were all dependent on Dak\'f1a. Therefore no one but Dak\'f1a could be envious of Lord \'c7
iva. That was the accusation of Sat\'e9.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.4.12
