scorching sunshine many vegetables and flowers dry up, and many grow luxuriantly. Thus it is the recipient that causes growth and dwindling. Similarly, }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 mah\'e4p\'fcru\'f1a-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 p\'e4da-}{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 p\'e4\'e0subhi\'f9}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 :}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the dust of the lotus feet of great personalities offers all good to the reci
pient, but the same dust can also do harm. Those who are offenders at the lotus feet of a great personality dry up; their godly qualities diminish. A great soul may forgive offenses, but K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a does not excuse offenses to the dust of his feet, just as one c
an tolerate the scorching sunshine on his head but cannot tolerate the scorching sunshine on his feet. An offender glides down more and more; therefore  naturally he continues to commit offenses at the feet of the great soul. Offenses are generally commit
ted by persons who falsely identify with the impermanent body. King Dak\'f1a was deeply engrossed in a misconception because he identified the body with the soul. He offended the lotus feet of Lord \'c7
iva because he thought that his body, being the father of the body of Sat\'e9, was superior to Lord \'c7
iva's. Generally, less intelligent men misidentify in that way, and they act in the bodily concept of life. Thus they are subject to commit more and more offenses at the lotus feet of great souls. One who has such a con
cept of life is considered to be in the class of animals like cows and asses.
\par 
