 "I am Brahman." This realization is auspicious. As long as one does not realize his identity as the soul, whatever he does is inauspicious. }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid12073593 \'c7iva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means 
auspicious, and devotees of Lord \'c7iva gradually come to the platform of spiritual identification, but that is not all. Auspicious life begins from the point of spiritual identification. But there are still more duties\emdash 
one has to understand one's relationship with the Supreme Soul. If one is actually a devotee of Lord \'c7
iva, he comes to the platform of spiritual realization, but if he is not intelligent enough, then he stops at that point, only realizing that he is spirit soul (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 aha\'e0 brahm\'e4smi}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ). If he is intel
ligent enough, however, he should continue to act in the way of Lord \'c7iva, for Lord \'c7iva is always absorbed in the thought of V\'e4sudeva. As previously explained, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sattva\'e0 vi\'e7uddha\'e0 vasudeva-\'e7abditam:}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord \'c7iva is always in meditation on the lotus feet of V\'e4sudeva, \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Thus the auspicious position of Lord \'c7iva is realized if one takes to the worship of Vi\'f1\'ebu because Lord \'c7iva says in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7iva Pur\'e4\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  that the topmost worship is worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. Lord \'c7iva is worshiped because he is the greatest devotee of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. One should not, however, make the mistake of considering Lord \'c7iva and Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu to be on the same level. That is also an atheistic idea. It is also enjoined in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vai\'f1\'ebav\'e9ya Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  that Vi\'f1\'ebu, or N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, is the exalted Supreme Personality of Godhead, and no one should be compared to Him as equal, even Lord \'c7iva or Lord Brahm\'e4, not to speak of other demigods.
\par 
