Do you think that greater, more respectable personalities than you, such as Lord Brahm\'e4, do not know this inauspicious person who goes under the name Lord \'c7
iva? He associates with the demons in the crematorium, his locks of hair are scattered all over his body, he is garlanded with human skulls and smeared with ashes from the cr
ematorium, but in spite of all these inauspicious qualities, great personalities like Brahm\'e4 honor him by accepting the flowers offered to his lotus feet and placing them with great respect on their heads.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 It is useless to condemn a great personality like Lord \'c7
iva, and this is being stated by his wife, Sat\'e9, to establish the supremacy of her husband. First she said, "You call Lord \'c7iva inauspicious because he associates with demons in crematoriums, covers his body with the ashes of the dead
 and garlands himself with the skulls of human beings. You have shown so many defects, but you do not know that his position is always transcendental. Although he appears inauspicious, why do personalities like Brahm\'e4
 respect the dust of his lotus feet and place on their heads with great respect those very garlands which are condemned by you?" Since Sat\'e9 was a chaste woman and the wife of Lord \'c7iva, it was her duty to establish the elevated position of Lord \'c7
iva, not only by sentiment but by facts. Lord \'c7iva is not an ordinary living entity. This is the conclusion of Vedic scripture. He is neither on the level of the Supreme Personality of Godhead nor on the level of the ordinary living entities. Brahm\'e4
 is in almost all cases an ordinary living entity. Sometimes, when there is no ordinary living entity available, the post of Brahm\'e4 is occupied by an expansion of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, but generally this post is occupied by a greatly pious living entity within this universe. Thus constitutionally Lord \'c7iva's position is  higher than that of Lord Brahm\'e4, although Lord \'c7iva appeared as the son of Brahm\'e4
. Here it is mentioned that even personalities like Brahm\'e4 accept the so-called inauspicious flowers and the dust of the lotus feet of Lord \'c7iva. Great sages like Mar\'e9ci, Atri, Bh\'e5gu and the other  nine great sages who are descendants of Brahm
\'e4 also respect Lord \'c7iva in such a way because they all know that Lord \'c7iva is not an ordinary living entity.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In many }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Pur\'e4\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 it is sometimes asserted that a demigod is elevated to such a high position that he is almost on an equal level with the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but the conclusion that Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is the Supreme Personality of Godhead is confirmed in every scripture. Lord \'c7iva is described in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  to be like cu
rd or yogurt. Curd is not different from milk. Since milk is transformed into curd, in one sense curd is also milk. Similarly, Lord \'c7
iva is in one sense the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but in another sense he is not, just as curd is milk although we ha
ve to distinguish between the two. These descriptions are in the Vedic literature. Whenever we find that a demigod occupies a position apparently more elevated than that of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, it is just to draw the devotee's attention to 
that particular demigod. It is also stated in the }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 that if one wants to worship a particular demigod, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is sitting in everyone's heart, gives him greater and greater attachment for that demigod so that he may be elevated to the demigod's abode. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Y\'e4nti deva-vrat\'e4 dev\'e4n }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 (Bg. 9.25)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 By worshiping demigods one can elevate himself to the abodes of the demigods; similarly, by worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead one can be elevated to the spiritual kingdom. This is stated in different places in Vedic literature. Here Lord \'c7
iva is praised by Sat\'e9, partially due to her personal respect for Lord \'c7iva, since he is her husband, and partially due to his exalted position, which exceeds that of ordinary living entities, even Lord Brahm\'e4. The position of Lord \'c7
iva is accepted by Lord Brahm\'e4, so Dak\'f1a, Sat\'e9's father, should also recognize him. That was the point of Sat\'e9's statement. She did not actually come to her father's house to participate in the function, althou
gh before coming she pleaded with her husband that she wanted to see her sisters and her mother. That was a plea only, for actually at heart she maintained the idea that she would convince her father, Dak\'f1
a, that it was useless to continue being envious of Lord \'c7iva. That was her main purpose. When she was unable to convince her father, she gave up the body he had given her, as will be seen in the following verses.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.4.17
