pati, the master of many living creatures and one of the great officers of the great universal affairs, his position was so exalted that Sat\'e9 should accept his good qualities instead of vilifying him. The answer to that argument is that Sat\'e9
 was not vilifying but defending. If possible she should have cut out Dak\'f1a's tongue because he blasphemed Lord \'c7iva. In other words, since Lord \'c7iva is the protecto
r of religion, a person who vilifies him should be killed at once, and after killing such a person, one should give up his life. That is the process, but because Dak\'f1a happened to be the father of Sat\'e9
, she decided not to kill him but to give up her own life in order to compensate for the great sin she had committed by hearing blasphemy of Lord \'c7iva. The instruction set forth here in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  is that one should not tolerate at any cost the activities of a person who vilifies or blasphemes an authority. If one is a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 he should not give up his body because by doing so he would be responsible for killing a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba;}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  therefore a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 should leave the place or block his ears so that he will not hear the blasphemy. If one happens to be a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriya}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  he has the power to punish any man; therefore a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1
atriya}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  should at once cut out the tongue of the vilifier and kill him. But as far as the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 are concerned, they should immediately give up their bodies. Sat\'e9 decided to give up her body because she thought herself to be among the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas.
}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  As stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 , }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 striyo vai\'e7y\'e4s tath\'e4 \'e7\'fcdr\'e4\'f9 }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 (Bg. 9.32)}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Women, laborers and the mercantile class are on the same level. Thus since it is recommended that }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
\'e7\'fcdras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  should immediately give up their bodies upon hearing blasphemy of an exalted person like Lord \'c7iva, she decided to give up her life.
