l who has come to enjoy the material world may do so under direction so that at the end he becomes detached from such material enjoyment and is eligible to enter into the transcendental position. The four different social orders\emdash }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahmac\'e4r}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e9}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 , g\'e5hastha, v\'e4naprastha}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sanny\'e4sa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 \emdash 
gradually train a person to come to the platform of transcendental life. The activities and dress of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 g\'e5hastha}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or householder are different from those of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sanny\'e4s
\'e9,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  one in the renounced order of life. It is impossible for one person to adopt both orders. A }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  cannot act like a householder, nor can a householder act like a }
{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sanny\'e4s\'e9,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  but above these two kinds of persons, one who engages in material activities and one who has renounced material activities, there is the person who is transcendental to both. Lord \'c7
iva is in the transcendental position because, as stated before, he is always absorbed in the thought of Lord V\'e4sudeva within himself. Therefore neither the activities of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 g\'e5hastha}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 nor those of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  in the renounced order can be applicable for him. He is in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 paramaha\'e0sa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 stage, the highest perfectional stage of life. The transcendental position of Lord \'c7iva is also explained in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4, }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid2098204 Second Chapter, verse 52 and 53}{
\i\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid2098204 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  It is stated there that when one fully 
engages in  transcendental service of the Lord by performing activities without fruitive results, one is elevated to the transcendental position. At that time he has no obligation to follow the Vedic injunctions or the different rules and regulations of t
he }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 When one is above the directions of the Vedic ritualistic injunctions for attaining different allurements and is fully absorbed in transcendental thought, which means thought of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in devotional service, that positi
on called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 buddhi-yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sam\'e4dhi,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 ecstasy. For a person who has attained this stage, neither the Vedic activities for realizing material enjoyment nor those for renunciation are applicable.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.4.21
