The yogic process is to control the air passing within the body in different places called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'f1a\'f6-cakra,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the six circles of air c
irculation. The air is raised from the abdomen to the navel, from the navel to the heart, from the heart to the throat, from the throat to between the eyebrows and from between the eyebrows to the top of the cerebrum. That is the sum and substance of prac
ticing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Before practicing the real }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 system one has to practice the sitting postures because this helps in the breathing exercises which control the airs going upwards and downwards. This is a great technique which one has to practice to attain the highest perfectional stage of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  but such practice is not meant for this age. No one in this age can attain the perfectional stage of such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 but people indulge in practicing sitting postures, which is more or less a gymnastic process. By such bodily
 gymnastics one may develop good circulation and may therefore keep his body fit, but if one simply restricts oneself to that gymnastic process one cannot attain the highest perfectional stage. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  process, as described in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Ke\'e7ava-\'e7ruti,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  prescribes
 how one can control his living force according to his desire and transmigrate from one body to another or from one place to another. In other words, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 practice is not meant to keep the body fit because any transcendental process of spiritual realizatio
n automatically helps one to keep the body fit, for it is the spirit soul that keeps the body always fresh. As soon as the spirit soul is out of the body, the material body immediately begins to decompose. Any spiritual process keeps the body fit without 
separate endeavor, but if one takes it that the ultimate aim of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is to maintain the body, then he is mistaken. The real perfection of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 is elevation of the soul to a higher position or the liberation of the soul from material entanglement. Some }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 try to elevate the soul to higher planetary systems where the standard of life is different from that of this planet and where the material comforts, life-span and other facilities for self-realization are greater, and some }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  endeavor to elevate the soul to the spiritual world, the spiritual Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha planets. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bhakti-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 process directly elevates the soul to the spiritual planets where life is eternally blissful and full of knowledge; therefore }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bhakti-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is considered to be the greatest of all }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  systems.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.4.26
