iva, who is one of the three great personalities of Godhead in charge of the management of the material world, and si
mply by meditating on his lotus feet she derived such great pleasure that she forgot everything in relationship with her body. This pleasure was certainly material because she gave up her body for another body that was also material, but by this example w
e can appreciate the devotee's pleasure in concentrating his mind and attention on the lotus feet of the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'ebu, or K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. There is such transcendental bliss in simply meditating on the lotus feet of the Lord that one can forget everything but the Lord's transcendental form. This is the perfection of yogic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sam\'e4dhi,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or ecstasy. In this verse it is stated that by such meditation she became free from all contamination. What was that contamination? The contamination was her concept of the body derived from Dak\'f1
a, but she forgot that bodily relationship in trance. The purport is that when one becomes free from all bodily relationships within this material world and simply places himself in the position of an eternal servant of the Supreme Lord, it is 
to be understood that all the contamination of his material attachment has been burnt by the blazing fires of transcendental ecstasy. It is not necessary for one to manifest a blazing fire externally, for if one forgets all his bodily relationships within
 this material world and becomes situated in his spiritual identity, it is said that one has been freed from all material contamination by the blazing fire of yogic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sam\'e4dhi,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or ecstasy. That is the topmost perfection of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  If one keeps his bodily relationships within this material world and poses himself as a great }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yog\'e9,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  he is not a bona fide }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yog\'e9.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid6370757 Second Canto}{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is stated, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yat-k\'e9rtana\'e0 yat-smara\'eba\'e0 }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 (}{\i\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid6370757 Bh\'e4g}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 . 2.4.15)}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Simply by chanting the holy name of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, simply by remembering the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, simply by offering prayers to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one is immediately freed from material contamination, the material bodily concept, by the blazing fire of ecstasy. This effect takes place immediately, without a second's delay.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 According to \'c7r\'e9 J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9, that Sat\'e9
 quit her body means that she gave up within her heart her relationship with Dak\'f1a. \'c7r\'e9 Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura also comments that since Sat\'e9 is the superintendent deity 
of the external potency, when she quit her body she did not get a spiritual body but simply transferred from the body she had received from Dak\'f1a. Other commentators also say that she immediately transferred herself into the womb of Menak\'e4
, her future mother. She gave up the body she had received from Dak\'f1a and immediately transferred herself to another, better body, but this does not mean that she got a spiritual body.
\par 
