emain. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 T\'e9rth\'e9kurvanti t\'e9rth\'e4ni}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bh}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 g.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 1.13.10). The places are sanctified due to the presence of pure devotees; any place automatically becomes a place of pilgrimage if either the Lord or His pure devotee remains or resides there. In other words, such a pur
