has or spiritual worlds, and impersonal speculators are promoted to the impersonal Brahman effulgence; but it sometimes so happens that a miscreant like Aj\'e4mila is immediately promoted to the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha-loka simply by chanting the name of N\'e4r
\'e4ya\'eba. Although when Aj\'e4mila uttered this vibration he intended to call his son N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba took it seriously and immediately gave him promotion to Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha-loka, despite his background, which was full of sinful activities. Similarly King Dak\'f1a was always engaged in the pious activities of performing sacrifices, yet simply because of creating a little misunderstanding with Lord \'c7
iva, he was severely taken to task. The conclusion is, therefore, that the supreme will is the ultimate judgment; no one can argue upon this. A pu
re devotee therefore submits in all circumstances to the supreme will of the Lord, accepting it as all-auspicious.
