 First Canto, Second Chapter, it is stated that everyone should try to understand whether the Supreme Personality of Godhead is satisfied by his activity. In other words, the aim of our activities should be to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Go
dhead. Just as in an office it is the duty of the worker to see that the proprietor or the master is satisfied, so everyone's duty is to see whether the Supreme Personality of Godhead is satisfied by one's activity. Activities to satisfy the Supreme Godhe
ad are prescribed in the Vedic literature, and execution of such activities is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  In other words, acting on behalf of the Supreme Lord is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  One should know very well that any activity besides }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is the cause of material bondage. That is explained in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  Third Chapter, ninth verse: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'ebo 'nyatra loko 'ya\'e0 karma-bandhana\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Karma-bandhana\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 means that if we do not work for the satisfaction of the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'ebu, then the reaction of our work will bind us. One should not work for his own sense gratification. Everyone should work for the satisfaction of God. That is called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 After the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 was performed by Dak\'f1a, all the demigods expected }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pras\'e4dam,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the remnants of foodstuffs offered to Vi\'f1\'ebu. Lord \'c7iva is
 one of the demigods, so naturally he also expected his share of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pras\'e4dam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  from the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  But Dak\'f1a, out of his envy for Lord \'c7
iva, did not invite \'c7iva to participate in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  nor did he give him his share after the offering. But after the destruction of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  arena by the followers of Lord \'c7iva, Lord Brahm\'e4 pacified him and assured him that he would get his share of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pras\'e4dam.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Thus he was requested to rectify whatever destruction was caused by his followers.
\par In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Third Chapter, eleventh verse, it is said that all the demigods are satisfied when one performs }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Because the demigods expect }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pras\'e4dam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  from }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efas, yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 must be performed. Those who engage in sense gratificatory materialistic activities must perform }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  otherwise they will be implicated. Thus Dak\'f1
a, being the father of mankind, was performing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and Lord \'c7iva expected his share. But since he was not invited, there was trouble. By the mediation of Lord Brahm\'e4
, however, everything was settled satisfactorily.
\par The performance of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is a very difficult task because all the demigods must be invited to participate in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 In this Kali-yuga it is not possible to perform such costly sacrifices, nor is it possible to invite the demigods to participate. Therefore in this age it is recommended, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efai\'f9 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-pr\'e4
yair yajanti hi sumedhasa\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bh}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 g.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 11.5.32). Those who are intelligent should know that in the Kali-yuga there is no possibility of performing the Vedic sacrifices. But unless one pleases the demigods, there
 will be no regulated seasonal activities or rainfall. Everything is controlled by the demigods. Under the circumstances, in this age, in order to keep the balance of social peace and prosperity, all intelligent men should execute the performance of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  by chanting the holy names Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4
ma, Hare Hare. One should invite people, chant Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and then distribute }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pras\'e4dam.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  This }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 will satisfy all the demigods, and thus there will be peace and prosperity in the world. Another difficulty in performing the Vedic rituals is that if one fails to satisfy even one demigod out of the many hundreds of thousands of demigods, just as Dak
\'f1a failed to satisfy Lord \'c7iva, there will be disaster. But in this age the performance of sacrifice has been simplified. One can chant Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and by pleasing K\'e5\'f1\'eba one can satisfy all the demigods automatically.
\par }\pard\plain \s277\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Fourth Canto, Sixth Chapter, of the }{\cs341\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid11288628  entitled "Brahm\'e4 Satisfies Lord \'c7iva."
