iva becomes the best benedictor in spiritual life. It is said that once a poor }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  worshiped Lord \'c7iva for a benediction, and Lord \'c7iva advised the devotee to go to see San\'e4
tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9. The devotee went to San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 and informed him that Lord \'c7iva had advised him to seek out the best benediction from him (San\'e4tana). San\'e4tana had a touchstone with him, which he kept with the ga
rbage. On the request of the poor }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 gave him the touchstone, and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 was very happy to have it. He now could get as much gold as he desired simply by touching the touchstone to iron. But after he left San\'e4tana, he thought, "If a touchstone is the best benediction, why has San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 kept it with the garbage?" He therefore returned and asked San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9, "Sir, if this is the best benediction, why did you keep it with the garbage?" San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 then informed hi
m, "Actually, this is not the best benediction. But are you prepared to take the best benediction from me?" The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  said, "Yes, sir. Lord \'c7
iva has sent me to you for the best benediction." Then San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 asked him to throw the touchstone in the water nearby and then come back. The poor }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 did so, and when he returned, San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 initiated him with the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Thus by the benediction of Lord \'c7iva the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
