rya, and in spite of his committing the great offense of killing all the sleeping sons of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, for which he was condemned even by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Arjuna excused him by not killing him because he happened to be the son of a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma-bandhu\'f1u}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  used here is significant. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Brahma-bandhu}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 means a person who is born of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  father but whose activities are not up to the standard of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Such a person is not a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  but is a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma-bandhu.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Dak\'f1a proved himself to be a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 brahma-bandhu.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  He was born of a great }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  father, Lord Brahm\'e4, but his treatment of Lord \'c7iva was not exactly brahminical; therefore he admitted that he was not a perfect }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord \'c7iva and Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, however, are affectionate even to an imperfect }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord \'c7iva punished Dak\'f1
a not as one does his enemy, but he punished him just to bring him to his senses, so that he would know that he had done wrong. Dak\'f1a could understand this, and he acknowledged the great mercy of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Lord \'c7iva towards the fallen 
}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  including even himself. Although he was fallen, his vow was to execute the sacrifice, as is the duty of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 and thus he began his prayers to Lord \'c7iva.
\par 
