\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 The 
specific function of a human being in society, irrespective of his social status, is to practice control of the mind and senses by observing the regulative principles enjoined in the Vedic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'e4stras.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord \'c7iva is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pa\'e7upati}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  because he protects the living entities in their developed consciousness so that they may follow the Vedic system of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 var\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4\'e7rama.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pa\'e7u}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 refers to the animal as well as to the human entity. It is stated here that Lord \'c7iva is always interested in protecting the animals and the animal-like living entities who are not very advanced in the spiritual sense. It is also stated that the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are produced from the mouth of the Supreme Lord. We should always remember that Lord \'c7iva is being addressed as the representative of the Supreme Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. In the Vedic literature it is described that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are born from the mouth of the universal form of Vi\'f1\'ebu, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriyas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 are born from His arms, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are born from His abdomen or waist, and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are born from His 
legs. In the formation of a body, the head is the principal factor. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are born from the mouth of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in order to accept charity for worship of Vi\'f1
\'ebu and to spread Vedic knowledge. Lord \'c7iva is known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pa\'e7upati,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the protector of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 and other living entities. He protects them from the attacks of non-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or uncultured persons who are against the self-realization process.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 Another feature of this word is that persons who are simply attached to the rit
ualistic portion of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and do not understand the situation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead are not any more advanced than animals. In the beginning of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r
\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is confirmed that even though one performs the rituals of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  if he does not develop a sense of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, then all his labor in performing Vedic rituals is considered to be simply a waste of time. Lord \'c7iva's aim in destroying the Dak\'f1a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  was to punish Dak\'f1
a because by neglecting him (Lord \'c7iva), Dak\'f1a was committing a great offense. Lord \'c7
iva's punishment was just like that of a cowherd boy, who keeps a stick to frighten his animals. It is commonly said that to give protection to animals, a stick is needed because animals cannot reason and argue. Their reasoning and argument is }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 argumentum ad baculum;}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 unless there is a rod, they do not obey. Force is required for the animalistic class of men, whereas those who are advanced are convinced by reasons, arguments and scriptural authority. Persons who are simply
 attached to Vedic rituals, without further advancement of devotional service or K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, are almost like animals, and Lord \'c7iva is in charge of giving them protection and sometimes punishing them, as he punished Dak\'f1a.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.7.15
