iva expresses herein his regret at having been angry and disturbing the sacrificial activities of Dak\'f1a. King Dak\'f1
a had insulted him in many ways, and thus he had become angry and had frustrated the entire sacrificial ceremony. Later, when he was pleased with them, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 performances were reinstituted, and therefore he regretted his activities. Now he says that due to his mind's being fixed on the lotus feet of the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'eb
u, he is no longer disturbed by the ordinary critics of his way of life. From this statement of Lord \'c7iva it is understood that as long as one is on the material platform he is affected by the three modes of material nature. As soon as he is in K\'e5
\'f1\'eba consciousness, however, one is no longer affected by such material activities. One should therefore always be fixed in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, busy in the transcendental loving service of th
e Lord. It is guaranteed that such a devotee will never be affected by the actions and reactions of the three modes of material nature. This fact is also corroborated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Anyone who is fixed in the transcendental service of the Lord has surpassed all the material qualities and is situated in the status of Brahman-realization, in which one is not afflicted by hankering for material objects. The recommendation of the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is that one should always be K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious and should never
 forget his transcendental relationship with the Lord. This program has to be followed strictly by everyone. From the statement of Lord \'c7iva it is understood that he was always in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, and thus he remained free from material affliction. The only remedy is, therefore, is to continue K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness rigidly, in order to get out of the contamination of the material modes.
\par 
