Like an elephant that has suffered in a forest fire 
but can forget all its troubles by entering a river, our minds, O Lord, always merge in the nectarean river of Your transcendental pastimes, and they desire never to leave such transcendental bliss, which is as good as the pleasure of merging in the Absol
ute.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
