vara}{\insrsid11288628 . In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid11288628  it is said that all activities should be performed as }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid14426631 Vi\'f1\'ebu}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa,}{\insrsid11288628  for the pleasure of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. Unless we please Him, whatever we do is the cause of our bondage in the material world. This is confirmed herein by the wife of Dak\'f1
a: "Without Your presence, the grandeur of this sacrificial ceremony is useless, just as a body without the head, howeve
r decorated it may be, is useless." The comparison is equally applicable to the social body. Material civilization is very proud of being advanced, but it is actually the useless trunk of a body without a head. Without K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, without an understanding of Vi\'f1\'ebu, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, any advancement in a civilization, no matter how sophisticated, is of no value. There is a statement in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4
gavatam}{\insrsid11288628 : }{\i\insrsid11288628\charrsid2980245 bhagavad-bhakti-h\'e9nasya j\'e4ti\'f9 \'e7\'e4stra\'e0 japas tapa\'f9 apr\'e4\'ebasyaiva dehasya ma\'eb\'f2ana\'e0 loka-ra\'efjanam}{\i\insrsid11288628 . }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
The purport is that sometimes when a friend or relative dies, especially among lower class men, the dead body is decorated. Dressed and ornamented, the body is taken in procession. That sort of decoration of the dead body has no actual
 value because the life force is already gone. Similarly, any aristocracy, any social prestige or any advancement of material civilization without K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness is as good as the decoration of a dead body. The name of the wife of Dak\'f1
a was Pras\'fcti, and she was the daughter of Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu. Her sister, Devah\'fcti, was married to Kardama Muni, and Kapiladeva, the Personality of Godhead, became her son. Pras\'fcti, then, was the aunt of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. She was asking the favor of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu in an affectionate mode; since she was His aunt, she sought some special favor. Also significant in this verse is that the Lord is praised with the goddess of fortune. Wherever Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is worshiped, naturally there is the favor of the goddess of fortune. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is addressed as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 am\'e5ta,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  transcendental. The demigods, including Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva, were produced after the creation, but Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu existed before the creation. He is addressed, therefore, as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 am\'e5ta.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is worshiped with His internal energy by the Vai\'f1
\'ebavas. Pras\'fcti, the wife of Dak\'f1a, implored the Lord to turn the priests into Vai\'f1\'ebavas instead of simply fruitive workers performing sacrifices for some material benefits.
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 
