The devastation indicated in this verse is the partial devastation of the lower planets within the universe at the time when Lord Brahm\'e4
 goes to sleep. The higher planetary systems, beginning with Janaloka, Maharloka and Tapoloka, are not inundated at the time of this devastation. The Lord is the creator, as indicated in this verse, because the energies of creation ar
e manifested through His body, and after annihilation, He conserves all the energy within His abdomen.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Another significant point in this verse is that the demigods said, "We are all Your servants [}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bh\'e5ty\'e4n}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ]. Give us Your protection." The demigods depend on the protection of Vi\'f1\'eb
u; they are not independent. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 therefore, condemns the worship of demigods because there is no need of it and clearly states that only those who have lost their sense go asking favors of the demigods. Generally, if anyone has material desire to be fulfilled, he can ask Vi\'f1\'eb
u instead of going to the demigods. Those who worship demigods are not very intelligent. Besides that, the demigods say, "We are Your eternal servants." So those who are servants, or devotees of the Lord
, are not very much concerned with fruitive activities, the performance of the prescribed }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or mental speculation. They simply serve the Supreme Personality of Godhead sincerely, with love and faith, performing everything with that loving service, and the Lord gives such devotees direct protection. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, "Simply surrender unto Me, and I will give you protection from all the reactions of sinful activities." This material world is so created that one has to act sinfully, know
ingly or unknowingly, and unless his life is dedicated to Vi\'f1\'eb
u, he has to suffer all the reactions of sinful activities. But one who surrenders and dedicates his life for the service of the Lord has direct protection from the Lord. He has no fear of suffe
ring from sinful activities, nor does he desire, willingly or unwillingly, to do anything which is sinful.
\par 
