 it is said that K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. There may be many gods, from Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7
iva, Indra and Candra down to the rulers of the lower planetary systems, the presidents, ministers, chairmen and kings. In fact, anyone can think that he is God. That is the false, puffed-up conviction of material life. Actually Vi\'f1\'eb
u is the Supreme Lord, but there is even one above Vi\'f1\'ebu, for Vi\'f1\'ebu is also the plenary portion of a part of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In this verse this is referred to by the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 a\'e0\'e7\'e4\'e0\'e7\'e4\'f9,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  which means part and parcel of a part and parcel. There are similar verses in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 which indicate that the Supreme Lord's parts and parcels again expand into other parts and parcels. As described in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  there are many manifestations of Vi\'f1\'eb
u and many manifestations of living entities. Vi\'f1\'ebu manifestations are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sv\'e4\'e0\'e7a,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  partial manifestations, and the living entities are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vibhinn
\'e4\'e0\'e7a.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The demigods like Brahm\'e4 and Indra have been promoted to such exalted positions by pious activities and austerities, but actually Vi\'f1\'ebu, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is the master of everyone. In the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ekale \'e9\'e7vara k\'e5\'f1\'eba, \'e4ra saba bh\'e5tya.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  This means that K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a alone is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and all others, even the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vi\'f1\'ebu-tattva}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and certainly the living entities, are His servitors. Baladeva is the immediate expansion of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. He also engages in the service of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and certainly the ordinary living entities are serving. Everyone is created, constitutionally, for serving K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Here the Gandh
arvas acknowledge that although the demigods may represent themselves as the Supreme, actually they are not supreme. Real supremacy belongs to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 K\'e5\'f1\'ebas tu bhagav\'e4n svayam}{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 is the statement of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  "K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the only Supreme Lord." Worship of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a alone, therefore, includes worship of all the parts and parcels, just as watering the root of a tree also waters all the branches, twigs, leaves and flowers.
\par 
