\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid11288628 The br\'e4hma\'ebas said: }{\fs28\insrsid11288628 
Dear Lord, You are sacrifice personified, You are the offering of clarified butter, You are the fire, You are the chanting of Vedic hymns by which the sacrifice is conducted, You are the fuel, You are the flame, You are the ku\'e7
a grass, You are the sacrificial pots, You are the priests who perform the yaj\'efa, You are the demigods headed by Indra, and You are the sacrificial animal. Everything that is sacrificed is You or Your energy.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In this statement Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u's all-pervasiveness is partially explained. It is said in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vi\'f1\'ebu Pur\'e4\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  that as a fire situated in one
 place emanates its heat and illumination everywhere, so whatever we see within the material or spiritual worlds is also nothing but a manifestation of different energies emanating from the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ' statement is that Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is everything\emdash the fire, the offering, the clarified butter, the utensils, the place of sacrifice and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ku\'e7a.
}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He is everything. It is confirmed herein that the performance of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  in this age is as good as all other }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efas}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  in all other ages. If one performs }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  by chanting Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R
\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare, there is no need to arrange elaborate paraphernalia for the prescribed sacrificial ceremonies recommended in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  In the chant of the holy names, Hare and K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Hare}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means the energy of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 K\'e5\'f1\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vi\'f1\'ebu-tattva.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  Combined together they are everything. In this age, persons are harassed by the influence of Kali-yuga and cannot arrange for all the requisite paraphernalia for performing sacrifice as recommended in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  But if one simply chants Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, it is to be understood that he is performing all kinds of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 because there is nothing within our vision except Hare, the energy of K\'e5\'f1\'eba and K\'e5\'f1\'eba. There is no difference between K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and His energies. Thus since everything is a manifestation of His energy, it is to be understood that everything is K\'e5\'f1\'eba. One simply has to accept everything in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, and he is a liberated perso
n. He should not misunderstand that because everything is K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba has no personal identity. K\'e5\'f1\'eba is so full that in spite of keeping Himself separate from everything by His energy, He is everything. This is confirmed in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Ninth Chapter. 
He is spread throughout the creation as everything, but still He is not everything. The philosophy recommended by Lord Caitanya is that He is simultaneously one and different.
