 it is said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4m:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, or K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, is the supreme enjoyer of all the results of sacrifices, austerities and penances; in whatever one may engage, the ultimate goal is Vi\'f1\'ebu. If he does not know that, a person is misled. As the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u has nothing to demand from anyone. He is self-satisfied, self-sufficient, but He accepts the offerings of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  because of His friendly attitude toward all livin
g entities. When His share of the sacrificial results was offered to Him, He appeared to be very pleased. It is said in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  (9.26), }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 patra\'e0 pu\'f1pa\'e0
 phala\'e0 toya\'e0 yo me bhakty\'e4 prayacchati:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  if any devotee offers Him even a small leaf, or a flower or 
water, if it is done with love and affection, the Lord accepts it and is pleased. Although He is self-sufficient and does not need anything from anyone, He accepts such offerings because, as Supersoul, He has such a friendly attitude toward all living ent
ities. Another point here is that He does not encroach upon another's share. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  there is a share for the demigods, Lord \'c7iva, and Lord Brahm\'e4, and a share for Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. He is satisfied with His own share and does not encroach upon others'. Indirectly, He indicated that He was not satisfied with Dak\'f1a's trying to deny Lord \'c7iva his share. Maitreya addressed Vidura as sinless because Vidura was a pure Vai\'f1\'eb
ava and never committed any offense to any demigod. Although Vai\'f1\'ebavas accept Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu as the Supreme, they are not prone to offend demigods. They give them proper respect. Vai\'f1\'ebavas accept Lord \'c7iva as the best Vai\'f1\'eb
ava. For a Vai\'f1\'ebava there is no possibility of offending any demigods, and the demigods are also pleased with the Vai\'f1\'ebava because they are faultless devotees of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.7.50
