u, and Lord \'c7iva was born out of the body of Brahm\'e4. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is, therefore, the supreme cause. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  also it is stated that in the beginning there was only Vi\'f1\'ebu, N\'e4r\'e4
ya\'eba, but there was no Brahm\'e4 or \'c7iva. Similarly, \'c7a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya confirmed this: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba\'f9 para\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, or Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, is the origin, and Brahm\'e4
 and \'c7iva are manifested after creation. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is also }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4tme\'e7vara,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the Supersoul in everyone. Under His direction, everything is prompted from within. For example, in the
 beginning of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is stated, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 tene brahma h\'e5d\'e4:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He first educated Lord Brahm\'e4 from within.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord K
\'e5\'f1\'eba states, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 aham \'e4dir hi dev\'e4n\'e4m:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is the origin of all demigods, including Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva. In another place in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  K\'e5\'f1\'eba states, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhava\'f9:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 "Everything is generated from Me." This includes all the demigods. Similarly, in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 janm\'e4dyasya yata\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  And in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Upani\'f1ads}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is the statement }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yato v\'e4 im\'e4ni bh\'fct\'e4ni j\'e4yante.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Everything is generated from Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, everything is maintained by Him, and everything is annihilated by His energy. Therefore, by their actions and reactions, the energies which come from Him create the cosmic manifestations, and they also disso
lve the whole creation. Thus the Lord is the cause and also the effect. Whatever effect we see is the interaction of His energy. And because the energy is generated from Him, He is both cause and effect. Simultaneously, everything is different and the sam
e. It is said that everything is Brahman: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sarva\'e0 khalv ida\'e0 brahma.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  In the highest vision, nothing is beyond Brahman, and therefore Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva are certainly nondifferent from Him.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.7.51
