tata\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash therefore; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 padma-pal\'e4\'e7a-locan\'e4t}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash from the lotus-eyed Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 du\'f9kha-chidam}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash 
one who can mitigate others' difficulties; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 te}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash your; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 m\'e5gay\'e4mi}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash I am searching after; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 ka\'efcana}{\insrsid11288628 
\emdash anyone else; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 ya\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash who; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 m\'e5gyate}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash searches; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 hasta-g\'e5h\'e9ta-padmay\'e4}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash 
taking a lotus flower in the hand; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 \'e7riy\'e4}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash the goddess of fortune; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 itarai\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash by others; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 a\'ecga}{\insrsid11288628 
\emdash my dear boy; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 vim\'e5gyam\'e4\'ebay\'e4}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash one who is worshiped.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\b\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid11288628 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11288628 
My dear Dhruva, as far as I am concerned, I do not find anyone who can mitigate your distressed condition but the Supreme Personality of Godhead, whose eyes are like lotus petals. Many demigods such as Lord Brahm\'e4
 and others seek the pleasure of the goddess of fortune, but the goddess of fortune herself, with a lotus flower in her hand, is always ready to render service to the Supreme Lord.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 Sun\'e9ti pointed out herewit
h that the benediction received from the Supreme Personality of Godhead and that received from the demigods are not on an equal level. Foolish persons say that no matter whom one worships one will get the same result, but actually that is not a fact. In }
{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 it is also said that benedictions received from the demigods are all temporary and are meant for the less intelligent. In other words, because the demigods are all materialistically conditioned souls, although they are situated in very exalted 
positions, their benedictions cannot be permanent. Permanent benediction is spiritual benediction, since a spirit soul is eternal. It is also said in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 that only persons who have lost their intelligence go to worship the demigods. Therefore Sun\'e9ti told her son that he should not seek the mercy of the demigods, but should directly approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead to mitigate his misery.

\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Material opulences are controlled by the Supreme Personality of Godhead through His different potenc
ies and specifically the goddess of fortune. Therefore, those who are after material opulences seek the pleasure or mercy of the goddess of fortune. Even the highly placed demigods worship the goddess of fortune, but the goddess of fortune, Mah\'e4-Lak
\'f1m\'e9 herself, is always seeking the pleasure of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Anyone, therefore, who takes to the worship of the Supreme Lord automatically receives the blessings of the goddess of fortune. At this stage of his life, Dhruva Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja was seeking material opulences, and his mother advised rightly that even for material opulences it is better to worship not the demigods but the Supreme Lord.
\par Although a pure devotee does not seek benedictions from the Supreme Lord for material advancement, still it is stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 that pious persons go to the Lord even for material benedictions. A person who goes to the Supreme Personality of Godhead for material gain is gradually purified in association with the Supreme Lord. Thus he becomes free from a
ll material desires and is elevated to the platform of spiritual life. Unless one is raised to the spiritual platform it is not possible for him to completely transcend all material contamination.
\par Sun\'e9ti, the mother of Dhruva, was a farseeing woman, and therefore she advised her son to worship the Supreme Lord and no one else. The Lord is described herein as lotus eyed (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 padma-pal\'e4\'e7a-locan\'e4t}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628 ). When a person is fatigued, if he sees a lotus flower all his fatigue can be immediately reduced to nil. Similarly, w
hen an aggrieved person sees the lotus face of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, immediately all his grief is reduced. A lotus flower is also an insignia in the hand of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u as well as in the hand of the goddess of fortune. The worshipers of the goddess of fortune and Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu together certainly are very opulent in all respects, even in material life. The Lord is sometimes described as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7iva-viri\'efci-nutam,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  which means that Lord \'c7iva and Lord Brahm\'e4 also offer their respectful obeisances unto the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.8.24
