The instruction of Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's mother, Sun\'e9ti, was actually meant for fulfilling his desired objective. Therefore, after deliberate consideration and with intelligence and fixed determination, he left his father's house.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 Both the mother and the son were lamenting Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's being insulted by his stepmother and his father's not having taken any step on this issue. But mere lamentation is useless\emdash one should find out the means to mitigate one's lam
entation. Thus both mother and son decided to take shelter of the lotus feet of the Lord because that is the only solution to all material problems. It is indicated in this connection that Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja left his father's capital city to go to a secluded place to search out the Supreme Personality of Godhead. It is the instruction of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja also that if one is seeking peace of mind he should free himself from all contamination of family life and take shelter of the Supreme Godhead by going to the forest. To the Gau\'f2\'e9ya Vai\'f1\'ebava this forest is the forest of V\'e5nd\'e4, or V
