rada said; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 janany\'e4}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash by your mother; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 abhihita\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash stated; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 panth\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash the path; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 sa\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash that; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 vai}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash certainly; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 ni\'f9\'e7reyasasya}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash the ultimate goal of life; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 te}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash for you; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 bhagav\'e4n}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 v\'e4sudeva\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash K\'e5\'f1\'eba; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 tam}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash unto Him; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 bhaja}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash render your service; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 tam}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash by Him; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 prava\'eba-\'e4
tman\'e4}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash fully absorbing your mind.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\b\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid11288628 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11288628 The great sage N\'e4rada told Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja: The instruction given by your mother, Sun\'e9ti, to follow the path of devotional service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is just suitable for you. You should therefore completely absorb yourself in the devotional service of the Lord.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's demand was to achieve an abode even greater than Lord Brahm
\'e4's. Within this universe, Lord Brahm\'e4 is supposed to be in the most exalted position, for he is the chief of all demigods, but Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja want
ed a realm beyond his. Therefore his desire was not to be fulfilled by worshiping any demigod. As described in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 the benedictions offered by the demigods are all temporary. Therefore N\'e4rada Muni asked Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja to follow the path which was recommended by his mother\emdash to worship K\'e5\'f1\'eba, V\'e4sudeva. When K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a offers anything, it is beyond the expectation of the devotee. Both Sun\'e9ti and N\'e4rada Muni knew that the demand of Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was impossible for any demigod to fulfill, and therefore b
oth of them recommended following the process of devotional service to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 N\'e4rada Muni is referred to here as }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid13398982 
Bhagav\'e4n}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  because he can bless any person just as the Supreme Personality of Godhead can. He was very pleased with Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, and he 
could have at once personally given whatever he wanted, but that is not the duty of the spiritual master. His duty is to engage the disciple in proper devotional service as prescribed in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'e4stras.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  K\'e5\'f1\'eba was similarly present before Arjuna, and even though He could have given him all facilities for victory over the opposing party without a fight, He did not do so; He asked him to fight. In the same way, N\'e4
rada Muni asked Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja to undergo devotional discipline in order to achieve the desired result.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.8.41
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 TEXT 41
