\par ya icchecchreya \'e4tmana\'f9
\par eka\'e0 hy eva hares tatra
\par k\'e4ra\'eba\'e0 p\'e4da-sevanam
\par }\pard \s23\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\insrsid11288628 
\par }\pard\plain \s271\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s268\qj \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 dharma-artha-k\'e4ma-mok\'f1a}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash 
the four principles of religiosity, economic development, sense gratification and liberation; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 \'e4khyam}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash by the name; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 ya\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash who; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 icchet}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash may desire; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 \'e7reya\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash the goal of life; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 \'e4tmana\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash of the self; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 ekam hi eva}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash only the one; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 hare\'f9}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash of the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 tatra}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash in that; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 k\'e4ra\'ebam}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash the cause; }{\cs337\i\insrsid11288628 p\'e4da-sevanam}{\insrsid11288628 \emdash worshiping the lotus feet.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\b\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid11288628 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid11288628 
Any person who desires the fruits of the four principles of religiosity, economic development, sense gratification and, at the end, liberation, should engage himself in the devotional service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead because worship of His 
lotus feet yields the fulfillment of all of these.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid11288628\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid11288628 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 it is said that only with the sanction of the Supreme Personality of Godhead can the demigods offer benedictions. Therefore, whenever any sacrifice is offered to a demigod, the Supreme Lord in the form of }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid7540773 N
\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-\'e7il\'e4}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or }{\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid7540773 \'c7}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid7540773 \'e4lagr\'e4ma-\'e7il\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 is put forward to observe the sacrifice. Actually, the demigods cannot give any benediction without the sanction of the Supreme Lord. N\'e4rada Muni, therefore, advised that even for religiosit
y, economic development, sense gratification or liberation, one should approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead, offer prayers and ask for the fulfillment of his desire at the lotus feet of the Lord. That is real intelligence. An intelligent person nev
er goes to demigods to pray for anything. He goes directly to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the cause of all benediction.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 As Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba has said in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  performance of ritualistic ceremonies is not actually religion. The real path
 of religion is to surrender at the lotus feet of the Lord. For one who is actually surrendered to the lotus feet of the Lord, there is no question of any separate endeavor for economic development. A devotee engaged in service to the Lord is not disappoi
nted in the satisfaction of his senses. If he wants to satisfy his senses, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a fulfills that desire. As far as liberation is concerned, any devotee fully engaged in the service of the Lord is already liberated; therefore there is no separate necessity for his liberation.
\par N\'e4rada Muni therefore advised Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja to take shelter of V\'e4sudeva, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and engage himself in the way that his mother had advised, for that would help him fulfill his desire. In this verse N\'e4
rada Muni has especially stressed the devotional service of the Lord as the only way. In other words, even if one is full of material desires, he can continue his devotional service to the Lord, and all his desires will be fulfilled.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.8.42
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 TEXT 42
