 system is described in summary, and special stress is given to the breathing exercise for stopping the disturbing mind. The mind, by nature, is always oscillating, f
or it is very fickle, but the breathing exercise is meant to control it. This process of controlling the mind might have been very possible in those days millions of years ago when Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja took to it, but at the present moment the mind has to be fixed directly on the lotus feet of the Lord by the chanting process. By chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 one immediately concentrates on the sound vibration and thinks of the lotus feet of the Lord, and very quickly one is elevated to the position of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sam\'e4dhi,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or trance. If one goes on chanting the holy names of the Lord, which are not different from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, naturally his mind becomes absorbed in thought of the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 It is here recommended to Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja that he meditate on the supreme }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 guru}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or supreme spiritual master. The supreme spiritual master is K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who is therefore known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 caitya-guru.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 This refers to the Supersoul, who is sitting in everyone's heart. He helps, as stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  from within, and He sends the spi
ritual master, who helps from without. The spiritual master is the external manifestation of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 caitya-guru,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or the spiritual master sitting in everyone's heart.
\par The process by which we give up our thoughts of material things is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 praty\'e4h\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  which entails being freed from all material thoughts and engagements. The word }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 abhidhy\'e4yet,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  which is used in this verse, indicates that unless one's mind is fixed, one cannot meditate. The conclusion, therefore, is that meditation means thinking of the Lord withi
n. Whether one comes to that stage by the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 a\'f1\'f6\'e4\'ecga-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  system or by the method which is recommended in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 especially for this present age\emdash to constantly chant the holy name of the Lord\emdash the goal is to meditate on the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.8.45
