 is known as the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Dv\'e4da\'e7\'e4k\'f1ara-mantra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  This }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is chanted by Vai\'f1\'ebava devotees, and it begins with }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pra\'ebava,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 o\'e0k\'e4ra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  There is an injunction that those who are not }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 cannot pronounce the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pra\'ebava mantra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  But Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was born a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriya.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He at once admitted before N\'e4rada Muni that as a }{
