 Still, although not a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  but a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Dhruva was allowed, on the authority of N\'e4rada, to pronounce the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pra\'ebava o\'e0k\'e4ra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  This is very significant. Especially in India, the caste }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  ob
ject greatly when persons from other castes, who are not born in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  families, recite this }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pra\'ebava mantra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
