\cf1\insrsid11288628  In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 the Lord personally accepts that anyone, even one of a low species, can be elevated to the highest position and go back home, back to Godhead, simply if he worships properly.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 The prescribed rules, as stated here by N\'e4rada Muni, ar
e that one should accept the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  through a bona fide spiritual master and hear the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 in the right ear. Not only should one chant or murmur the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  but in front of him he must have the Deity or physical form of the Lord. Of course, when the Lord
 appears it is no longer a physical form. For example, when an iron rod is made red-hot in a fire, it is no longer iron; it is fire. Similarly, when we make a form of the Lord\emdash 
whether of wood, or stone, or metal, or jewel, or paint, or even a form within the mind\emdash it is a bona fide, spiritual, transcendental form of the Lord. One must not only receive the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 from the bona fide spiritual master like N\'e4rada Muni or his representative in the disciplic succession, but one must chant the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  And not only 
must one chant, but he should also offer whatever foodstuff is available in his part of the world, according to time and convenience.
\par The method of worship\emdash chanting the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and preparing the forms of the Lord\emdash is not stereotyped, nor is it exactly the sa
me everywhere. It is specifically mentioned in this verse that one should take consideration of the time, place and available conveniences. Our K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement is going on throughout the entire world, and we also install Deities in different c
enters. Sometimes our Indian friends, puffed up with concocted notions, criticize, "This has not been done. That has not been done." But they forget this instruction of N\'e4rada Muni to one of the greatest Vai\'f1\'ebavas, Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja. One has to consider the particular time, country and conveniences. What is convenient in India may not be convenient in the Western countries. Those who are not actually in the line of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4c\'e4ryas,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  or who personally have no knowledge of how to act in the role of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4c\'e4rya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  unnecessarily
 criticize the activities of the ISKCON movement in countries outside of India. The fact is that such critics cannot do anything personally to spread K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. If someone does go and preach, taking all risks and allowing all considerations for time and place, it might be that there are changes in the manner of worship, but that is not at all faulty according to }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
\'e7\'e4stra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  \'c7r\'e9man V\'e9rar\'e4ghav\'e4c\'e4rya, an }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4c\'e4rya}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  in the disciplic succession of the R\'e4m\'e4nuja-Samprad\'e4ya, has remarked in his commentary that }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ca\'eb\'f2\'e4las,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or conditioned souls who are born in lower than }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 families, can also be initiated according to circumstances. The formalities may be slightly changed here and there to make them Vai\'f1\'ebavas.
\par Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu recommends that His name should be heard in every nook and corner of the world. How is this possible unless one preaches everywhere? The cult of Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma,
}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and He especially recommends }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 K\'e5\'f1\'eba-kath\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or the cult of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He recommends that every Indian, considering this task to be }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 paropak\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or welfare activity, take the Lord's message to other residents of the world. "Other residents of the world" does not refer only to those who are exactly like the Indian }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriyas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or like the caste }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  who claim to be }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 because they were born in the families of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The principle that only Indians and Hindus should be brought into the Vai\'f1\'eb
ava cult is a mistaken idea. There should be propaganda to bring everyone to the Vai\'f1\'ebava cult. The K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is meant for this purpose. There is no bar to propagating the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement even among people who are born in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ca\'eb\'f2\'e4la, mleccha}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yavana}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  families. Even in India, this point ha
s been enunciated by \'c7r\'e9la San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 in his book }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Hari-bhakti-vil\'e4sa,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  which is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sm\'e5ti}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 and is the authorized Vedic guide for Vai\'f1\'ebavas in their daily behavior. San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 says that as bell metal can turn to gold when mixed with mercury in a chemical process, so, by the bona fide }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 d\'e9k
\'f1\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or initiation method, anyone can become a Vai\'f1\'ebava. One should take initiation from a bona fide spiritual master coming in the disciplic succession, who is authorized by his predecessor spiritual master. This is call
ed }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 d\'e9k\'f1\'e4-vidh\'e4na.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba states in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vyap\'e4\'e7ritya:}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  one should accept a spiritual master. By this process the entire world can be converted to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par 
