 leaves are very important in the method of worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 salilai\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means "by the water." Of course, Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was worshiping on the bank of the Yamun\'e4. The Yamun\'e4 and the Ganges are sacred, and sometimes devotees in India insist that the Deity must be worshiped with water of the Ganges or Yamun\'e4. But here we understand }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
de\'e7a-k\'e4la}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  to mean "according to time and country." In the Western countries there is no River Yamun\'e4 or Ganges\emdash water from such sacred rivers is not available. Does this mean that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
arc\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  worship should be stopped for that reason? No. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Salilai\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  refers to any water\emdash whatever is available\emdash 
but it must be very clear and collected purely. That water can be used. The other paraphernalia, such as flower garlands, fruits and vegetables, should be collected according to the country and according to their availability. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Tulas\'e9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  leaves are very important for satisfying the Lord, so as far as possible, an arrangement should be made for growing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 tulas\'e9}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 leaves. Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was advised to worship the Lord with the fruits and flowers available in the forest. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a frankly says that He accepts vegetables, fruits, flowers, etc. One should not offer Lord V\'e4sudeva anything other than what is prescribed herein by the great authority N\'e4rada Muni. One cannot offer to th
e Deity according to one's whims but since these fruits and vegetables are available anywhere in the universe, we should observe this small point very attentively.
