\cf1\insrsid11288628  is very significant. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Brahman}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means one who not only is the greatest, but who has the potency to expand to an unlimited extent. How was it possible for Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja to capture Brahman within his heart? This question has been very nicely answered by J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9. He 
says that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the origin of Brahman, for since He comprises everything material and spiritual, there cannot be anything greater than He. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 also the Supreme Godhead says, "I am the resting place of Brahman." Many persons, especially the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers, consider Brahman the biggest, all-expanding substance, but according to this verse and other Vedic literatures, such as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the resting place of Brahman is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, just as the resting place of the sunshine is the sun globe. \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, therefore, says that since the transcendental form of the Lord is the seed of all greatness, He is the Supreme Brahman. Since the Supreme Brahman was situated in the heart of Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, he became heavier than the heaviest, and therefore everything trembled in all three worlds and in the spiritual world.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mahat-tattva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 or the sum total of the material creation, is to be understood as the ultimate end of all universes, including all the living entities therein. Brahman is the resort of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mahat-tattva,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 which includes all material and spiritual entities. It is described in this connection that the Supreme Brahman, the Personality of Godhead, is the master of both }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pradh\'e4na}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 puru\'f1a.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Pradh\'e4na}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  means subtle matter, such as ether. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Puru\'f1a}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 means the spiritual spark living entities who are entangled in that subtle material existence. These may also be described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 par\'e4 prak\'e5ti}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 apar\'e4 prak\'e5ti,
}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  as stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  K\'e5\'f1\'eba, being the controller of both the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 prak\'e5tis,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is thus the master of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pradh\'e4na}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 puru\'f1a.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  In the Vedic hymns also the Supreme Brahman is described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 anta\'f9pravi\'f1\'f6a\'f9 \'e7
\'e4st\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  This indicates that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is controlling everything and entering into everything. The }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628   further confirms this: }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 a\'eb\'f2\'e4ntarastha-param\'e4\'ebu-cay\'e4ntarastham:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He has not only entered the universes, but He has entered even into the atom. In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  K\'e5\'f1\'eba also says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vi\'f1\'f6abhy\'e4ham ida\'e0 k\'e5tsnam.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The Supr
eme Personality of Godhead controls everything by entering into everything. By associating constantly with the Supreme Personality in his heart, Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja naturally became equal to the greatest, Brahman, by His association, and thus became the heaviest, and the entire universe trembled. In conclusion, a person who always concentrates on the transcendental form of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a within his heart can very easily strike the whole world with wonder at his activities. This is the perfection of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  performance, as confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628 . }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Yogin\'e4m api sarve\'f1\'e4m:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  of all }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yog\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bhakti-yog\'e9,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 who thinks of K\'e5\'f1\'eba always within his heart and engages in His loving transcendental service, is the topmost. Ordinary }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  can exhibit wonderful material activities, known as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 a\'f1\'f6a-siddhi,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  eight kinds of yogic perfection, but a pure devotee of the Lord can surpass these perfections by performing activities which can make the whole universe tremble.
