An atheistic argument against the supremacy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead states that if God, the Supreme Person, appears and disappears and sleeps and awakens, then what is the difference between God and the living entity? Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja is carefully distinguishing the existence of the Supreme Personality of Godhead from that of the living entities. He points out the following differences. The Lord is eternally liberated. Whenever He appears, even within th
is material world, He is never entangled by the three modes of material nature. He is known, therefore, as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 try-adh\'e9\'e7a,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the master of the three modes of material nature. In }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  (7.14) it is said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid2842109 daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1\'e4 gu\'eba}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 may\'e9 mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the livi
ng entities are all entangled in the three modes of material nature. The external energy of the Lord is very strong, but the Lord, as the master of the three modes of material nature, is ever liberated from the action and reaction of those modes. He}{
\cf1\insrsid2842109  is, therefore, }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 uncontaminated, as }{\cf1\insrsid2842109 it is }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 stated in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'c9\'e7opani\'f1ad.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 The contamination of the material world does not affect the Supreme Godhead. K\'e5\'f1\'eba therefore says in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 that those who are rascals and fools think of Him as an ordinary human being, not knowing His }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 para\'e0 bh\'e4vam.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid2842109 P}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ara\'e0 bh\'e4vam}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  refers to His being always transcendentally situated. Material contamination cannot affect Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 
Another difference between the Lord and the living entity is that a living entity is always in darkness. Even though
 he may be situated in the mode of goodness, there are still so many things which are unknown to him. But it is not the same for the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He knows past, present and future and everything that is happening in everyone's heart. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  confirms this (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ved\'e4ha\'e0 samat\'e9t\'e4ni}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ). The Lord is not part of the soul\emdash 
He is the unchangeable Supreme Soul, and the living entities are His parts and parcels. The living entity is forced to appear in this material world under the direction of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 daiva-m\'e4y\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 but when the Lord appears, He comes by His own internal potency, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4tma-m\'e4y\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Besides that, a living entity is within the time of past, present and future. His life has a beginning, a birth, and in the conditioned state his life ends with death. But the Lord is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4di-puru\'f1a,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  the original person. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Lord Brahm\'e4 offers his respect to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4di-puru\'f1a,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 Govinda, the original person, who has no beginning, whereas the creation of this material world has a beginning. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Ved\'e4nta}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 janm\'e4dy asya yata\'f9;}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 everything is born from the Supreme, but the Supreme has no birth. He has all the six opulences in full and beyond comparison, He is the master of material nature, His intelligence is not broken under any circumstances, and He stands aloof, alt
hough He is the maintainer of the whole creation. As stated in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid2842109 Ka\'f6ha Up.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  2.2.13), }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 nityo nity\'e4n\'e4
\'e0 cetana\'e7 cetan\'e4n\'e4m.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  The Lord is the supreme maintainer. Living entities are meant to serve Him by offering sacrifices, for He is the rightful enjoyer
 of the results of all sacrifices. Everyone, therefore, should engage himself in the devotional service of the Lord with his life, his riches, his intelligence and his words. This is the original, constitutional position of the living entities. One should
 never compare the sleeping of an ordinary living entity }{\cf1\insrsid2842109 with}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 the sleeping of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the Causal Ocean. There is no stage at which the living entity can compare to the Supreme Person. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers, being unable to 
adjust to all this, come to the conclusion of impersonalism or voidism.
\par 
