\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was cognizant of the defective 
nature of his own devotional service. Pure devotional service is without material form and is not covered by mental speculation or fruitive activities. Pure devotional service is therefore called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 ahaituk\'e9,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  unmotivated. Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja knew that he had come to worship the Lord in devotional service with a motive\emdash 
to get the kingdom of his father. Such an adulterated devotee can never see the Supreme Personality of Godhead face to face. He therefore felt very grateful for the causeless mercy of the Lord. The Lord is so merciful that }{\cf1\insrsid8067757 He }{
\cf1\insrsid13201997 not only}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  fulfill}{\cf1\insrsid13201997 s}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the desires of a devotee who is driven by ignorance and desires for material benefit, but He also gives }{\cf1\insrsid13201997 him}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  all protection, just as a cow gives milk to a newly born calf. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  it is said that the
 Lord gives intelligence to the constantly engaged devotee so that he may gradually approach the Lord without difficulty. A devotee must be very sincere in his devotional service; then, although there may be many things wrong on the devotee's part, K\'e5
\'f1\'eba will guide him and gradually elevate him to the highest position of devotional service.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid11288628 The Lord is addressed herein by Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 puru\'f1\'e4rtha-m\'fcrti,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the ultimate goal of life. Generally }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 puru\'f1\'e4rtha}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is taken to mean execution of a type of religious pr
inciple or worship of God in order to get material benediction. Prayers for material benediction are intended for satisfying the senses. And when one is frustrated and cannot fully satisfy the senses in spite of all endeavor, he desires liberation, or fre
edom from material existence. These activities are generally called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 puru\'f1\'e4rtha.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  But actually the ultimate goal is to understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 pa\'efca-puru\'f1\'e4rtha,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  the ultimate goal of life. Lord Caitanya therefore taught us
 not to ask from the Supreme Personality any benediction such as material wealth, popularity or a good wife. One should simply pray to the Lord to be constantly engaged in His transcendental loving service. Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, being cognizant of his desire for material benefit, wanted protection from the Lord so that he might not be misled or deviated from the path of devotional service by material desires.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid11288628 SB 4.9.18
