reat devotee. Generally, the Lord does not award a pure devotee material opulence, even though he may desire it. But Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's case was different. The Lord knew that he was such a great devotee that in spite of having material opulence he would nev
er be deviated from love of God. This example illustrates that a highly qualified devotee can have the facility of material enjoyment and at the same time execute love of God. This, however, was a special case for Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
