ja is the glory of the Manu dynasty, or the human family. The human family begins from Manu. The Sanskrit word for man is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 manu\'f1ya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  which means "descendant of Manu." Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja }{
\cf1\insrsid4002800 is not only }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 the glory of the family of Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, but he is the glory of the entire human society. Because Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja had already surrendered to the Supreme Godhead, he was especially requested not to do anything unbefitting a surrendered soul.
