The living entities have three kinds of vision, according to their positions in self-realization. According to the bodily concept of life, one sees differentiation in terms of varieties of bodies. The living entity actually passes through many v
arieties of material forms, but despite all such changes of body, he is eternal. When living entities, therefore, are viewed in the bodily concept of life, one appears to be different from another. Lord Manu wanted to change the vision of Dhruva Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja, who was looking upon the Yak\'f1as as different from him or as his enemies. Factually no one is an enemy or a friend. Everyone is passing through different types of bodies under the law of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 karma,}{\insrsid11288628 
 but as soon as one is situated in his spiritual identity, he does not see differentiation in terms of this law. In other words, as stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid10497941 ,}{\insrsid4002800  }{
\i\insrsid11288628\charrsid4002800 brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4\line na \'e7ocati na k\'e4\'eck}{\i\insrsid4002800\charrsid4002800 \'f1ati}{\i\insrsid10497941 /}{\i\insrsid4002800\charrsid4002800  sama\'f9 sarve\'f1u bh\'fcte\'f1u }{
\i\insrsid11288628\charrsid4002800 mad-bhakti\'e0 labhate par\'e4m}{\insrsid4002800\charrsid4002800 (}{\insrsid10497941 Bg. }{\insrsid4002800\charrsid4002800 18.54)}{\insrsid10497941 .}{\insrsid11288628\charrsid4002800 
