da, was already known throughout the universe as a great devotee of the Lord, constantly thinking of His lotus feet. Such a pure, uncontaminated devotee of the Lord is worthy to have all the benedictions that can be o}{\cf1\insrsid15673964 
ffered by the demigods. He doesn'}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 t have to worship the demigods }{\cf1\insrsid15673964 separately for such benediction}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 . Kuvera is the treasurer of the demigods, and he is personally offering whatever b
enediction Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja would like to have from him. \'c7r\'e9la Bilvama\'ecgala \'d6h\'e4kura stated, therefore, that for persons who engage in the devotional service of the Lord, all material benedictions wait like maidservants. Mukti-dev\'e9
 is just waiting at the door of the devotee to offer liberation, or more than that, at any time. To be a devotee is therefore an exalted position. Simply by rendering transcendental loving service unto the Supreme Personality of}{\cf1\insrsid15673964 
 Godhead}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  one can have all the benedictions of the world without separate endeavor. Lord Kuvera said to Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja that he had heard that }{\cf1\insrsid15673964 he}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  was always in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sam\'e4dhi,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or thinking of the lotus feet of the Lord. In other words, he knew that for Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja there was nothing desirable within the three materi
al worlds. He knew that Dhruva would ask for nothing but to remember the lotus feet of the Supreme Lord constantly.
