nly in order to please the Supreme Lord, otherwise one becomes entangled in the resultant reactions. According to the four divisions of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 var\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e4\'e7rama, k\'f1
atriyas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are especially advised to perform great ceremonial sacrifices and to distribute their accumulated money very liberally. Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, as a king and ideal }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  performed many such sacrifices, giving very liberally in charity. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 K\'f1atriyas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are supposed to earn their money and accumulate great riches. Sometimes they do it by acting sinfully. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 K\'f1atriyas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 are meant to rule over a country; Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, for example, in the course of ruling, had to fight and kill many Yak\'f1as. Such action is necessary for }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriyas.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  A }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriya}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  should not be a coward, and he should not be nonviolent; to rule over the country he has to act violently.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11288628 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 K\'f1atriyas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai
\'e7yas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  are therefore especially advised to give in charity at least fifty percent of their accumulated wealth. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 it is recommended that even though one enters the renounced order of life, he still cannot give up the performance of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa, d\'e4na}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 tapasya.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  They are never to be given up. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Tapasya}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is meant for the renounced order of life; those who are retired from worldly activities should perform }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 
tapasya,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  penances and austerities. Those who are in the material world, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 k\'f1atriyas}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cf1\insrsid6511997 the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 vai\'e7yas,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  must give }{\cf1\insrsid6511997 in }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 charity. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Brahmac\'e4r\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  in the beginning of their lives, should perform different kinds of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efas.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, as an ideal king, practically emptied his treasury by giving }{\cf1\insrsid6511997 in }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
charity. A king is not meant simply to realize taxes from the citizens and accumulate wealth to spend in sense gratification. World monarchy has failed ever since kings began to satisfy their personal senses with the taxes accumulated from the 
citizens. Of course, whether the system is monarchy or democracy, the same corruption is still going on. At the present moment there are different parties in the democratic government, but everyone is busy trying to keep }{\cf1\insrsid6511997 t}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628 h}{\cf1\insrsid6511997 eir}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  post}{\cf1\insrsid6511997 s}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  or trying to keep }{\cf1\insrsid6511997 t}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 h}{\cf1\insrsid6511997 eir}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 political party in power. The}{\cf1\insrsid6511997 y}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  have very little time to think of the welfare of the citizens, whom they oppress with heavy taxes in the form of income tax, sales tax and many other taxes\emdash 
people sometimes have eighty to ninety percent of their income taken
 away, and these taxes are lavishly spent for the high salaries drawn by the officers and rulers. Formerly, the taxes accumulated from the citizens were spent for performing great sacrifices as enjoined in the Vedic literature. At the present moment, howe
ver, almost all forms of sacrifice are not at all possible; therefore, it is recommended in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  that people should perform }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa.}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  Any householder, regardless of his position, can perform this }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  without expenditure. All the 
family members can sit down together and simply clap their hands and chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mah\'e4-mantra.}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  Somehow or other, everyone can manage to perform such a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and distribute }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628\charrsid5135716 pras\'e4da}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  to the people in general. That is quite sufficient for this age of Kali. The K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement is based on this principle: chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 at every moment, as much as possible, both inside and outside of the temples, and, as far as possible, distribute }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid7871358 pras\'e4da}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 .}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  This process can be accelerated with th
e cooperation of state administrators and those who are producing the country's wealth. Simply by liberal distribution of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid7871358 pras\'e4da}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 sa\'eck\'e9rtana,}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628  the whole world can become peaceful and prosperous.
\par Generally in all the material sacrifices recommended in th
e Vedic literature there are offerings to the demigods. This demigod worship is especially meant for less intelligent men. Actually, the result of such sacrifice goes to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 , }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4m:}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  He is actually the enjoyer of all sacrifices}{\cf1\insrsid7871358  (Bg. 5.29)}{
\cf1\insrsid11288628 . His name}{\cf1\insrsid7871358  is}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 , therefore, }{\cf1\insrsid7871358  Yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 puru\'f1a.
\par Although }{\cf1\insrsid7871358 he}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  was a great devotee and had nothing to do with these sacrifices, }{\cf1\insrsid7871358 still, }{\cf1\insrsid11288628 to set an example to his people}{\cf1\insrsid7871358 ,}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  }{
\cf1\insrsid7871358 Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  performed many sacrifices and gave all his wealth in charity. For as long as he lived as a householder, he never spent a farthing for his sense gratification. In this verse the word }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 karma-phala-pradam}{\cf1\insrsid11288628  is very significant. The Lord awards everyone different kinds of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 karma}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 as the individual living entities desire; He is the Supersoul present within the heart of everyone, and He is so kind and liberal that He gives everyone full facilities to perform whatever acts one wants. Then the result of the action is also enjoye
d by the living entity. If anyone wants to enjoy or lord it over material nature, the Lord gives him full facilities, but he becomes entangled in the resultant reactions. Similarly, if anyone wants to engage himself fully in devotional service, the Lord g
ives him full facilities, and the devotee enjoys the results. The Lord is therefore known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11288628 karma-phala-prada.
\par 
