a or about K\'e5\'f1\'eba, then gradually he develops the quality of unalloyed love, and by that love only he can conquer the unconquerable. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers aspire to become one with the Supr
eme Lord, but a devotee surpasses that position. }{\cf1\insrsid8457921 A devotee n}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 ot only become}{\cf1\insrsid3086638 s}{\cf1\insrsid11288628 
 one in quality with the Supreme Lord, but he sometimes becomes the father, mother or master of the Lord. Arjuna also, by his devotional service, made Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba his chariot driver;
