\cs375\fs28\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  While King P\'e5
thu thus spoke, the humility of his nectarean speeches pleased the reciters very much. Then again they continued to praise the King highly with exalted prayers, as they had been instructed by the great sages.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1064765 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid1064765\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Here the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 muni-codit\'e4\'f9}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  indicates instructions received from great sages and saintly persons. Although Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5
thu was simply enthroned on the royal seat and was not at that time exhibiting his godly powers, the reciters like the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'fcta,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4gadha}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vand\'e9}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  understood that King P\'e5
thu was an incarnation of God. They could understand this by the instructions given by the great sages and learned }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 We have to understand the incarnations of God by the instructions of authorized persons. We cannot manufacture a God by our own concoctions. As stated by Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu-\'e7\'e4stra-guru:}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  one has to test all spiritual matters according to the instructions of saintly persons, scriptures and the spiritual master. The spiritual master is one who follows the instr
uctions of his predecessors, namely the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhus,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or saintly persons. A bona fide spiritual master does not mention anything not mentioned in the authorized scriptures. Ordinary people have to follow the instructions of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu, \'e7\'e4stra}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 guru.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Those statements made in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 and those made by the bona fide }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 guru}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  cannot differ from one another.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Reciters like the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'fcta}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4gadha}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  were confidentially aware that King P\'e5thu was an incarnation of the Personality of Godhead. Although the King denied
 such praise because he was not at that time exhibiting his godly qualities, the reciters }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid2709631 nonetheless }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
did not stop praising him. Rather, they were very pleased with the King, who, although actually an incarnation of God, was so humble and delightful in his dealings with devotees. In this connection we may note that previously }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
(4.15.21)}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it was mentioned that King P\'e5thu was smiling and was in a pleasant mood while speaking to the reciters. Thus we have to learn from the Lord or His incarnation how to become g
entle and humble. The King's behavior was very pleasing to the reciters, and consequently the reciters continued their praise and even foretold the King's future activities, as they had been instructed by the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhus}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and sages.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.16.2
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 TEXT 2
