\par }\pard\plain \s268\qj \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 na alam}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash not able; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 
vayam}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash we; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 te}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash your; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 mahima}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash glories; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 
anuvar\'ebane}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash in describing; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 ya\'f9}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash you who; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 deva}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash 
the Personality of Godhead; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 varya\'f9}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash foremost; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 avatat\'e4ra}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash descended; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 m\'e4yay
\'e4}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash by His internal potencies or causeless mercy; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vena-a\'ecga}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash from the body of King Vena; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'e4tasya}{
\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash who have appeared; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 ca}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash and; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 pauru\'f1\'e4\'ebi}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash 
glorious activities; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 te}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash of you; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 v\'e4ca\'f9-pat\'e9n\'e4m}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash of great orators; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 api}{
\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash although; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 babhramu\'f9}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash became bewildered; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 dhiya\'f9}{\cs372\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash the minds.

\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3872544 {\b\cf11\insrsid3872544\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid3872544 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs377\fs28\cf9\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The reciters continued:}{
\cs375\fs28\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Dear King, you are a direct incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, and by His causeless mercy you have descended on this earth. Therefore it is not possible for us to actually glorify your exalted activities. Although you have appeared through the body of King Vena, even great orators and speakers like Lord Brahm\'e4
 and other demigods cannot exactly describe the glorious activities of Your Lordship.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1064765 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid1064765\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4yay\'e4}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  means "by your causeless mercy." The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers explain the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 as meaning "illusion" or "falseness." However, there is another meaning of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash that is, "causeless mercy." There are two kinds of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y
\'e4-yogam\'e4y\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mah\'e4m\'e4y\'e4.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Mah\'e4m\'e4y\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 is an expansion of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yogam\'e4y\'e4,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and both these }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4s}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are different ex
pressions of the Lord's internal potencies. As stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the Lord appears through His internal potencies (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4tma-m\'e4yay\'e4}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). We should therefore reject the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da explanation that the Lord appears in a body given by the external potency, the ma
terial energy. The Lord and His incarnation are fully independent and can appear anywhere and everywhere by virtue of the internal potency. Although born out of the so-called dead body of King Vena, King P\'e5
thu was still an incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead by the Lord's internal potency. The Lord can appear in any family. Sometimes He appears as a fish incarnation (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 matsya-avat\'e4ra}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 )}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid4944184 ,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or a boar incarnation (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'e4ha-avat\'e4ra}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
). Thus the Lord is completely free and independent to appear anywhere and
 everywhere by His internal potency. It is stated that Ananta, an incarnation of the Lord who has unlimited mouths, cannot reach the end of His glorification of the Lord, although Ananta has been describing the Lord since time immemorial. So what to speak
 of demigods like Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva and others? It is said that the Lord is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7iva-viri\'efci-nutam}{\cs372\cf9\insrsid4944184\charrsid5197105 \emdash }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
always worshiped by demigods like Lord \'c7iva and Lord Brahm\'e4. If the demigods cannot find adequate language to express the glories of the Lord, then what to speak of others? Consequently reciters like the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'fcta}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4gadha}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  felt inadequate to speak about King P\'e5thu.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 
By glorifying the Lord with exalted verses, one becomes purified. Although we are unable to offer prayers to the Lord in an adequate fashion, our dut
y is to make the attempt in order to purify ourselves. It is not that we should stop our glorification because demigods like Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva cannot adequately glorify the Lord. Rather, as stated by Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, everyone should glorify the Lord according to his own ability. If we are serious and sincere devotees, the Lord will give us the intelligence to offer prayers properly.
\par }{\insrsid14643438 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.16.3
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 TEXT 3
\par }\pard\plain \s276\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s410\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15957092 \b\v\f250\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 AQaaPYaudar\'e9[vSa" Pa*QaaehR\'84re"\line  k-l/avTaarSYa k-QaaMa*Taad*Taa" )
