\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Information is given herein concerning the selection of the king by the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  According to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  system, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eb
as}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are considered to be the heads of the society and therefore to be situated in the topmost social position. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the institution of four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'ebas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4\'e7ramas,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 is very scientifically designed. As stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 is not a man-made institution, but is God-made. In this narration it is clearly indicated that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  used to control the royal power. When an evil king like
 Vena ruled, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  would kill him through their brahminical powers and would select a proper ruler by testing his qualifications. In other words, the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the intelligent men or great sages, would control the monarchical powers. Here we have an indication of how the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  elected King P\'e5thu to the throne as the protector of the citizens. The citizens, being skinny due to hunger, approached the King and informed him that necessary action should be taken. The structure of the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  was so nice that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 would guide the head of state. The head of state would then give protection to the citizens. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriyas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 would take charge of protecting the people in general, and under the protection of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriyas,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vai\'e7yas}{
