\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it is said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pit\'e8n y\'e4nti pit\'e5-vrat\'e4\'f9.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Those who are interested in family welfare are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
pit\'e5-vrat\'e4\'f9.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  There is a planet called Pit\'e5loka, and the predominating deity of that planet is called Aryam\'e4. He is somewhat of a demigod, and by satisfyi
ng him one can help ghostly family members develop a gross body. Those who are very sinful and attached to their family, house, village or country do not receive a gross body made of material elements but remain in a subtle body, composed of mind, ego and
 
intelligence. Those who live in such subtle bodies are called ghosts. This ghostly position is very painful because a ghost has intelligence, mind and ego and wants to enjoy material life, but because he doesn't have a gross material body, he can only cre
ate disturbances for want of material satisfaction. It is the duty of family members, especially the son, to offer oblations to the demigod Aryam\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid6162134 , or}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. From time immemorial in India the son of a dead man goes to Gay\'e4 and, at a Vi\'f1\'ebu temple there, offers oblations for the benefit of his ghostly father. It is not that everyone's father becomes a ghost, but the oblations of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pi\'eb\'f2a}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are offered to the lotus feet of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu so that if a family member happens to become a ghost, he will be favored with 
a gross body. However, if one is habituated to taking the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pras\'e4da}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, there is no chance of his becoming a ghost or anything lower than a human being. In Vedic civilization there is a performance called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7r\'e4ddha}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 by which food is offered with faith and devotion. If one offers oblations with faith and devotion\emdash either to the lotus feet of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu or to His representative in Pit\'e5loka, Aryam\'e4\emdash 
one's forefathers will attain material bodies to enjoy whatever material enjoyment is due them. In other words, they do not have to become ghosts.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
