\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 In the previous verse two significant words are used: }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 asa\'e0sakta\'f9,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  meaning "without attachment," and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 budha\'f9,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 meaning "fully cognizant of everything." By full cognizance it is meant that one should know about his own constitutional position as well as the position of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. According to \'c7r\'e9 Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h
\'e4kura, in this verse Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is describing Himself, or the Param\'e4tm\'e4. The Param\'e4tm\'e4 is always distinguished from the embodied soul as well as the material world. Therefore He has been described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
para.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  That }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 para,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or Supreme Personality of Godhead, is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 eka,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid6581285  meaning one.}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 The Lord is one, whereas the conditioned souls embodied within the material world exist in many varieties of form. There are demigods, human beings, animals, trees, birds, bees and so forth. Thus the living entities are not }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
eka}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  but many. As confirmed in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas:}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nityo nity\'e4n\'e4\'e0 cetana\'e7 cetan\'e4n\'e4m.}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  The living entities, who are many and who are entangled in this material world, are not pure. However, the Supreme Personality of Godhead is pure and detached. Due to being cove
red by the material body, the living entities are not self-effulgent, but the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Param\'e4tm\'e4, is self-effulgent. The living entities, being contaminated by the modes of material nature, are called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sagu\'eba,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  whereas Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nirgu\'eba,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 not being under the influence of the material modes. The living entities, being encaged in material qualities, are }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gu\'eb\'e4\'e7rita,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 whereas the Supreme Personality of Godhead is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gu\'eb\'e4\'e7raya.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  The conditioned soul's vision is covered by material contamination; therefore he cannot see the cause of his }{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid6581285 resultant }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 action and he cannot see his past lives. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, not being covered by a material body, is the witness of all the activities of the living e
ntity. But both of them, the living entity and the Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, are }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4tm\'e4,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or spirit. They are one in quality, yet they are different in so many ways, especially in regard to the six opulences the Supreme Personality of Godhead has in full. Full knowledge means that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'e9va-\'e4tm\'e4,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the living entity, must know both his position and the Supreme's position. That is full knowledge.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.20.8
