 If one works according to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 system and does not desire fruitive results, he gets satisfaction gradually. Discharging one's occupational duty as a means of rendering devotional service unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the ultimate goal of life. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  confirms this as the process of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-yoga.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 In other words, we should act only for the satisfaction and service of the Lord. Otherwise we will be entangled by the resultant actions.
