\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  cannot be bound in devotional service. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Karm\'e9s}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  fully engage in the 
activities of the body. Their aim of life is to give comfort to the body only. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 J\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 try to get out of entanglement by philosophical speculation, but they have no standing in the liberated position. Because they do not take shelter under the lotus feet of the Lord, they fall down from the exalted position of Brahman realization. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Yog\'e9s}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  also have a bodily concept of life\emdash they think that they can achieve something spiritual by exercising the body through }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dh\'e4ra\'eb\'e4, 
\'e4sana, pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4ma,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  etc. A devotee's position is
 always transcendental because of his intimate relationship with the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, to remain always aloof from the actions and reactions of the body and engage in one's real occupation, namely}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid4685630 ,}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  rendering service to the Lord, can }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid4685630\charrsid5197105 only}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid4685630  }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 be possible for devotees.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 

