\par }\pard\plain \s373\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 
To give protection to the general mass of people who are citizens of the state is the prescribed occupational duty for a king. By acting in that way, the king in his next life shares one sixth of the result of the pious act
ivities of the citizens. But a king or executive head of state who simply collects taxes from the citizens but does not give them proper protection as human beings has the results of his own pious activities taken away by the citizens, and in exchange for
 his not giving protection he becomes liable to punishment for the impious activities of his subjects.
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1064765 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid1064765\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
The question may be raised here that if everyone engaged in spiritual activities to attain salvation and became indifferent to the activit
ies of the material world, then how could things as they are go on? And if things are to go on as they ought to, how can a head of state be indifferent to such activit}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid13847189 ies? In answer to this question}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7reya\'f9,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid13847189 "}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 auspicious,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid13847189 "
}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is used here. The division of activities in society as arranged by the Supreme Personality of Godhead was not blindly or accidentally created, as foolish people say. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma
\'eba}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  must do his duty properly, and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriya,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vai\'e7ya}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and even the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  must do the same. And every 
one of them can achieve the highest perfection of life-liberation from this material bondage. This is confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 . }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Sve sve karma
\'eby abhirata\'f9 sa\'e0siddhi\'e0 labhate nara\'f9:}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "By executing one's prescribed duties, one can attain the highest perfection."}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid13847189  (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid13847189 18.45}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid13847189\charrsid5197105 )}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu advised Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5
thu that a king is not enjoined to give up his kingdom and the responsibility of protecting the }{\cs337\i\insrsid3830402 praj\'e4s}{\cs383\insrsid3830402  or citizens}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 to instead go away to the Himalayas for liberation. He can attain liberation while executing his royal duties. The royal duty or the duty of the head of state is to see that the }{\cs337\i\insrsid3830402 praj\'e4s}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or the general mass of people are doing their respective duties for spiritual salvation. A secular state does not necessitate a king or head of state who is indifferent to the activities of the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 praj\'e4s.}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In the modern state the government has many rules and regulations for conducting the duties of the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 praj\'e4s,}{\insrsid5197105 
 but the government neglects to see that the citizens advance in spiritual knowledge. If the government is carele
ss in this matter, the citizens will act whimsically, without any sense of God realization or spiritual life, and thus become entangled in sinful activities.
\par An executive head should not be callous to the welfare of the general mass of people while he simply goes on collecting taxes. The king's real duty is to see that the citizens gradually become fully K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious means completely free from all sinful activities. As soon as there is complete eradication of sinful activities in the sta
te, then there will be no more war, pestilence, famine or natural disturbances. This was actually prevailing during the reign of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira. If a king or head of the government is able to induce the citizens to become K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious, then he is 
worthy to rule over the mass of people; otherwise, he has no right to levy taxes. If the king looks after the spiritual interests of the citizens, he can levy taxes without difficulties. In this way both the subjects and the king will be happy during this
 life, and in the next life the king will be able to share one sixth of the pious activities of the citizens. Otherwise, by levyi}{\insrsid3830402 ng taxes on the sinful citizens}{\insrsid5197105 
 he will have to share the reactions of their sinful activities.
\par This same principle can be appli
ed to parents and spiritual masters as well. If parents simply give birth to children like cats and dogs but cannot save their children from imminent death, they become responsible for the activities of their animalistic children. Lately, such children ar
e
