Now I wish to engage in the service of the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and to serve just }{\insrsid7299173 as the goddess of fortune}{\insrsid5197105  who car}{\insrsid7299173 ries a lotus flower in her hand}{\insrsid5197105 
 because His Lordship, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is the reservoir of all transcendental qualities. I am afraid that the goddess of fortune and I w}{\insrsid7299173 ill}{\insrsid5197105 
 quarrel because both of us would be attentively engaged in the same service.
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1064765 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid1064765\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The Lord is here addressed as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 akhila-p\'fcru\'f1
ottama,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the Supreme Personality of Godhead, }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5507146 who is }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Lord of the entire creation. }{\cs380\i\cf1\insrsid5507146\charrsid5507146 P}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 uru\'f1a}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5507146  means the enjoyer,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 uttama}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5507146  means the best.}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  There are different kinds of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1as}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or enjoyers within the universe. Generally they can be divided into three classes\emdash 
those who are conditioned, those who are liberated}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5507146 ,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and those who are eternal. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the Supreme Lord is called the supreme eternal of all eternals (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nityo nity\'e4n\'e4m}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
). Both the Supreme Personality of Godhead and the living entities are eternal. The supreme eternals are the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5507146 vi\'f1\'ebu-tattva}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and His expansions. So }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nitya}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  refers to the}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5507146  Personality of Godhead}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  beginning from K\'e5\'f1\'eba}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5507146  up}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  to Mah\'e4-Vi\'f1\'ebu, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba and other expansions of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. As stated in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  (}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4m\'e4di-m\'fcrti\'f1u}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ), there are millions and trilli}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5507146 ons of expansions of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  as R\'e4ma, N
\'e5si\'e0ha, Var\'e4ha and other incarnations. All of them are called eternals.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 mukta}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  refers to the living entities who never come within this material world. The }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 baddhas}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are those living entities who are almost eternally living within 
this material world. The }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 baddhas}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are struggling very hard within this material world to become free from the threefold miseries of material nature and to enjoy life, whereas the }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 muktas}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are already liberated. They never come into this material world. Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is the master of this material world, and there is no question of His being controlled by material nature. Consequently, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is addressed here as }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 p\'fcru\'f1ottama,}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the best of all living entities\emdash namely }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vi\'f1\'ebu-tattvas}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'e9va-tattvas.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  It is a great 
offense, therefore, to compare Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'e9va-tattva}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or consider them on an equal level. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers equalize the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'e9
vas}{\insrsid5197105  and the Supreme Lord and consider them to be one, but that is the greatest offense to the lotus feet of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par Here in the material world we have practical experience that a superior person is worshiped by an inferior one. Similarly, }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 p\'fcru\'f1ottama,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the greatest, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, or Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, is always worshiped by others. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja therefore decided to engage in the service of the lotus feet of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja is considered to be an incarnation of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, but he is called a }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e7akty\'e4ve\'e7a}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  incarnation. Another significant word in this verse is }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 gu\'eb\'e4layam,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  which refers to Vi
\'f1\'ebu as the reservoir of all transcendental qualities. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers take the Absolute Truth to be }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 nirgu\'eba}{\insrsid5507146  (without qualities}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
), in accordance with the impersonalistic view, but actually the Lord is the reservoir of all good qualities. One of the most important qualities of the Lord is His inclination to His devotees, called }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 bhakta-vatsala.}{
\insrsid5197105  The devotees are always very much inclined to render service unto the lotus feet of the Lord, and the Lord is also very much inclined to accept loving service 
from His devotees. In that exchange of service there are many transcendental transactions, which are called transcendental qualitative activities. Some of the transcendental qualities of the Lord are that He is omniscient, omnipresent, all-pervasive, all-
powerful, the cause of all causes, the Absolute Truth, the reservoir of all pleasures, the reservoir of all knowledge, the all-auspicious and so on.
\par P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja desired to serve the Lord with the goddess of fortune, but this desire does not mean that he was situated on the platform of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 m\'e4dhurya-rasa.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 The goddess of fortune is engaged in}{\insrsid5507146  the service of the Lord in the}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 m\'e4dhurya}{\cs337\i\insrsid5507146 -rasa }{\insrsid5507146\charrsid5197105 of}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  conjugal love. Although her position is on the chest of the Lord, the goddess of fortune, in her position as a devotee, takes pleasure in serving the lotus feet of the Lord. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was thinking only of the lotus feet of the Lord because he is on the platform of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 d\'e4sya-rasa}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or servitorship of the Lord. From the next verse we learn that P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was thinking of the goddess of fortune as the universal mother, }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 jagan-m\'e4t\'e4.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Consequently there was no question of his competing with her on the platform of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 m
\'e4dhurya-rasa.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Nonetheless he feared that she might take offense at his engaging in the service of the Lord. This suggest
s that in the absolute world there is sometimes competition between servitors in the service of the Lord, but such competition is without malice. In the Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha worlds if a devotee excels in the service of the Lord, others do not become envious of his excellent service but rather aspire to come to the platform of that service.}{\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
