\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Mother Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9, the goddess of fortune, is well known for alwa
ys massaging the lotus feet of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. She is an ideal wife because she takes care of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba in every detail. She }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid2510553\charrsid5197105 not only}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid2510553  }{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 takes care of His lotus feet but of the household affairs of the Lord as well. She cooks nice foods for Him, fans Him while He eats, smoothes sandalwood pulp on His face}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid2510553 ,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and sets His bed and sitting places in the right order. In this way she is always engaged in the service of the Lord, and there is hardly any opportunity for any other devotee to intrude upon His daily ac
tivities. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was therefore almost certain that his intrusion into the service of the goddess of fortune would irritate her and cause her to become angry with him. But why should mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the mother of the universe, be angry with an insignificant devotee like P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja? All this was not very likely. Yet P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, just for his personal protection, appealed to the Lord to take his part. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was engaged in performing the ordinary Vedic rituals and sacrifices according to }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or fruitive activities, but the Lord, being so kind and magnanimous, was ready to award P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja the highest perfectional stage of life, namely devotional service.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 When a person performs Vedic rituals and sacrifices, he does so to elevat
e himself to the heavenly planets. No one can become qualified to go back home, back to Godhead, by means of such sacrifices. But the Lord is so kind that He accepts a little insignificant service, and therefore it is stated in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vi\'f1\'ebu Pur\'e4\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  that by following the principles of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 one can satisfy the Supreme Lord. When the Lord is satisfied, the performer of sacrifices is elevated to the platform of devotional service. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja therefore expected that his insignificant service to the 
Lord would be accepted by Him as being greater than that of Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9. The goddess of fortune is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ca\'efcal\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid876056  (restless}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
) because she is very restless and is always coming and go}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid876056 ing. So P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja indicates}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  that even though she might go away out of anger, there would be no harm for Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu, because He is self-sufficient and can do anything and everything without the help of Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9. For example, when Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu begot Lor}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid876056 d Brahm\'e4 from His navel, He didn'}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 t take any help from Lak\'f1m\'e9, who was 
just sitting by Him and massaging His lotus feet. Generally if a son is to be begotten, the husband impregnates the wife, and in due course of time the son is born. But in the case of Lord Brahm\'e4's birth, Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'eb
u did not impregnate Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9. Being self-sufficient, the Lord begot Brahm\'e4 from His own nav}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid876056 el. Therefore, P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja i}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
s confident that even if the goddess of fortune became angry with him there would be no harm, neither to the Lord nor to himself.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
