The sum and substance of religious life is to execute the orders of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and one who does so is perfectly religious. In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the Supreme Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 man-man\'e4 bhava mad-bhakta\'f9:}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "Just think of Me always and become My devotee." }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid10179230 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid10179230 
18.65}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid10179230\charrsid5197105 ) }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Furthermore, the Lord says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "Give up all kinds of material engagement and simply surrender unto Me." }{\cf1\insrsid10179230 (}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bg. 18.66}{\cf1\insrsid10179230 )}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 This is the primary principle of religion. Anyone who directly executes such an order from the Personality of Godhead is actually a religious person. Others are described as pretenders, for there are many
 activities going on throughout the world in the name of religion which are not actually religious. For one who executes the order of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, however, there is only good fortune throughout the world.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105 

