pratinandy\'e4rthavad vaca\'f9,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  which indicate that the Lord appreciat
ed the very meaningful prayers of the King. When a devotee prays to the Lord, it is not to ask for material benefits but to ask the Lord for His favor; he prays that he may be engaged in the service of the Lord's lotus feet birth after birth. Lord Caitany
a therefore uses the words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mama janmani janmani,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 which mean "birth after birth," because a devotee is not even interested in stopping the repetition of birth. The Lord and the devotee appear in this material world birth after birth, but such births are transcendental. In the Fourth Chapter of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the Lord informed Arjuna that both He and Arjuna had undergone many, many births previously, but the Lord remembered everything about them whereas Arjuna had forgotten. The Lord and His confidential devote
es appear many times to fulfill the Lord's mission, but since such births are transcendental, they are not accompanied by the miserable conditions of material birth, and they are therefore called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 divya,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  transcendental.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 One must understand the transcendenta
l birth of the Lord and the devotee. The purpose of the Lord's taking birth is to establish devotional service, which is the perfect system of religion, and the purpose of the birth of a devotee is to broadcast the same system of religion, or the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  cult, all over the world. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was an incarnation of the power of the Lord to spread the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  cult, and the Lord blessed him to remain fixed in his position. Thus when the King refused to accept any material benediction, the Lord appreciated that
 refusal very much. Another significant word in this verse is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 acyuta,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 which means "infallible." Although the Lord appears in this material world, He is never to be considered one of the conditioned souls, who are all fallible. When the Lord appears, He rem
ains in His spiritual position, uncontaminated by the modes of material nature, and therefore in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the Lord expresses the quality of His appearance as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4tma-m\'e4yay\'e4,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "performed by internal potency." The Lord, being infallible, is not forced by ma
terial nature to take birth in this material world. He appears in order to reestablish the perfect order of religious principles and to vanquish the demoniac influence in human society.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.20.35, SB 4.20.36, SB 4.20.35-36
