The terms "pious" and "impious" are applicable only in reference to the activities of an ordinary living being. But Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu was a directly empowered incarnation of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu; therefore he w
as not subject to the reactions of pious or impious activities. As we have already explained previously, when a living being is specifically empowered by the Supreme Lord to act for a particular purpose, he is called a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7
akty\'e4ve\'e7a-avat\'e4ra.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was not only a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7akty\'e4ve\'e7a-avat\'e4ra}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
