i nirdahati kintu ca bhakti-bh\'e4j\'e4m:}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  for devotees the results of past pious and impious activities are nullified by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4rabdh\'e4
n eva}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  mean "as if achieved by past deeds," but in the case of P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja there was no question of reaction to past deeds, and thus the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 eva}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is used here to indicate comparison to ordinary persons. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the Lord says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 avaj\'e4
nanti m\'e4\'e0 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\'f9.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  This means that sometimes people misunderstand an incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead to be an ordinary man. The Supreme Godhead, His incarnations or His dev
otees may pose themselves as ordinary men, but they are never to be considered as such. Nor should an ordinary man not supported by authorized statements of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  be accepted as an incarnation or devotee. By the evidence of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4
m\'e9 detected Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu to be a direct incarnation of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, although Lord Caitanya never disclosed the fact. It is therefore generally recommended that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4
c\'e4rya}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 guru}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  should not be accepted as an ordinary man.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105 
