 ("all great souls") is very significant. When a person is very great and famous, many unscrupulous persons become his enemies, for envy is the nature of materialists. In any meeting there are different classes of 
men, and it is to be supposed, therefore, that because P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was very great, he must have had several enemies present in the assembly, although they could not express themselves. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5
