A king is supposed to be appointed by the Supreme Personality of Godhead to look after the interests of his particular planet. On every planet there is a predominating person, just as we now
 see that in every country there is a president. If one is president or king, it should be understood that this opportunity has been given to him by the Supreme Lord. According to the Vedic system, the king is considered a representative of Godhead and is
 
offered respects by the citizens as God in the human form of life. Actually, according to Vedic information, the Supreme Lord maintains all living entities, and especially human beings, to elevate them to the highest perfection. After many, many births in
 lower species, when a living entity evolves to the human form of life and in particular to the civilized human form of life, his society must be divided into four gradations, as ordered by the Supreme Personality of Godhead in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid7687818 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 c\'e4tur-var\'ebya\'e0 may\'e4 s\'e5\'f1\'f6am,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 etc.). The four social orders\emdash the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
\emdash are natural divisions of human society, and}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid7687818 ,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  as declared by P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
