kingdom was to raise the citizens to the standard of God consciousness. Since there was a great assembly in the arena of sacrifice, there were different types of men present, but he was especially interested in speaking to those who were not atheists. It 
has already been explained in the previous verses that P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja advised the citizens to become }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 adhok\'f1aja-dhiya\'f9,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid12331916  which means God conscious}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious, and in this verse he specifically presents the authority of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  even though his father w
as a number one atheist who did not abide by the injunctions mentioned in the Vedic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  who practically stopped all sacrificial performances}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid12331916 ,
}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and who so disgusted the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  that they not only dethroned him but cursed and killed him. Atheistic men 
do not believe in the existence of God, and thus they understand everything which is happening in our daily affairs to be due to physical arrangement and chance. Atheists believe in the atheistic S\'e4\'eckhya philosophy of the combination of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prak\'e5ti}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1a.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 They believe only in matter and hold that matter under certain conditions of amalgamation gives rise to the living force, which then appears as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1a,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the enjoyer; then, by a combination of matter and the living force, the many varieties of material manifestation come into existence. Nor do atheists believe in the injunctions of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  According to them, all the Vedic injunctions are simply theories that have no practical application in life. Taking all this into consideration, P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja suggeste
d that theistic men will solidly reject the views of the atheists on the grounds that there cannot be many varieties of existence without the plan of a superior intelligence. Atheists very vaguely explain that these varieties of existence occur simply by 
chance, but the theists who believe in the injunctions of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  must reach all their conclusions under the direction of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vi\'f1\'ebu Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it is said that the entire }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  institution is meant to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhe
ad. The rules and regulations set up for the execution of the duties of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdras}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmac\'e4r\'e9s, g\'e5hasthas, v\'e4naprasthas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sanny\'e4s\'e9s}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are all meant to satisfy the Supreme Lord. At the present moment, although the so-called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  have lost their original culture, they claim to be }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  by birthright. Yet they have rejected the proposition that such social and spiritual orders are especially meant for worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. The dangerous M
\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da theory set forth by \'c7a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya\emdash that God is impersonal\emdash does not tally with the injunctions of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu therefore described the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers as the greatest offenders against the Personality of Godhead. According to the Vedic system, one who does not abide by the orders of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is called a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 n\'e4stika,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or atheist. When Lord Buddha preached his theory of nonviolence, he was obliged to deny the authority of the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and for this reason he was considered by the followers of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  to be a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 n\'e4stika.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  But although \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu very clearly enunciated that the followers of Lord Buddha's philosophy are }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid12331916 n\'e4stikas}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid12331916  or atheists}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  because of their denial of the authority of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  He considered the \'c7a\'ec
karites, who wanted to establish Vedic authority by trickery and who actually followed the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da philosophy of Buddha's school, to be more dangerous than the Buddhists themselves. The \'c7a\'eckarite philosophers' theory that we have to 
imagine a shape of God is more dangerous than denial of the existence of God. Notwithstanding all the philosophical theorizing by atheists or M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s, the followers of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness rigidly live according to the injunctions given in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  which is accepted as the essence of all Vedic scripture. In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it is said:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid12911530 yata\'f9 prav\'e5ttir bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0 }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 yena sarvam ida
\'e0 }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12911530 tatam\line sva-karma\'eb\'e4 tam abhyarcya }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 siddhi\'e0 vindati m\'e4nava\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid12911530  }{\cs383\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid12911530\charrsid12911530 (Bg. }{
\i0\cf1\insrsid12911530\charrsid12911530 18.46}{\cs383\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid12911530\charrsid12911530 )}{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid12911530 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12911530 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 This }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid12911530 means}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the original source of everything, as described in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  (}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 janm\'e4dy asya yata\'f9}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). The Lord Himself also confirms in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid12911530 aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhava\'f9:}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "I am the origin of everything." The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the original source of all emanations, and at the same time, as Param\'e4tm\'e4
, He is spread all over existence. The Absolute Truth is therefore the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and every living being is meant to satisfy the Supreme Godhead by performing his respective duty (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid12911530 sva-karma\'eb\'e4
 tam abhyarcya}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu wanted to introduce this formula amongst his citizens.}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid12911530 
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
The most important point in human civilization is that while one engages in different occupational duties, he must try to satisfy the Supreme Lord by the execution of such duties. That is the highest perfection of life. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Svanu\'f1
\'f6hitasya dharmasya sa\'e0siddhir hari-to\'f1a\'ebam:}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  by discharging one's prescribed duty, one can become very successful in life if he simply satisfies the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The vivid exampl
e is Arjuna. He was a }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriya,}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  his duty was to fight, and by executing his prescribed duty he satisfied the Supreme Lord and therefore became perfect. Everyone should foll}{
\cs383\insrsid12911530 ow this principle. The atheists who do not}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are condemned in }{\cs347\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs347\i\insrsid12911530 , }{\cs347\insrsid12911530\charrsid12911530 in the Si
xteenth Chapter}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  by the following statement: }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 t\'e4n aha\'e0 dvi\'f1ata\'f9 kr\'fcr\'e4n sa\'e0s\'e4re\'f1u nar\'e4dham\'e4n}{\cs337\i\insrsid12911530  }{\cs383\insrsid12911530 (Bg. }{
\insrsid12911530 16.19}{\cs383\insrsid12911530\charrsid5197105 )}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 .}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 In this verse it is clearly said that persons who are envious of the Supreme Personality of Godhead are the lowest of mankind and are very mischievous. U
nder the regulative principles of the Supreme, such mischievous persons are thrown into the darkest region of material existence and are born of }{\cs337\i\insrsid12911530 asuras}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or atheists. Birth after birth, such }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 asuras}{\insrsid5197105  go still further down, finally to animal forms like those of
 tigers or similar ferocious beasts. Thus for millions of years they have to remain in darkness without knowledge of K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par The Supreme Personality of Godhead is known as Puru\'f1ottama, or the best of all living entities. He is a person like all other living entities, but He is the leader or the best of all living beings. That is stated in the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas}
{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  also. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Nityo nity\'e4n\'e4\'e0 cetana\'e7 cetan\'e4n\'e4m.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 He is the chief of all eternals, the chief of all living entities, and He is complete and full. He has no need to derive b
enefit by interfering with the affairs of other living entities, but because He is the maintainer of all, He has the right to bring them to the proper standard so that all living entities may become happy. A}{\insrsid16336427 s a}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  father wants all of his children to become happy under his direction}{\insrsid16336427 , s}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 imilarly, God, or K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, has the right to see that all living entities are happy. There is no possibility of becoming happy within this material world. The father and the sons are eternal, but i
f a living entity does not come to the platform of his eternal life of bliss and knowledge, there is no question of happiness. Although Puru\'f1
ottama, the best of all living entities, has no benefit to derive from the common living entities, He does have the
 right to discriminate between their right and wrong ways. The right way is the path of activities meant to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as we have already discussed (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 svanu\'f1\'f6hitasya dharmasya sa\'e0
siddhir hari-to\'f1a\'ebam}{\insrsid5197105 ). A living entity may eng
age in any occupational duty, but if he wants to have perfection in his duties, he must satisfy the Supreme Lord. As such, one who pleases Him gets better facilities for living, but one who displeases Him gets involved in undesirable situations.
\par It is therefore concluded that there are two kinds of duties\emdash mundane duty and duty performed for the sake of }{\cs337\i\insrsid16336427 yaj\'efa}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or sacrifice (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). Any }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 karma}{\insrsid16336427  or activity}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  one performs which is not for the purpose of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efa}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 is a cause of bondage. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'ebo'nyatra loko'ya\'e0 karma-bandhana\'f9:}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "Work done as a sacrifice for Vi\'f1\'eb
u has to be performed, otherwise work binds one to this material world." }{\cs337\insrsid16336427 (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Bg}{\cs337\insrsid5197105 . }{\insrsid5197105 3.9}{\cs337\insrsid16336427 )}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Karma-bandhana\'f9,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or the bondage of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 karma,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is administered under the regulations of the stringent laws of mate
rial nature. Material existence is a struggle to conquer the impediments put forth by material nature. The }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 asuras}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 are always fighting to overcome these impediments, and by the illusory power of material nature the foolish living entities work very hard within this material world and take this to be happiness. This is called }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4.}{
\insrsid5197105  In that hard struggle for existence, they deny the existence of the supreme authority, Puru\'f1ottama, the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par In order to regulate the activities of the living entities, God has given us codes, just as a king gives codes of law in a state, and whoever breaks the law is punished. Similarly, the Lord has given the infallible knowledge of the }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  which are not contaminated by the four defects of human life\emdash namely}{\insrsid16336427 ,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the tendency to commit mistakes, to be illusioned, to cheat and to have imperfect senses. If we do not take direction from the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 but act whimsically according to our own choice, we are sure to be punished by the laws of the Lord, who offers dif
ferent types of bodies in the 8,400,000 species of forms. Material existence, or the sense gratification process, is conducted according to the type of body we are given by }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 prak\'e5ti,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or material nature. As such, there must be divisions of pious and impious activities (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 pu\'ebya}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 p\'e4pa}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). In }{
\cs347\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it is clearly stated:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 ye\'f1\'e4\'e0 tv anta-gata\'e0 p\'e4pa\'e0}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid16336427  }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 jan\'e4n\'e4\'e0 pu\'ebya-karma\'eb\'e4m\line te dvandva-moha-nirmukt\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid16336427  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhajante m\'e4\'e0 d\'e5\'f2ha-vrat\'e4\'f9
