\cs386\cf1\insrsid16336427 es of the impious path of life (}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 this is possible only when one engages }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid16336427 exclusively in pious activities)}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 can understand his eternal relationship with the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Thus one engages in }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid16336427 Hi}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 s transcendental loving service." }{\insrsid16336427 (Bg. 7.28}{
\insrsid16336427\charrsid5197105 )}{\insrsid16336427  }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 This life of engaging always in the loving service of the Lord is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 adhok\'f1aja-dhiya\'f9,}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or a life of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, which King P\'e5thu meant his citizens to follow.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 
The different varieties of life and of material existence do not come about by chance and necessity; they are different 
arrangements made by the Supreme Lord in terms of the pious and impious activities of the living entities. By performing pious activities one can take birth in a good family in a good nation, one can get a beautiful body or can become very well educated o
r
 very rich. We see, therefore, that in different places and in different planets there are different standards of life, bodily features and educational statuses, all awarded by the Supreme Personality of Godhead according to pious or impious activities. V
a
rieties of life, therefore, develop not by chance but by prearrangement. There is a plan, which is already outlined in the Vedic knowledge. One has to take advantage of this knowledge and mold his life in such a way that at the end, especially in the huma
n form of life, he may go back home, back to Godhead, by practicing K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par The theory of chance can best be explained in the Vedic literature by the words }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 aj\'ef\'e4ta-suk\'e5ti,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  which refer to pious activities performed without the actor's knowledge. 
But these are also planned. For example, K\'e5\'f1\'eba comes like an ordinary human being, He comes as a devotee like Lord Caitanya, or He sends His repre}{\insrsid10430931 sentative, the spiritual master}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or pure devotee. This is also the planned activity of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. They come to canvass and educate, and thus a person in the illusory energy of the Supreme Lord gets a chance to mix with them, talk with them}{\insrsid10430931 ,}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and take lessons from them, and somehow or other if a conditioned soul surrenders to such personalities and by intimate association with them chances to become K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious, he is saved from the material conditions of life. K\'e5\'f1\'eba therefore instructs:
