\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 As stated by Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu in His }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\'c7ik\'f1\'e4\'f1\'f6aka}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  instructions, by the chanting of the holy name of the Lord\emdash Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4
ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare\emdash or by the process of hearing and chanting of the glories of the Lord, one's mind is gradually cleansed of all dirt. Due to our mat
erial association since time immemorial, we have accumulated heaps of dirty things in our minds. The total effect of this takes place when a living entity identifies himself with his body and is thus entrapped by the stringent laws of material nature and 
put into the cycle of repeated birth and death under the false impression of bodily identification. When one is strengthened by practicing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 his mind is cleansed of this misunderstanding, and he is no longer interested in material existence or in sense gratification.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Bhakti,}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or devotional service, is characterized by }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vair\'e4gya}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 J\'ef\'e4na}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  refers to understanding that one is not his body, and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vair\'e4gya}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 means disinterest in sense gratification. These two primary principles of separation from material bondage can be realized on the strength of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 Thus when a devotee is fixed in the loving service of the lotus feet of the Lord, he will never come back to this material existence after quitting his body, as confirmed in }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  by the Lord }{\cs383\insrsid4399041 (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0 punar janma naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna}{\insrsid5197105 ).
\par In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vij\'ef\'e4na}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is specifically important. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 J\'ef\'e4na,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the knowledge of spiritual identity that one attains when he does not consider himself to be the body, is explained in }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  as }{\cs337\i\insrsid4399041 brahma-bh\'fcta}{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 ,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the revival of spiritual realization. In the conditioned state of material existence one cannot be spiritually realized because he identifies himself materially. The understanding of the distinction between material existence and spiritual
 existence is called }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  After coming to the platform of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 brahma-bh\'fcta}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  state, one ultimately comes to devotional service, in which he completely understands his own position and the position of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This understanding is explained here as }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vij\'ef\'e4na-vi\'e7e\'f1a.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  The Lord says, therefore, that knowledge of Him is }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vij\'ef\'e4na,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 science. In other words, when one is strengthened by scientific knowledge of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, his position of liberation is guaranteed. In }{\cs347\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs347\i\insrsid4399041  }{
\cs347\insrsid4399041\charrsid4399041 also}{\insrsid4399041 , }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 the science of devotional service is described as }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 pratyak\'f1\'e4vagama\'e0 dharmyam,}{\insrsid5197105 
 direct understanding of the principles of religion by realization}{\insrsid4399041  (Bg. 9.2)}{\insrsid5197105 .
\par By practicing }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  one can directly perceive his advancement in spiritual life. In other practices\emdash like }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 karma-yoga, j\'ef\'e4na-yoga}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 dhy\'e4na-yoga}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash one may not be confident about his progress, but in }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 one can become directly aware of his progress in spiritual life, just as a person who eats can understand that his 
hunger is satisfied. Our false appetite for enjoyment and lordship of the material world is due to a prominence of passion and ignorance. By }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 these two qualities are diminished, and one becomes situated in the mode of goodness. Gradually surpass
ing the mode of goodness, one is situated in pure goodness, which is not contaminated by the material qualities. When thus situated, a devotee no longer has any doubts; he knows that he will not come back to this material world.}{\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
