\par }\pard\plain \s373\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja advised hi
s citizens: Engaging your minds, your words, your bodies and the results of your occupational duties, and being always open-minded, you should all render devotional service to the Lord. According to your abilities and the occupations in which you are situ
ated, you should engage your service at the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead with full confidence and without reservation. Then you will surely be successful in achieving the final objective in your lives.
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1064765 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid1064765\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 As stated in the Eighteenth Chapter of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sva-karma\'eb\'e4 tam abhyarcya:}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  one has to worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead by }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid4399041 hi}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 s occupational duties. This necessitates accepting the principle of four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'ebas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4\'e7ramas.}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja therefore says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gu\'ebai\'f9 sva-karmabhi\'f9.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  This phrase is explained in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 C\'e4tur-var\'ebya\'e0 may\'e4 s\'e5\'f1\'f6a\'e0 gu\'eba-karma-vibh\'e4ga\'e7a\'f9:}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "The four castes (the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
) are created by the Supreme Personality of Godhead according to the material modes of
 nature and the particular duties discharged in those modes." A person who is situated in the mode of goodness is certainly more intelligent than others. Therefore he can practice the brahminical activities\emdash namely}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid544364 ,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  speaking the truth, controlling the sense
s, controlling the mind, remaining always clean, practicing tolerance, having full knowledge about one's self-identity, and understanding devotional service. In this way, if he engages himself in the loving service of the Lord as an actual }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  his aim to achieve the final interest of life is attained. Similarly, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriya's}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 duties are to give protection to the citizens, to give all his possessions in charity, to be strictly Vedic in the management of state affairs}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid544364 ,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and to be unafraid to fight whene
ver there is an attack by enemies. In this way, a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriya}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  can satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhead by his occupational duties. Similarly, a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
vai\'e7ya}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  can satisfy the Supreme Godhead by properly executing his occupational duties\emdash engaging himself in prod
ucing foodstuffs, giving protection to cows, and trading if necessary when there is an excess of agricultural production. Similarly, because }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid544364\charrsid544364 they}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 do not have ample intelligence, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid544364 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  should simply engage as workers to serve the higher statuses of social 
life. Everyone's aim should be to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhead by engaging his mind in thinking always of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, his words in always offering prayers to the Lord or preaching about the glories of the Lord, and his body in executing the service required to satisfy the Lord. As there are four divisions within our body\emdash 
the head, the arms, the belly and the legs\emdash similarly, human society, taken as a whole, is divided into four classes of men according to their material qualities and occupational du
ties. Thus the brahminical or intelligent men have to execute the duty of the head, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriyas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  must fulfill the duty of the arms, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vai\'e7ya}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  class must fulfill the duty of the belly, and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdras}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  must fulfill the duty of the legs. In executing the prescribed duties of }{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid544364 life, no one is higher or lower, for although there are such divisions as higher}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  an}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid544364 d lower, }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
since there is actually a common interest\emdash to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhead\emdash there are no distinctions between them.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The question may b
e raised that since the Lord is supposed to be worshiped by great demigods like Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva and others, how can an ordinary human being on this planet serve Him? This is clearly explained by P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja by the use of the word 
}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yath\'e4dhik\'e4ra,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "according to one's ability." If one sincerely executes his occupational duty, that will be sufficient. One does not need to become like Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord 
\'c7iva, Indra, Lord Caitanya or R\'e4m\'e4nuj\'e4c\'e4rya, whose capabilities are certainly far above ours. Even a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdra,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 who is in the lowest stage of life according to the material qualities, can achieve the same success. Anyone can become successful in devotional service provided he displays no duplicity. It is explained here that one must be very frank and open-minded (
}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 am\'e4yina\'f9}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). To be situated in a lower status of life is not a disqualification for success in devotional service. The only qualification is that whether one is a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdra,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 he must be open, frank and free from reservations. Then, by performing his particular occupational duty under the guidance of a proper spiritual master, he can achieve the highest success in life. As confirmed by the Lord Himself, }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 striyo vai\'e7y\'e4s tath\'e4 \'e7\'fcdr\'e4s te 'pi y\'e4nti par\'e4\'e0 gatim}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 (Bg. 9.32)}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 . It does not mat
ter what one is, whether a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya, \'e7\'fcdra}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid544364  or a degraded woman. If h}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
e engages himself seriously in devotional service, working with body, mind and intelligence, he is sure to be successful in going back home, back to Godhead. The Lord's lotus feet are described here as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'e4ma-dugh\'e4\'ec
ghri-pa\'eckajam}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  because they have all power to fulfill the desires of everyone. A devotee is }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid8923350 happy even in this life because}{\cs372\cf9\insrsid8923350\charrsid5197105 \emdash }{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 although in material existence we have many needs}{\cs372\cf9\insrsid8923350\charrsid5197105 \emdash }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 all his material needs are satisfied, an
d when he at last quits his body, he goes back home, back to Godhead, without a doubt.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
