The Supreme Personality of Godhead is transcendental and not contaminated by this material world. But although He is concentrated spirit soul wit
hout material variety, for the benefit of the conditioned soul He nevertheless accepts different types of sacrifice performed with various material elements, rituals and mantras and offered to the demigods under different names according to the interests 
and purposes of the performers.
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1064765 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid1064765\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 For material prosperity there are recommendations in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  for various types of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efa}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  (sacrifice). In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  (}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 3.10}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ) it is confirmed that Lord Brahm\'e4 created all living entities, including human beings and demigods, and advised them to perform }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efa}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  according to their material desires (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 saha-yaj\'ef\'e4\'f9 praj\'e4\'f9 s\'e5\'f1\'f6v\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
). These performances are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  because their ultimate goal is to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'ebu. The purpose of performing }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is to get material benefit, but because the aim is to simultaneously satisfy the Supreme Lord, such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efas}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  have been recommended in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Such performances are, of course, known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or material activities, and all material activities are certainly contaminated by the three modes of material nature. Generally the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  ritualistic ceremonies are performed in the mode of passion, yet the conditioned souls, both human beings and demigods, are obliged to perform these }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efas}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  because without them one cannot be happy at all.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura comments that these }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  ritualistic ceremonies, although contaminated, contain touches of devotional service because whenever there is a performance of any }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid4198056 
yaj\'efa}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is given a central position. This is very important because even a little endeavor to please Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and is of great value. A tinge of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  purifies the material nature of the performances, which by devotional service gradually c
ome to the transcendental position. Therefore although such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are superficially material activities, the results are transcendental. Such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj
\'efas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid4198056  as S\'fcrya-yaj\'efa, Indra-yaj\'efa,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Candra-yaj\'efa}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid4198056 , etc.,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 are performed in the names of the demigods, but these dem
igods are bodily parts of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The demigods cannot accept sacrificial offerings for themselves, but they can accept them for the Supreme Personality of Godhead, just as a departmental tax collector of a government cannot col
lect taxes for his personal account but can realize them for the government. Any }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efa}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  performed with this complete knowledge and understanding is described in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahm\'e4rpa\'ebam,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or a sacrifice offered to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Sinc
e no one but the Supreme Lord can enjoy the results of sacrifice, the Lord says that He is the actual enjoyer of all sacrifices (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'ef}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid4198056 a-tapas\'e4\'e0 sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). Sacrifices should be performed with this view in mind. As stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahm\'e4rpa\'eba\'e0 brahma havir\line brahm\'e4gnau brahma\'eb\'e4 hutam\line 
