rtance of devotional service for both the rulers and the citizens of the state. Now he explains how one can be steadily fixed in devotional service. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, while instructing \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, has compared the devotional service of the L
ord with a creeper. A creeper has a feeble stem and requires the support of another tree to grow, and while growing, it requires sufficient protection so that it may not be lost. While describing the system of protection for the creeper of devotional serv
ice, \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu has especially stressed protection from offenses unto the lotus feet of Vai\'f1\'ebavas. }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid3036598 This is}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3036598 vai\'f1\'eb
av\'e4}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 par\'e4dha.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Apar\'e4dha}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid3036598  means offense.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  If one commits }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3036598 vai\'f1\'ebav\'e4par\'e4dha}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  all of his progress in devotional service will be checked
. Even though one is very much advanced in devotional service, if he commits offenses at the feet of a Vai\'f1\'ebava, his advancement is all spoiled. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 it is found that a very great }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Durv\'e4s\'e4 Muni, committed a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3036598\charrsid3036598 vai\'f1\'ebav\'e4par\'e4dha}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3036598 ,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and thus for one full year had to travel all over the universe, even to Vaiku\'eb\'f6haloka, to defend himself from the offense. At last, even when he approached the Supreme Personality of Godhead in Vaiku\'eb
\'f6ha, he was refused protection. Therefore one should be very careful about committing offenses at the feet of a Vai\'f1\'ebava. The most grievous type of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3036598\charrsid3036598 vai\'f1\'ebav\'e4par\'e4dha}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gurv-apar\'e4dha,}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 which refers to offenses at the lotus feet of the spiritual master. In the chanting of the holy name of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, this }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gurv-apar\'e4dha}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 is considered the most grievous offense. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Guror avaj\'ef\'e4 \'e7ruti-\'e7\'e4stra-nindanam}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). Among the ten offenses committed against the chanting of the holy name, the first offenses are disobedience of the spiritual master and blasphemy of the Vedic literature.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The simple definition of }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid3036598 "}{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid3036598 Vai\'f1\'ebava}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid3036598 "}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is given by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu: a person who immediately reminds one of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, is a Vai\'f1\'ebava. In this verse, both Vai\'f1\'ebavas and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are mentioned. A Vai\'f1\'ebava is a learned }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba
}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and is therefore designated as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba-vai\'f1\'ebava, br\'e4hma\'eba-pa\'eb\'f2ita}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or as a Vai\'f1\'ebava and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In other words, a Vai\'f1\'ebava is supposed to be a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  already, but a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  may not be a pure Vai\'f1\'ebava. When a person understands his pure identity, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahma j\'e4n\'e4ti,}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  he immediately becomes a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 stage, one's understanding of the Absolute Truth is mainly based on the impersonal view. When a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  however, rises to the platform of personal understanding
 of the Supreme Godhead, he becomes a Vai\'f1\'ebava. A Vai\'f1\'ebava is transcendental even to a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In the material conception, the position of a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is the highest in human society, but a Vai\'f1\'ebava is transcendental even to a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Both the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and Vai\'f1\'ebava are spiritually advanced. A }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba's}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  qualifications are mentioned in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 as truthfulness, mental equanimity, control of the senses, the power of tolerance, simplicity, knowledge of the Absolute Truth, firm faith in the scriptures, 
and practical application of the brahminical qualities in life. In addition to all these qualifications, when one fully engages in the transcendental loving service of the Lord, he becomes a Vai\'f1\'ebava. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja warns his citizens who are actually engaged in the devotional service of the Lord to take care against offenses to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and Vai\'f1\'eb
avas. Offenses at their lotus feet are so destructive that even the descendants of Yadu who were born in the family of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba were destroyed due to offens
es at their feet. The Supreme Personality of Godhead cannot tolerate any offense at the lotus feet of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and Vai\'f1\'eb
avas. Sometimes, due to their powerful positions, princes or government servants neglect the position of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and Vai\'f1\'ebavas, not k
nowing that because of their offense they will be ruined.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
