 Godhead, is the prime protector of brahminical culture and the cow. Without knowing and respecting these, one cannot realize the science of God, and without this knowledge, any welfare activities or humanitarian propaganda cannot be successful. The Lord 
is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1a,}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or the supreme enjoyer. Not only is He the enjoyer when He appears as a manifested incarnation, but He is the enjoyer since time immemorial, from the very beginning (}
{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid1339728 pur\'e4tana}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ), and eternally (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nityam}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Yac-cara\'eb\'e4bhivandan\'e4t:}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said that the Supreme Personality of Godhead attained this opulence of eternal fame simply by worshiping the lotus feet of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it is said that the Lord does not need to work to achieve material gain. Since He is perpetually supreme
ly perfect, He does not need to obtain anything, but still it is said that He obtained His opulences by worshiping the lotus feet of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 These are His exemplary actions. When Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba was in Dv\'e4rak\'e4, He offered His respects by bowing down at the lotus feet of N\'e4rada. When Sud\'e4m\'e4 Vipra came to His house, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a personally washed his feet and gave him a seat on His personal bed. Although He is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba offered His respects to Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira and Kunt\'e9
. The Lord's exemplary behavior is to teach us. We should learn from His personal behavior how to give protection to the cow, how to cultivate brahminical qualities and how to respect the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and the Vai\'f1\'ebavas. The Lord says in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 , }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yad yad \'e4carati \'e7re\'f1\'f6
has tat tad evetaro jana\'f9:}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  "If the leading personalities behave in a certain manner, others follow them automatically." }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid1339728\charrsid5197105 (}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid1339728 Bg. }{
\cf1\insrsid1339728 3.21}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid1339728\charrsid5197105 )}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid1339728  }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Who can be more of a leading personality than the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and whose behavior c
ould be more exemplary? It is not that He needed to do all these things to acquire material gain, but all of these acts were performed just to teach us how to behave in this material world.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The Supreme Personality of Godhead is described herein as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mahattama-agra\'eb\'e9\'f9.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Within this material world, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mahattamas,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or great personalities, are Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva, but He is above them all. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba\'f9 paro'vyakt\'e4t:}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 the Supreme Personality of Godhead is in a transcendental position, above everything}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid1339728  that is}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  cre
