\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  His situation is transcendental, for he is free from the four defects of conditional life, which are the tendencies t
o commit mistakes, to be illusioned, to cheat and to possess imper}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid13044224 fect senses. A perfect Vai\'f1\'ebava or K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious person}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 is always in this transcendental position because he speaks according to K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His representative. Because Vai\'f1\'ebavas speak exactly according to the tune of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, whatever they say is free from these four defects. For example, K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
