y everyone should surrender unto Him. These devotional activities are transcendental and free from mistakes, illusion, cheating and imperfection. Therefore anyone who is a sincere devotee of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and who preaches this cult, speaking only on the basis of K\'e5\'f1\'eba's instructions, is understood to be }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 virajam,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or free from the defects of material contamination. A genuine }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or Vai\'f1\'ebava therefore depends eternally on the conclusion of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Vedas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or Vedic versions presented by the Supreme Personality of Godhead Himself. Only from Vedic knowledge can we understand the actual position of the Absolute Truth, who, as described in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is manifested in three features\emdash namely impersonal B}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14557577 rahman, localized Param\'e4tm\'e4 and}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  at last, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This knowledge is perfect from time immemorial, and the brahminical or Vai\'f1\'ebava culture depends on this principle eternally. One should therefore study the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  with faith, not only for one's personal knowledge, but for the sake of spreadin
g this knowledge and these activities through real faith in the words of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ma\'ecgala}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  ("auspicious") in this verse is very significant. \'c7r\'e9la \'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9
 quotes that to do what is good and to reject what is not good is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ma\'ecgala,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or auspicious. To do what is good means to accept everything favorable to the discharge of devotional service, and to reject what is not good means to reject everything not favorable for discharging devotional service. In our K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement, we accept this principle by rejecting four prohibited items\emdash namely}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14557577 ,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  illicit sex life, i}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14557577 ntoxication, gambling and flesh-}
{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 eating\emdash and accepting the daily chanting of at least sixteen rounds of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mah\'e4-mantra}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and 
daily meditation three times a day by chanting the G\'e4yatr\'e9 }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantra.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 In this way one can keep his brahminical culture and spiritual strength intact. By following these principles of devotional service strictly, chanting twenty-four hours a day the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mah\'e4-mantra}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 \emdash Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare\emdash 
one makes positive progress in spiritual life and ultimately becomes completely fit to see the Supreme Personality of Godhead face to face. Because the ultimate goal of studying or understanding the Vedic knowledge is to find K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, one who follows the Vedic principles as described above can from the very beginning see all the features of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Absolute Truth, very}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14557577  distinctly, as one can see hi}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 s own face completely reflected in a clear mirror. The conclusion is, therefore, that a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  does not become a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  simply because he is a living entity or is born in a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 family; he must possess all the qualities mentioned in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and practice the brahminical principles in his life. Thus he ultimately becomes a fully K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious person and can understand what K\'e5\'f1\'eba is. How a devotee continuously sees K\'e5\'f1\'eba face to face within his heart is described in the }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 as follows:
