ras about their good fortune, for the Kum\'e4ras are always auspicious by dint of their life in celibacy. Since they are always engaged on the path of liberation, there was no question of ill fortune. In other words, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4
hma\'ebas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and Vai\'f1\'ebavas who are strictly following the path of spiritual advancement are always fortunate. The question was asked by P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja for his own sake, since he was in the position of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 g\'e5hastha}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and in charge of the royal authority. Kings are not only }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 g\'e5hasthas,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  who are generally absorbed in sense gratification, but are sometimes employed to kill a
nimals in hunting because they have to practice the killing art, otherwise it is very difficult for them to fight their enemies. Such things are not auspicious. Four kinds of sinful activities\emdash 
associating with woman for illicit sex, eating meat, intoxication and gambling\emdash are allowed for the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriyas.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 For political reasons, sometimes they have to take to these sinful activities. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 K\'f1atriyas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  do not refrain from gambling. One vivid example is the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas. When the P\'e4
\'eb\'f2avas were challenged by the opposite party, Duryodhana, to gamble and risk their kingdom, they could not refrain, and by that gambling they lost their kingdom, and their wife was insulted. Similarly, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriyas}
{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  cannot refrain from fighting if challenged by the opposite party. Therefore P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, taking consideration of all these facts, inquired whether there is any auspicious path. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 G\'e5hastha}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  life is inauspicious because }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 g\'e5hastha}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 means consciousness for sense gratification, and as soon as there is sense gratification, one's position is always full of dangers. This material world is said to be }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pada\'e0 pada\'e0 yad vipad\'e4\'e0 na te\'f1\'e4m,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  dangerous in every step }{\i\cf1\insrsid16085486\charrsid16085486 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  10.14.58)}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
. Everyone in this material world is struggling hard for sense gratification. Clearing all these points, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu inquired from the four Kum\'e4
ras about the fallen conditioned souls who are rotting in this material world due to their past bad or inauspicious activities. Is there any possibility for their auspicious spiritual life? In this verse, the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 indriy\'e4
rth\'e4rtha-vedin\'e4m}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is very significant. It indicates persons whose only aim is to satisfy the senses. They are also described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 patit\'e4n\'e4m,}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or fallen. Only one who stops all activities for sense gratification is considered to be elevated. Another significant word is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sva-karmabhi\'f9.}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 One becomes fallen by dint of his own past bad activities. Everyone is responsible for his fallen condition because of his own activities. When activities are changed to devotional service, one's auspicious life begins.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs380\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
