\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid15149999 ahi\'e0s\'e4}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or nonviolence. A }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 titik\'f1ava\'f9 k\'e4
ru\'ebik\'e4\'f9}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\i\cf1\insrsid16085486\charrsid16085486 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  3.25.21)}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
. A devotee should be tolerant and should be very much compassionate toward others. For example, if he suffers personal injury, he should tolerate it, but i}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid15149999 f someone else suffers injury, he}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  need not tol
erate it. The whole world is full of violence, and a devotee's first business is to stop this violence, including the unnecessary slaughter of animals. A devotee is the friend not only of human society but of all living entities, for he sees all living en
tities as sons of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He does not claim himself to be the only son of God and allow all others to be killed, thinking that they have no soul. This kind of philosophy is never advocated by a pure devotee of the Lord. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Suh\'e5da\'f9 sarva-dehin\'e4m:}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  a true devotee is the friend of all living entities. K\'e5\'f1\'eba claims in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  to be the father of all species of living entities; consequently the devotee of K\'e5\'f1\'eba is always a friend of all. This is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ahi\'e0s\'e4.}{
\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Such nonviolence can be practiced only when we follow in the footsteps of great }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4ryas.}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Therefore, according to our Vai\'f1\'eb
ava philosophy, we have to follow the great }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  of the four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid15149999 samprad\'e4yas}{\cs380\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or disciplic successions.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12259978 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Trying to advance in spiritual life outside the discipl
ic succession is simply l}{\cs383\insrsid15149999 udicrous. It is said, therefore:}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4ryav\'e4n puru\'f1o veda}{\cs337\i\insrsid12259978  }{\insrsid15149999 (}{
\cs337\i\insrsid12259978 Ch\'e4nd. Up.}{\insrsid15149999  6.14.2)}{\insrsid12259978 .}{\cs383\insrsid12259978  O}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ne who follows the disciplic succession of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{
\cs383\insrsid12259978  knows things as they are}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 . }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Tad-vij\'ef}{\cs337\i\insrsid12259978 \'e4n\'e4rtha\'e0 sa gurum ev\'e4bhigacchet}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105  }{\cs347\insrsid12259978 (}{
\cs347\i\insrsid12259978\charrsid12259978 Mund. Up.}{\insrsid12259978  1.2.12).}{\cs383\insrsid12259978  I}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 n order to understand the transcendental science, one must approach the bona fide spiritual master. The word 
}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 sm\'e5ty\'e4}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is very important in spiritual life. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Sm\'e5ty\'e4}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  means remembering K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a always. Life should be molded in such a way that one cannot remain alone without thinking of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. We should live in K\'e5\'f1\'eba so that while eating, sleeping, walking and working we remain only in K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Our K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness society recommends that we arrange our living so that we can remember K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In our ISKCON society the devotees, while engaged in making Spiritual Sky incense, are also hearing about the glories of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a or His devotees. The }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stra}{\cs383\insrsid12259978  recommends:}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 smartavya\'f9 satata\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebu\'f9}{\cs337\i\insrsid12259978 .}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu should be remembered always, constantly. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vismartavyo na j\'e4tucit:}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Vi\'f1\'ebu should never be forgot
ten. That is the spiritual way of life. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Sm\'e5ty\'e4.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  This remembrance of the Lord can be continued if we hear about Him constantly. It is therefore recommended in this verse: }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 mukund\'e4carit\'e4grya-s\'e9dhun\'e4.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 S\'e9dhu}{\cs383\insrsid12259978  means nectar.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  To hear about K\'e5\'f1\'eba from }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid5197105  or similar authentic literature is to live in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. Such concentration in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness can be achieved by persons who are strictly following the rules and regulative principles. We have recommended in our K\'e5\'f1\'eba co
nsciousness movement that a devotee chant sixteen rounds on beads daily and follow the regulative principles. That will help the devotee be fixed in his spiritual advancement in life.
\par }\pard \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 {\insrsid5197105 It is also stated in this verse that by controlling the senses }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 one can become a }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 sv\'e4m\'e9}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 gosv\'e4m\'e9.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  One who is therefore enjoying this supertitle, }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 sv\'e4m\'e9}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 gosv\'e4m\'e9,}{\insrsid5197105  must be very strict in controlling his senses. Indeed, he must be master of his senses. This is possible when one does not desire any material sense gratification. I
f, by chance, the senses want to work independently, he must control them. If we simply practice avoiding material sense gratification, controlling the senses is automatically achieved.
\par Another important point mentioned in this connection }{\insrsid2639854 (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 aninday\'e4}{\cs337\i\insrsid2639854 ) }{\insrsid2639854 is that }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
we should not criticize others' methods of religion. There are different types of religious systems operating under different qualities of material nature. Those operating in the modes of ignorance and passion cannot be as perfect as that system in the m
ode of goodness. In }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid5197105 
 everything has been divided into three qualitative divisions; therefore religious systems are similarly categorized. When people are mostly under the modes of passion and ignorance, their system of religion will be of the 
same quality. A devotee, instead of criticizing such systems, will encourage the followers to stick to their principles so that gradually they can come to the platform of religion in goodness. Simply by criticizing them, a devotee's mind will be agitated.
 Thus a devotee should tolerate and learn to stop agitation.
\par Another feature of the devotee is }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 nir\'e9hay\'e4,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  simple living. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Nir\'e9h\'e4}{\insrsid2639854  means gentle, }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 meek}{\insrsid2639854 
 or }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 simple. A devotee should not live very gorgeously and imitate a materialistic person. Plain living and high 
thinking are recommended for a devotee. He should accept only so much as he needs to keep the material body fit for the execution of devotional service. He should not eat or sleep more than is required. Simply eating for living, and not living for eating,
 
and sleeping only six to seven hours a day are principles to be followed by devotees. As long as the body is there it is subjected to the influence of climatic changes, disease and natural disturbances, the threefold miseries of material existence. We can
not avoid them. Sometimes we receive letters from neophyte devotees questioning why they have fallen sick, although pursuing K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. They should learn from this verse that they have to become tolerant (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 
dvandva-titik\'f1ay\'e4}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ). This is the world of duality. }{\insrsid2639854 B}{\insrsid2639854\charrsid5197105 ecause he has fallen sick}{\insrsid2639854 , one should not think that}{\insrsid2639854\charrsid5197105 
 he has fallen from K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.}{\insrsid2639854  }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 One should not think that  K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness can continue without impediment from any material opposition. Lord \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a therefore advises in }{\cs347\i\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 , }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 t\'e4\'e0s titik\'f1asva bh\'e4rata:}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 "My dear Arjuna, please try to tolerate all these disturbances. Be fixed in your K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious activities."}{\insrsid2639854  (Bg. 2.14}{\insrsid2639854\charrsid5197105 )}{\insrsid5197105 
