\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 In our material existence we accept a higher form of life as a blessing and a lower form a}{
\cf1\insrsid13251051 s a curse. This distinction of }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 higher}{\cf1\insrsid13251051  and lower}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  only exists as long as the different material qualities (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gu\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
) interact. In other words, by our good activities we are elevated to the higher planetary systems or to a higher standard of life (good education, beautiful body, etc.). These are the results of pious activities. Si
milarly, by impious activities we remain illiterate, get ugly bodies, a poor standard of living, etc. But all these different states of life are under the laws of material nature through the interaction of the qualities of goodness, passion and ignorance.
 However, all these qualities will cease to act at the time of the dissolution of the entire cosmic manifestation. The Lord therefore says in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4brahma-bhuvan\'e4l lok\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid13251051  }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 punar \'e4vartino 'rjuna\line m\'e4m upetya tu kaunteya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid13251051  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 punar janma na vidyate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid13251051  \line }{\i0\cf1\insrsid13251051\charrsid13251051 (Bg. 8.16)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
Even though we elevate ourselves to the highest planetary system by the scientific advancement of knowledge or by the religious principles of life\emdash great sacrifices and fruitive activities\emdash 
at the time of dissolution these higher planetary systems and life on them will be destroyed. }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid13251051 T}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid13251051\charrsid5197105 he words}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid13251051  i}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
n this verse }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid13251051 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e9\'e7a-vidhva\'e0sit\'e4\'e7i\'f1\'e4m}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid13251051 )}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid13251051  }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
indicate that all such blessings will be destroyed by the supreme controller. We will not be protected. Our bodies, either in this planet or in another planet, will be destroyed, 
and again we will have to remain for millions of years in an unconscious state within the body of Mah\'e4-Vi\'f1\'eb
u. And again, when the creation is manifested, we have to take birth in different species of life and begin our activities. Therefore we should not b
e satisfied simply by a promotion to the higher planetary systems. We should try to get out of the material cosmic manifestation, go to the spiritual world and take shelter of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. That is our highest achievement. We should 
n
ot be attracted by anything material, higher or lower, but should consider them all on the same level. Our real engagement should be in inquiring about the real purpose of life and rendering devotional service to the Lord. Thus we will be eternally blesse
d in our spiritual activities, full of knowledge and bliss.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 Regulated human civilization promotes }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 
dharma, artha, k\'e4ma}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 mok\'f1a.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 In human society there must be religion. Without religion, human society is only animal society. Economic development and sense 
gratification must be based on religious principles. When religion, economic development and sense gratification are adjusted, liberation from this material birth, death, old age and disease is assured. In the present age of Kali, however, there is no que
s
tion of religion and liberation. People have taken interest only in economic development and sense gratification. Therefore, despite sufficient economic development all over the world, dealings in human society have become almost animalistic. When everyth
ing becomes grossly animalistic, dissolution takes place. This dissolution is to be accepted as }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e9\'e7a-vidhva\'e0sit\'e4\'e7i\'f1\'e4m.}{\insrsid5197105 
 The Lord's so-called blessings of economic development and sense gratification will be conclusively dissolved by destruction. At the end of
 this Kali-yuga, the Lord will appear as the incarnation of Kalki, and His only business will be to kill all human beings on the surface of the globe. After that killing, another golden age will begin. We should therefore know that our material activities
 are just like childish play. Children may play on the bea}{\insrsid11749094 ch}{\insrsid5197105 
 and the father will sit and watch this childish play, the construction of buildings with sand, the construction of walls and so many things, but finally the father will ask the children to come ho
me. Then everything is destroyed. Persons who are too much addicted to the childish activities of economic development and sense gratification are sometimes especially favored by the Lord when He destroys their construction of these things.
\par It is said by the Lord: }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yasy\'e4ham anug\'e5h\'eb\'e4mi hari\'f1ye tad-dhana\'e0 \'e7anai\'f9.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  The Lord told Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja that His special favor is shown to His devotee when He takes away all the devotee's material opulences. Generally, therefore, it is experienced that Vai\'f1\'ebavas are not very opulent in the material sense. When a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava, pure devotee, tries to be materially opulent and at the same time desires to serve the Supreme Lord, his devotional service is checked. The Lord, in order to show him a special favor, destroys his so-c
alled economic development and material opulences. Thus the devotee, being frustrated in his repeated attempts at economic development, ultimately takes solid shelter under the lotus feet of the Lord. This kind of action may also be accepted as }{
\cs337\i\insrsid11749094 \'e9\'e7a-vidhva\'e0}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 sit\'e4\'e7i\'f1\'e4m,}{\insrsid5197105  whereby the Lord destroys one's material opulences but enriches }{\insrsid11749094 him}{\insrsid5197105 
 in spiritual understanding. In the course of our preaching work, we sometimes see that materialistic persons come to us and offer their obeisances to take blessings, which means
 they want more and more material opulences. If such material opulences are checked, such persons are no longer interested in offering obeisances to the devotees. Such materialistic persons are always concerned about their economic development. They offer
 obeisances to saintly persons or the Supreme Lord and give something in charity for preaching work with a view that they will be rewarded with further economic development.
\par However, when one is sincere in his devotional service, the Lord obliges the devote
e to give up his material development and completely surrender unto Him. Because the Lord does not give blessings of material opulence to His devotee, people are afraid of worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu because they see that the Vai\'f1\'eb
avas, who are worshipers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, are poor in superficial material opulences. Such materialistic persons, however, get immense opportunity for economic development by worshiping Lord \'c7iva, for Lord \'c7iva is the husband of the goddess Durg
\'e4, }{\insrsid11749094 and Durg\'e4 is }{\insrsid5197105 the proprietor of this universe. By the grace of Lord \'c7iva, a devotee gets the opportunity to be blessed by the goddess Durg\'e4. R\'e4va\'eb
a, for example, was a great worshiper and devotee of Lord \'c7iva, and in return he got all the blessings of goddess Durg\'e4, so much so that his whole kingd
om was constructed of golden buildings. In Brazil, in this present age, huge quantities of gold have been found, and from historical references in the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Pur\'e4\'ebas,}{\insrsid5197105  we can guess safely that this was R\'e4va\'eb
a's kingdom. This kingdom was, however, destroyed by Lord R\'e4macandra.
\par By studying such incidents, we can understand the full meaning of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e9\'e7a-vidhva\'e0sit\'e4\'e7i\'f1\'e4m.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 The Lord does not bestow material blessings upon the devotees, for they may be entrapped again in this material world by continuous birth, death, old age and disease. Due to materialistic opulences, persons like R\'e4va\'eb
a become puffed up for sense gratification. R\'e4va\'eba even dared kidnap S\'e9t\'e4, who was both the wife of Lord R\'e4macandra and the goddess of fortune, thinking that he would be able to enjoy the pleasu
re potency of the Lord. But actually, by such action, R\'e4va\'eba became }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vidhva\'e0sita,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or ruined. At the present moment human civilization is too much attached to economic development and sense gratification and is therefore nearing the path of ruination.}{\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
