In this verse it is specifically advised that instead of wasting time in the human form of life endeavoring for economic development and sense gratification, one should try to cultivate spiritual values by understanding the}{\cf1\insrsid9067852 
 Supreme Personality of Godhead}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  who is existing with}{\cf1\insrsid9067852 in}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the individual soul within everyone's heart. The individual soul and the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His Param\'e4tm\'e4
 feature are both sitting within this body, which is covered by gross and subtle elements. To understand this is to attain actual spiritual culture. There are two ways of advancing in spiritual culture\emdash 
by the method of the impersonalist philosophers and by devotional service. The impersonalist comes to the conclusion that he and the Supreme S}{\cf1\insrsid9067852 pirit are one, whereas devotees or personalists}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  realize the Absol}{
\cf1\insrsid9067852 ute Truth by understanding that}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the Absolute Truth is the supreme predominator and we l}{\cf1\insrsid9067852 iving entities are predominated; therefore}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 our duty is to serve Him. The Vedic injunctions say}{\cf1\insrsid9067852 :}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tat tvam asi,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  "You are the same," and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 so'ham,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 "I am the same." The impersonalist conception of these }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantras}{\cf1\insrsid9067852  is that the Supreme Lord or the Absolute Truth}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 and the living entity are one, but from the devotee's point of view these }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantras}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  assert that both the Supreme Lord and ourselves are of the same quality. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Tat tvam asi, ayam \'e4tm\'e4 brahma.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 Both the Supreme Lord and the living entity are spirit. Understanding this is self-realization. The human form of life is meant for understanding the Supreme Lord and oneself by spiritual cultivat
ion of knowledge. One should not waste valuable life simply engaged in economic development and sense gratification.
