da conclusion of oneness without differentiation between the individual soul and the Supersoul. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da conclusion is that the living entity and the Supersoul are one; there is no difference. The}{\cf1\insrsid16476946 y}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 proclaim that there is no separate existence outside the impersonal Brahman and that the feeling of separation is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid16476946 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid16476946  or an illusion}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  by which one considers}{
\cf1\insrsid16476946  a rope to be a snake. The rope and the }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 snake argument is generally offered by the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers. Therefore these words, which represent }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vivarta-v\'e4da,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  are specifically mentioned herein. Actually Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supersoul, is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and He is eternally liberated. In other words, the Su
preme Personality of Godhead is living within this body along with the individual soul, and this is confirmed in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  They are likened to two friends sitting on the same tree. Yet Param\'e4tm\'e4
 is above the illusory energy. The illusory energy is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid16476946 bahira\'ecg\'e4 \'e7akti}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or external energy, and the living entity is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid16476946 ta\'f6asth\'e4 \'e7akti}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  or marginal potency. As stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the material energy, represented as earth, water, air, fire, sky, etc., and the spiritual energy, the living entity, are bot
h energies of the Supreme Lord. Even though the energies and the energetic are identical, the living entity, individual soul, being prone to be influenced by the external energy, considers the Supreme Personality of Godhead to be one with himself.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prapadye}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is also significant in this verse, for it refers to the conclusion of the }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 : }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sarva-dharm
\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid16476946  }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid16476946 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid16476946 18.66}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid16476946\charrsid5197105 )}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In another place the Lord says: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 janman\'e4m ante j\'ef\'e4nav\'e4n m\'e4\'e0 prapadyate}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid16476946 (}{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid16476946 Bg.}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid16476946 7.19)}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 . This }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prapadye}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 refers to the individual's surrender to the Supersoul. The individual soul, when surrendered, can understand that the Supreme Personality of Godhead, although situated within the heart of the individual soul, is superior to the ind
ividual soul. The Lord is always transcendental to the material manifestation, even though it appears that the Lord and the material manifestation are one and the same. According to the Vai\'f1\'eb
ava philosophy, He is one and different simultaneously. The material energy is a manifestation of His external potency, and since the potency is identical with the potent, it appears that the L}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid16476946 ord and individual soul are one,}
{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  but actually the individual soul is under the influence of material energy, and the Lord is always transcendental to it. Unless the Lord is superior to the individual soul, there is no question of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid16476946 prapadye}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or surrender unto Him. This word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prapadye}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 refers to the process of devotional service. Simply by nondevotional speculation on the rope and the sn
ake, one cannot approach the Absolute Truth. Therefore devotional service is stressed as more important than deliberation or mental speculation to understand the Absolute Truth.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 
