nscendentalists trying to overcome the influence of the modes of material nature\emdash the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s, yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhaktas.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 All of them attempt to overcome the influence of the senses, which is compared to the incessant waves of a river. The waves of a river flow ince
ssantly, and it is very difficult to stop them. Similarly, the waves of desire for material enjoyment are so strong that they cannot be stopped by any process other than }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhaktas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  by their transcendental devotional service unto the lotus feet of the Lord, become so overwhelmed with transcendental bliss that automatically their desires for material enjoyment stop. The }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  who are not attached to the lotus feet of the Lord, simply struggle against the waves of desire. They are de
scribed in this verse as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 rikta-mataya\'f9,}{\cf1\insrsid9201536  which means devoid of devotional service.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  In other words, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  although trying to be free from the desires of material activities, actually become more and more entangled in false philosophical specu
lation or strenuous attempts to stop the activities of the senses. As stated previously:
