\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
In this verse it is very clearly stated that a kingdom, state or empire must be governed under the instructions of saintly persons and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  like the Kum\'e4
ras. When monarchy ruled throughout the world, the monarch was actually directed by a board of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 and saintly persons. The king, as the administrator of the state, executed his duties as a servant of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  It was not that the kings or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  were dictators, nor did they consider themselves proprietors of the state. The kings were also well versed in Vedic literatures and thus were familiar with the injunction of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9 \'c9\'e7opani\'f1ad:
}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e9\'e7\'e4v\'e4syam ida\'e0 sarvam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 \emdash everything that exists belongs to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba also claims that He is the proprietor of all planetary systems (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid15277743 sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
). Since this is the case, no one can claim to be proprietor of the state. The king, president or head of the state should always remember that he is not the proprietor but the servant.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
In the present age, the king or president forgets that he is the servant of God and thinks of himself as servant of the people. The present democratic government is proclaimed to be a people's government, a government by the people
 and for the people, but this type of government is not sanctioned by the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  The }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 maintain that a kingdom should be governed for the purpose of satisfying the Supreme Personality of Godhead and should therefore be ruled by a representative of the 
Lord. The head of a state should not be appointed if he is bereft of all Vedic knowledge. In this verse it is clearly stated (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 veda-\'e7\'e4stra-vid arhati}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
) that all high government posts are especially meant for persons who are well conversant with the teachings of the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\insrsid5197105 
 there are definite instructions defining how a king, commander-in-chief, soldier and citizen should behave. Unfortunately there are many so-called philosophers in the present age who give instruction without citing authority, an
d many leaders follow their unauthorized instruction. Consequently people are not happy.
\par The modern theory of dialectical communism, set forth by Karl Marx and followed by communist governments, is not perfect. According to Vedic communism, no one in the s
tate should ever starve. Presently there are many bogus institutions which are collecting funds from the public for the purpose of giving food to starving people, but these funds are invariably misused. According to the Vedic instructions, the government 
should arrange things in such a way that there will be no question of starvation. In the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 it is stated that a householder must see to it that even a lizard or a snake does not starve. They also must be given food. In actuality, however, the
re is no question of starvation because everything is the property of the Supreme Lord, and He sees to it that there is ample arrangement for feeding everyone. In the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it is said: }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 eko bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0 yo vidadh\'e4ti k\'e4m\'e4n}{\cs337\i\insrsid3881925  }{\insrsid3881925 (}{\cs347\i\insrsid3881925 Ka\'f6ha Up. }{\insrsid3881925  2.2.13)}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 .}{\insrsid5197105  The Supreme Lord su
pplies the necessities of life to everyone, and there is no question of starvation. If anyone starves, it is due to the mismanagement of the so-called ruler, governor or president.
\par It is clear therefore that a person who is not well versed in the Vedic injunctions (}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 veda-\'e7\'e4stra-vit}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ) should not run for election as president, governor, etc. Formerly kings were }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 r\'e4jar\'f1is,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  which meant that although they were serving as kings, they were as good as saintly persons because they would not transgress any of the injunc
tions of the Vedic scriptures and would rule under the direction of great saintly persons and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 According to this arrangement, modern presidents, governors and chief executive officers are all unworthy of their posts because they are not conversant with Vedic administrative knowledge and they do not take direction from great saintly persons and }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Because of his disobedience to the orders of the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  King Vena, P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's father, was killed by the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja therefore knew very well that it behooved him to rule the planet as the servant of saintly persons and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas.
\par }{\cs337\i\insrsid14643438 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.22.46
