\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6555778 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nirvi\'f1a\'ecga\'f9}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid6555778  (uncontaminated}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ) is very significant because Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5
thu was not attached to the results of his activities. In this material world a person is always thinking of the proprietorship of everything he accumulates or works for. When the fruits of one's activities are rendered to th
e service of the Lord, one is actually practicing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-yoga.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Anyone can practice }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-yoga,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 but it is espe}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid6555778 cially easy for the householder}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  who can install the Deity of the Lord in the home and worship Him according to the methods of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga.
}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  This method includes nine items: hearing, chanting, remembering, serving, worshiping the Deity, praying, carrying out orders, serving K\'e5\'f1\'eba as friend and }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid6555778 
sacrificing everything for Him. }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 These methods of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-yoga}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  are being broadcast all over the world by the International Society for Krishna Consciousness. Anyone can learn these methods simply by following the examples of the members of the Society.
\par }\pard \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 In one's home or in a temple, the Deity is considered the proprietor of everything, and everyone is c
onsidered the Deity's eternal servant. The Lord is transcendental, for He is not part of this material creation. The words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prak\'e5te\'f9 param}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 are used in this verse because everything within this material w}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid6555778 orld is created by the external}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  material energy of the
 Lord, but the Lord Himself is not a creation of this material energy. The Lord is the supreme superintendent of all material creations, as confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 may\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9\line s\'fcyate sa-car\'e4caram\line hetun\'e4
