\cf1\insrsid5197105  Arci, and all these sons were begotten as he desired them. They were
 not born whimsically or by accident. How one can beget children according to one's own desire is practically unknown in the present age (Kali-yuga). In this regard the secret of success depends on the parents' acceptance of the various purificatory metho
ds known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sa\'e0sk\'e4ras.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The first }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sa\'e0sk\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na-sa\'e0sk\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 or child-begetting }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sa\'e0sk\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is compulsory, especially for the higher castes, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1
atriyas.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  As stated in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  sex life which is not against religious principles is K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a Himself, and according to religious principles, when one wants to beget a child he must perform the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na-sa\'e0sk\'e4ra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 before having sex. The mental state of the father and mother before sex will certainly affect the mentality of the child to be begotten. A child who is begotten out of lust may not turn out as the parents desire. As stated in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras, yath\'e4 yonir yath\'e4 b\'e9jam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Yath\'e4 yoni\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicates the mother, and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yath\'e4 b\'e9jam}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicates the father. If the mental state of the parents is prepared before they have sex, the child which they will beget will certainly reflect their mental condition. It is therefore understood by the words }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4tma-sammat\'e4n}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  that both P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and Arci underwent the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 garbh\'e4dh\'e4na}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  purificatory process before begetting 
children, and thus they begot all their sons according to their desires and purified mental states. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja did not beget his children out of lust, nor was he attracted to his wife for sense gratificatory purposes. He begot the children as a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 g\'e5hastha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 for the future administration of his government all over the world.
