As it is necessary for one to become very active in family life, similarly, after retirement from family life, it is necessary to control the mind and senses. This is possible when one engages himself fully in the devotional servi
ce of the Lord. Actually the whole purpose of the Vedic system, the Vedic social order, is to enable one to ultimately return home, back to Godhead. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 g\'e5hastha-\'e4\'e7rama}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is a sort of concession combining sense gratification with a regulative life. It is to 
enable one to easily retire in the middle of life and engage fully in austerities in order to transcend material sense gratification once and for all. Therefore in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4naprastha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  stage of life, }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tapasya,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or austerity, is strongly recommended. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu followed exactly all the rules of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4naprastha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 life, which is technically known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vaikh\'e4nasa-\'e4\'e7rama.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vaikh\'e4nasa-susammate}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is significant because in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4naprastha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  life the regulative principles are also to be strictly followed. In other words, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu was an ideal character in every sphere of life. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Mah\'e4
jano yena gata\'f9 sa panth\'e4\'f9:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  one should follow in the footsteps of great personalities. Thus by following the exemplary character of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu, one can become perfect in all respects while 
living this life or while retiring from active life. Thus after giving up this body, one can become liberated and go back to Godhead.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
