\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are advised to go to a secluded place in the forest and live alone in a sanctified spot there. By P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's behavior we can understand that when he went to the forest}{
\cf1\insrsid5462453 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 he did not eat any cooked food sent from the city by some devotees or disciples. As soon as one takes a vow to live in the forest, he must simply eat roots, tree trunks, fruits, dried leaves or whatever nature provides in that way. P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja strictly adopted these principles for living in the forest, and sometimes he ate nothing but dried leaves and drank nothing but a little water. Sometimes he lived on nothing but air, and sometimes he ate some fruit from the trees. In this way he
 lived in the forest and underwent severe austerity, especially in regards to eating. In other words, overeating is not at all recommended for one who wants to progress in spiritual life. \'c7r\'e9 R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 also warns }{\cf1\insrsid5462453 (}
{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5462453 aty\'e4h\'e4ra\'f9 pray\'e4sa\'e7 ca}{\cf1\insrsid5462453 ) }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 that too much eating and too much endeavor  are against the principles by which one can advance in spiritual life.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
It is also notable that according to Vedic injunction, to live in the forest is to live in the mode of complete goodness, whereas to live in the city is to l
ive in the mode of passion, and to live in a brothel or drinking house is to live in the mode of ignorance. However, to live in a temple is to live in Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha, which is transcendental to all the modes of material nature. This K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement affords one the opportunity to live in the temple of the Lord, which is as good as Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha. Consequently a K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious person does not need to go to the forest and artificially try to imitate Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P
\'e5thu or the great sages and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 munis}{\insrsid5197105  who used to live in the forest.
\par \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9, after retiring from his minister's seat in the government, went to V\'e5nd\'e4vana and lived beneath a tree, like Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu. Since then, many people have gone to V\'e5nd\'e4vana to imitate R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m
\'e9's behavior. Instead of advancing in spiritual life, many have fallen into material habits and even in V\'e5nd\'e4vana have become victims of illicit sex, gambling and intoxication. Th}{\insrsid5462453 is}{\insrsid5197105  K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement has been introduced in the Western countries, but it is not possible for Westerners to go to the forest and practice the severe austerities which were ideally practiced by P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja or R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9
. However, Westerners or anyone else can follow in the footsteps of \'c7r\'e9la Bhaktisiddh\'e4nta Sarasvat\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura by living in a temple, which is transcendental to residence in a forest, and to vow to accept }{\cs337\insrsid5462453 K}{
\cs337\insrsid5197105\charrsid5462453 \'e5\'f1\'eba}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 -pras\'e4da}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and nothing else, follow the regulative principles}{\insrsid5462453 ,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
