 is very important in this verse because the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ha\'f6ha-yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 a\'f1\'f6\'e4\'ecga-yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  practice }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y
\'e4ma,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  but generally they do not know the purpose behind it. The purpose of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4ma,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or mystic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is to stop the mind and senses from engaging in fruitive activities. The so-called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  who practice in Western countries have no idea of this. The aim of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eb
\'e4y\'e4ma}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is not to make the body strong and fit for working hard. The aim is worship of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In the previous verse it was specifically mentioned that whatever austerity, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4
ma}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and mystic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  practices P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja performed were performed for the sake of worshiping K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Thus P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja serves as a perfect example for }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  also. Whatever he did, he did to please the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
The minds of those who are addicted to fruitive activity are always filled with unclean desires. Fruitive activities are symptomatic of our polluted desire to dominate material nature
. As long as one continues to be subject to polluted desires, he has to accept one material body after another. So-called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  without knowledge of the real purpose of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga,}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  practice it in order to keep the body fit. Thus they engage themselves in fruiti
ve activities, and thus they are bound by desire to accept another body. They are not aware that the ultimate goal of life is to approach K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In order to save such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  from wandering throughout the different species of life, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  warn that in t
his age such yogic practice is simply a waste of time. The only means of elevation is the chanting of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mah\'e4-mantra.
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 King P\'e5thu's activities took place in Satya-yuga, and in this age this practice of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is misunderstood by fallen souls who a
re not capable of practicing anything. Consequently the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  enjoin: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 kalau n\'e4sty eva n\'e4sty eva n\'e4sty eva gatir anyath\'e4.}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  The conclusion is that unless the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karm\'e9s, j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  come to the point of devotional service to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, their so-called austerities and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  have no value. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 N\'e4r\'e4dhita\'f9:}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  if Hari, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is not worshiped, there is no point in practicing meditational }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga,}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  performing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-yoga}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or culturing empiric knowledge. As far as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4ma}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is concerned, chanting of the holy name of the Lord and dancing in ecstasy are also considered }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4ma.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 In a previous verse, Sanat-kum\'e4ra instructed Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu to engage constantly in the service of the Supreme Lord, V\'e4sudeva:
