\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4ma-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  system, engaged in the service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead as advised by the saint Sanat-kum\'e4ra. In this verse the words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1
am abhajat puru\'f1ar\'f1abha\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are significant: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1ar\'f1abha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  refers to Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu, the best amongst human beings, and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1am}
{\cf1\insrsid5197105  refers to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The conclusion is that the best man amongst all men engages in the service of the Supreme Person. One }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is worshipable, and the other }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is the worshiper. When the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 who worships, the living entity, thinks of becoming one with the Supreme person, he simply becomes bewildered and falls into the darkness of ignorance. As stated by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 , all living entities assembled in the battlefield, as well as K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself, were also present in the past as individuals and would continue to be present in the future as individuals also}{\cf1\insrsid16599184  (Bg. 2.12)}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 . Therefore the two }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1as,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the living entity and the Supreme Personality of Godhead, never lose their respective identities.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid16599184 Actually}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 one who is self-realized engages himself in the service of
 the Lord perpetually, both in this life and in the next. Indeed, for devotees there is no difference between this life and the next. In this life a neophyte devotee is trained to serve the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and in the next life he approache
s that Supreme Person in Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha and renders the same devotional service. Even for the neophyte devotee, devotional service is considered }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid16599184 brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Devotional service to the Lord is never considered a material activity. Since he is acting on the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahma-bh\'fcta}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 platform, a devotee is already liberated. He therefore has no need to practice any other type of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  in order to approach the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahma-bh\'fcta}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  stage. If the devotee adheres strictly to the orders of the spiritual master, follows the rules and regulations and chants the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantra,}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  it should be concluded that he is already at the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahma-bh\'fcta}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  stage, as confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}
{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 :
