When one who is not inspired by material desires and is not contaminated by the processes of fruitive activity and empiric speculation}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5525079 , he}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  fully engages in th}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5525079 e favorable service of the Lord.}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5525079 That}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhagavad-dharma,}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or pure devotional service. In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahma\'ebi}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 does not refer to the impersonal Brahman. Impersonal Brahman is a subordinate feature of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and since impersonal Brahman worshipers desire to merge into the Brahman effulgence, they cannot be considered followers of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhagavad-dharma.}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 After being baffled in his material enjoyment, the impersonalist may desire to merge into the existence of the Lord, but a pure devotee of the Lord has no such desire. Therefore a pure devotee is really }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhagavad-dharm\'e9.

\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 It is clear from this verse that Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5
