\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 N\'e4rada-pa\'efcar\'e4tra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 devotional service to the Lord is likened unto a queen. When a queen gives an audience, many maidservants follow her. The maidservants of devotional service are material opulence, liberation and mystic powers. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karm\'e9s}
{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are very much attached to material enjoyment}{\cf1\insrsid2121178 ;}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are very anxious to beco}{\cf1\insrsid2121178 
me freed from material clutches;}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are very fond of attaining the eight kinds of mystic perfection. From the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 N\'e4rada-pa\'efcar\'e4tra}
{\cf1\insrsid5197105  we understand that if one attains the stage of pure devotional service, he also attains all the opulences derived from fruitive activities, empiric philosophical speculation and mystic yogic practice. \'c7r\'e9la Bilvama\'ecgala \'d6
h\'e4kura therefore prayed in his }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 K\'e5\'f1\'eba-kar\'eb\'e4m\'e5ta:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 "My dear Lord, if I have unflinching devotion to You, You become manifest before me personally, and the results of fruitive activity and empiric philosophical speculation\emdash namely religion, economic development, sense gratification and liberation
\emdash become like personal attendants and remain standing before me as if awaiting my order." The idea here is that the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  by culture of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahma-vidy\'e4,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 spiritual knowledge, struggle very hard to get out of the clutches of material nature, but a devotee, by dint of his advancement in devotional service, automatically becomes detached from his material body. When the devotee's spiritual body begins to ma
nifest, he actually enters into his activities in transcendental life.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
At present we have contacted a material body, material mind and material intelligence, but when we become free from these material conditions, our spiritual body, spiritual mind and spi
ritual intelligence become manifest. In that transcendental state, a devotee attains all the benefits of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma, j\'ef\'e4na}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga.}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Although he never engages in fruitive activities or empiric speculation to attain mystic powers, automatically mystic powers app
ear in his service. A devotee does not want any kind of material opulence, but such opulence appears before him automatically. He does not have to endeavor for it. Because of his devotional service, he automatically becomes }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid2121178 
brahma-bh\'fcta}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  As stated before, this is confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4\'e0 ca yo 'vyabhic\'e4re\'eba\line bhakti-yogena sevate\line sa gu\'eb\'e4n samat
\'e9tyait\'e4n\line brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate
\par }\pard\plain \s384\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 
"One who is engaged in full devotional service, unfailing in all circumstances, at once transcends the modes of material nature and thus comes to the level of Brahman."}{\insrsid2121178  }{\cs383\insrsid2121178 (Bg. }{\insrsid2121178 14.26}{
\cs383\insrsid2121178\charrsid5197105 )}{\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
Because of his regular discharge of devotional service, a devotee attains the transcendental stage of life. Since his mind is transcendentally situated, he cannot think of anything but the lotus feet of the Lord. This is the meaning of the word }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 sa\'e0smara\'eba-anup\'fcrty\'e4.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  By constantly thinking of the lotus feet of the Lord, the devotee immediately becomes situated in }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e7uddha-sattva.}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'c7uddha-sattva}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  refers to that platform which is above the modes of material natur
e, including the mode of goodness. In the material world, the mode of goodness is considered to be representative of the highest perfection, but one has to transcend this mode and come to the stage of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e7uddha-sattva,}{
\insrsid5197105  or pure goodness, where the three qualities of material nature cannot act.
\par }\pard \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15149873 {\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kura gives the following example: If one has strong digestive power, after eating he automatically lights a fire within his stomach to digest everything and does not need to take medicine to
 aid his digestion. Similarly, the fire of devotional service is so strong that a devotee does not need to act separately to attain perfect knowledge or detachment from material attractions. A }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  may become detached from material attractions by prolonged discussions on subjects of knowledge and may in this way finally come to the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 brahma-bh\'fcta}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 stage, but a devotee does not have to undergo so much trouble. By virtue of his devotional service, he attains the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 brahma-bh\'fcta }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 stage without a doubt. The }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 are always doubtful about their constitutional position; therefore they mistakenly think of becoming one with the Supreme. However, a devotee's relationship with the Supreme becomes manifest beyond all doubt, and he immediately understands that his
 position is that of eternal servant of the Lord. }{\insrsid13178406 The }{\i\insrsid13178406\charrsid13178406 j}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  }{\insrsid13178406\charrsid5197105 may}{\insrsid13178406  }{\insrsid13178406\charrsid5197105 think}{\insrsid13178406  of attaining liberation }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 without }{\insrsid13178406 rendering }{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 devotion}{\insrsid13178406 al service, but actually this is not possible because their}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  intelligence is not as pure as that of a }{\insrsid13178406 pure }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
devotee. In other words, the }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  cannot become factually liberated unless they become elevat}{
\insrsid15149873 ed to the position of devotees. }{\i\insrsid15149873\charrsid15149873 \'c4ruhya k\'e5cchre\'eba }{\i\insrsid13178406\charrsid15149873 para\'e0 pada\'e0 tata\'f9 }{\i\insrsid5197105\charrsid15149873 patanty adho 'n\'e4d\'e5ta-yu\'f1mad-a
\'ecghraya\'f9}{\insrsid15149873  }{\cs337\i\insrsid15149873 (}{\cs337\i\insrsid15149873\charrsid15149873 Bh\'e4g. }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105  }{\insrsid5197105 1}{\insrsid15149873 0.2.32). }{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9}{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  may rise to the highest pos
ition, Brahman realization, but because of their lack of devotion unto the lotus feet of the Lord, they again fall down into material nature. Therefore }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na}{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yoga}{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  should not be accepted as the real processes for liberation. By discharging devotional service, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu automatically transcended all these positions. Since Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja P\'e5thu was a }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 \'e7akty\'e4ve\'e7a}{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  incarnation of the Supreme Lord, he did not have to act in any way to attain liberation. He came from the Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha world, or spiritual sky, in order to execute the will of the Supreme Lord on earth. Consequently he was to return home, back to Godhead, without having to execute }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na, yoga}{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 karma.}{\cs386\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Although P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was eternally a pure devotee of the Lord, he nonetheless adopted the process of 
devotional service in order to teach the people in general the proper process for executing the duties of life and ultimately returning home, back to Godhead.}{\cs386\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs386\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
