When the spiritual spark, which is described as one ten-thousandth part of the tip of a hair, is forced into material existence, that spark is covered by gross and subtle material elements. The material body is composed of five gross elements\emdash 
earth, water, fire, air and ether\emdash and three subtle elements\emdash mind, intelligence and ego. When one attains liberation, he is freed from these material coverings. Indeed, success in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 involves getting free from these material coverings and entering into spiritual existence. Lord Buddha's teachings of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nirv\'e4\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are based on this principle. Lord Buddha instructed his followers to give up these material coverings by means of meditation and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 Lord Buddha did not give any information about the soul, but if one follows his instructions strictly, he will ultimately become free from the material coverings and attain }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nirv\'e4\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 When a living entity gives up the materia
l coverings, he remains a spirit soul. This spirit soul must enter into the spiritual sky to merge into the Brahman effulgence. Unfortunately, unless the living entity has information of the spiritual world and the Vaiku\'eb\'f6
has, there is a 99.9 percent chance of his falling down again into material existence. There is, however, a small chance of being promoted to a spiritual planet from the Brahman effulgence, or the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmajyoti.}{
\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  This }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmajyoti}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is considered by impersonalists to be without variety, and the 
Buddhists consider it to be void. In either case, whether one accepts the spiritual sky as being without variety or void, there is none of the spiritual bliss which is enjoyed in the spiritual planets, the Vaiku\'eb\'f6has or K\'e5\'f1\'eb
aloka. In the absence of varieties of enjoyment, the spirit soul gradually feels an attraction to enjoy a life of bliss, and not having any information of K\'e5\'f1\'ebaloka or Vaiku\'eb\'f6
haloka, he naturally falls down to material activities in order to enjoy material varieties.}{\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }{\cs383\cf1\insrsid14643438\charrsid5197105 
