\'e4ga\'e7a\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Second Canto, Fifth Chapter, Lord Brahm\'e4 clearly explained to N\'e4
rada how the creation took place, and he explained one step after another the proper divisions of the senses, the controller of the senses, the objects of the senses, and the material elements, and he
 also explained how they are created one after another: the air from the sky, the fire from the air, the water from the fire, the earth from the water, etc. It is important to know thoroughly the process of creation as it applies to this cosmic manifestat
i
on. Similarly, this body is also created according to the same process by the Supreme Lord. The Personality of Godhead, after entering the universe, creates the cosmic manifestations one after another. Similarly, the living entity, after entering a womb o
f a mother, also collects his gross and subtle bodies, taking ingredients from the totality of sky, air, fire, water and earth. The words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yath\'e4-sth\'e4na\'e0 vibh\'e4ga\'e7a\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
