\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 As stated in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the source of material energy. Consequently He is sometimes called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid6108652 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 maya,}{\cf1\insrsid6108652  or the Supreme Person}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 who can create His pastimes through His potency known as the material energy. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'e9va,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or the individual living entity, becomes entrapped by the material 
energy by the supreme will of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105   we understand:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati
\line bhr\'e4mayan sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni\line yantr\'e4r\'fc\'f2h\'e4ni m\'e4yay\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6108652 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\cf1\insrsid6108652 "}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid6108652\charrsid6108652 
The Supreme Lord is situated in everyone's heart, O Arjuna, and is directing the wanderings of all living entities, who are seated as on a machine, made of the material energy.}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid6108652 " }{\cf1\insrsid6108652 (Bg. 18.61)}{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid6108652\charrsid6108652 
\par }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c9\'e7vara,}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is situated within the heart of all conditioned souls, and by His}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid6108652  supreme will the li
ving entity or individual soul}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  gets the facility to lord it over material nature in various types of bodies, which are known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yantra,}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 or the moving vehicle offered by the total material energy, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Although the individual living entity (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'e9va}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 ) and the Lord are both situated within the material energy, the Lord is directing the movements of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'e9va}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 soul by offering him different types of bodies through the material energy, and thus the living entity is wandering throughout the universes in various forms 
of body and becomes implicated in different situations, partaking of the reactions of fruitive activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s381\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5197105 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 When P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja became spiritually powerful by the enhancement of his spiritual knowledge}{\cs383\insrsid6108652 , }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and renunciation of material desires, he became a }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 prabhu,}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or master of his senses (sometimes called }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 gosv\'e4m\'e9}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 sv\'e4m\'e9).}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  This means that he was no longer controlled by the influence of material energy. When one is strong enough to give up the influence of material energy, he is called }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 prabhu.}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\insrsid6108652 svar\'fcpa}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 stha\'f9}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 is also very significant. The real identity of the individual soul lies in understanding or attaining the knowledge that he is eternally a servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. This understanding is called }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 svar\'fcpopalabdhi.}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  By culturing devotional service, the devotee gradually comes to understand his actual relationship with the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This understanding of one's pure spiritual position is called }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 svar\'fcpopalabdhi,}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  and when one attains that stage he can understand how he is related with the Supreme Personality of Godhead as a servant or friend}{\cs383\insrsid13511722 ,}{
\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or as a parent or conjugal lover. This stage of understanding is called }{\cs337\i\insrsid13511722 svar\'fcpa}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 stha\'f9.}{\cs383\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja realized this }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 svar\'fcpa}{\insrsid5197105  completely, and it will be clear in the later }{\insrsid13511722 chapters}{\insrsid5197105  that he personally left this world, or this body, by riding on a chariot sent from Vaiku
\'eb\'f6ha.
\par In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 prabhu}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  is also significant. As stated before, when one is completely self-realized and acts according to that position, he can be called }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 prabhu.}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  The spiritual master is addressed as "Prabhup\'e4da" because he is a completely self-realized soul. The word }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 p\'e4da}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  means "position," and }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 Prabhup\'e4da}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  indicates that he is given the position of }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 prabhu,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or the Supreme Personality of Godhead, for he acts on behalf of the
 Supreme Personality of Godhead. Unless one is a }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 prabhu,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or controller of the senses, he}{\insrsid13511722  cannot act as spiritual master. He is authorized by the S}{
\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 upreme }{\cs337\insrsid13511722\charrsid13511722 P}{\cs337\insrsid5197105\charrsid13511722 rabhu}{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 ,}{\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  or Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. In his verses praising the spiritual master, \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura writes:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d-dharitvena samasta-\'e7\'e4strair\line uktas tath\'e4 bh\'e4
vyata eva sadbhi\'f9}{\cs337\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
"The spiritual master is honored as much as the Supreme Lord because he is the most confidential servitor of the Lord." Thus P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja can also be called Prabhup\'e4da, or, as described herein, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prabhu.}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Another question may be raised in this connection. Since P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was a power incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7akty\'e4ve\'e7a-avat\'e4ra,}{
\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  why did he have to execute the regulative principles in order to become a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prabhu}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
? Because he appeared on this earth as an ideal king and because it is the duty of the king to instruct the citizens in the execution of devotional service, he followed all the regulative principles of devotional service in order to teach others. Simil
arly, Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, although K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself, taught us how to approach K\'e5\'f1\'eba as a devotee. It is said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4pani \'e4cari' bhakti \'e7ikh\'e4inu sab\'e4re.}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 
 Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu instructed others in the process of devotional service by setting the example Himself through His own personal actions. Similarly, P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, although a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7akty\'e4ve\'e7a-avat\'e4
ra}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  incarnation, still behaved exactly as a devotee in order to achieve the position of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prabhu.}{\cs386\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105  Furthermore, }{
