 indicate that a woman's duty or religious principle}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is to serve her husband in all conditions. In Vedic civilization a man is taught from the beginning of his life to become a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmac\'e4r\'e9,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  then an ideal }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 g\'e5hastha,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  then }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4naprastha,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  then }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sanny\'e4s\'e9,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 and the wife is taught just to follow the husband strictly in all conditions of life. After the period of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmacarya,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  a man accepts a householder's life, and the woman is also tau
ght by her parents to be a chaste wife. Thus when a girl and boy are united, both are trained for a life dedicated to a higher purpose. The boy is trained to execute his duty in accordance with the higher purpose of life, and the girl is trained to follow
 him. The chaste wife's duty is to keep her husband pleased in householder life in all respects, and when the husband retires from family life, she is to go to the forest and adopt the life of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4naprastha,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vana-v\'e4s\'e9.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  At that time the wife is to follow he
r husband and take care of him, just as she took care of him in householder life. But when the husband takes the renounced order of life, namely }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sanny\'e4sa,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 the wife is to return home and become a saintly woman, setting an example for her children and daughters-in-law and showing them how to live a life of austerity.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 When Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu took }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sanny\'e4sa,}{
