s material world people are engaged in different activities simply to achieve a little success in sense gratification. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karm\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are engaged in performing very difficult activities, and thus they open gigantic factories, build huge cities, make big scient
ific discoveries, etc. In other words, they are engaged in performing very costly sacrifices in order to be promoted to the higher planetary systems. Similarly, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are engaged in achieving a similar goal by accepting the tedious practices of mystic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 J\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are engaged in philosophical speculation in order to gain release from the clutches of material nature. In these ways everyone is engaged in performing very difficult tasks simply for the gratification of the senses. All of these are considered to
 be engaged in sense gratificatory activities (or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'f1aya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) because they all demand some facility for material existence. Actually the results of such activities are tempo}{\cf1\insrsid532114 rary, a}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 s K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself proclaims in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 , }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 antavat tu phala\'e0 te\'f1\'e4m:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  "The fruits
 [of those who worship the demigods] are limited and temporary." }{\cf1\insrsid532114 (Bg. 7.23) }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 Thus the fruits of the activities of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s, karm\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are ephemeral. Moreover, K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tad bhavaty alpa-medhas\'e4m:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  "They are simply meant for men of small intelligence." }{
\cf1\insrsid532114 (Bg. 7.23) }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'f1aya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  denotes sense gratification. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karm\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 flatly state that they want sense gratification. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  also want sense gratification, but they want it to a higher degree. It is their desire to show some miraculous results throug
h the practice of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Thus they strive very hard to achieve success in becoming smaller than the smallest or greater than the greatest, or in creating a planet like }{\cf1\insrsid532114 the }{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 earth}{\cf1\insrsid532114 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or, as scientists, by inventing so many wonderful machines. Similarly, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are also engaged in sense gratification, for they are simply interested in becoming one with the Supreme. Thus the aim of all these activities is sense gratification to a higher or a lower degree. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhaktas,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  however, are not interested in sense gratificatory practices; they are simply satisfied to get an opportunity to serve the Lord. Although they are satisfied in any condition, ther}{\cf1\insrsid532114 e is nothing they cannot obtain}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  because they are purely engaged in the service of the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs383\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5197105 The wives of the demigods c
