 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is especially stressed. This means that }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or devotional service, begins by hearing and chanting about Vi\'f1\'ebu. When we speak of Vi\'f1\'eb
u, we also refer to that which relates to Vi\'f1\'ebu. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7iva Pur\'e4\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Lord \'c7iva recommends Vi\'f1\'ebu worship to be the topmost worship, and better than Vi\'f1\'eb
u worship is worship of the Vai\'f1\'ebava or anything that is related to Vi\'f1\'ebu. The fact is explained herein that hearing and chanting about a Vai\'f1\'ebava is as good as hearing and chanting about Vi\'f1\'eb
u, for Maitreya has explained that anyone who hears about P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja with attention also attains the planet which Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e5thu attained. There is no duality between Vi\'f1\'ebu and the Vai\'f1\'ebava, and this is called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 advaya-j\'ef\'e4na.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  A Vai\'f1\'ebava is as important as Vi\'f1\'ebu, and therefore \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura wrote in his }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Gurv-a\'f1\'f6aka:

