 (meaning pious or well behaved}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) is very important, especially at the present moment. It is derived from the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  A perfect }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  is one who is always engaged in the devotional service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi's sons are described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhava\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 because of their complete obedience to their father. The father, king and spiritual master are supposed to be representatives of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and as such they have to be
 respected as the Supreme Lord. It is the duty of the father, the spiritual master and the king to regulate their subordinates in such a way that they ultimately become fully unalloyed devotees of the Supreme Lord. That is the duty of the superiors, and i
t is the duty of the subordinates to obey their orders perfectly and in a disciplined way. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7iras\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid15168485  (on their heads}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) is also significant, for the Pracet\'e4
s accepted the orders of their father and carried them on their heads, which means they accepted them in complete surrender.
