u lies in the ocean of Garbha within this universe, and from His navel the lotus flower sprouts. Lord Brahm\'e4 is generated from that lotus flower, and from Lord Brahm\'e4 the creation of this material world begins. As such, the Supreme Persona
lity of Godhead, Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, is the origin of the material senses and sense objects. Since Lord \'c7
iva considers himself to be one of the products of the material world, his senses are under the control of the supreme creator. The Supreme Lord is also known as H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7
a, master of the senses, which indicates that our senses and sense objects are formed by the Supreme Lord. As such, He can control our senses and out of His mercy engage them in the service of the master of the senses. In the conditione
d state, the living entity struggles in this material world and engages his senses for material satisfaction. However, if the living entity is graced by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he can engage these very senses in the service of the Lord. Lord 
\'c7iva desires not to be misled by the material senses but to engage always in the service of the Lord without being subject to contamination by materialistic influences. By the grace and help of Lord V\'e4
sudeva, who is all-pervading, one can engage his senses in devotional service without deviation, just as the Lord acts without deviation.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8216104 \'e7\'e4nt\'e4ya k\'fc\'f6a}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sth
\'e4ya sva-roci\'f1e}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are very significant. Although the Lord is within this material world, He is not disturbed by the waves of material existence. However,
 conditioned souls are agitated by six kinds of transformations; namely, they become agitated when they are hungry, when they are thirsty, when they are aggrieved, when they are illusioned, when they grow old}{\cf1\insrsid8216104 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 and when they are on the deathbed. Although conditioned souls become very easily illusioned by these conditions in the material world, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as the Supersoul, V\'e4
sudeva, is never agitated by these transformations. Therefore it is said here (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8216104 k\'fc\'f6a}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sth\'e4ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) that He is always pe
aceful and devoid of agitation because of His prowess, which is described herein as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sva-roci\'f1e,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 indicating that He is illuminated by His own transcendental position. In other words, the individual soul, although within the illumination of the Supreme, sometimes falls down from that illumination because of his tiny position, and when he fal}{
\cf1\insrsid8216104 ls down he enters into material}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  conditional life. The Lord, however, is not subject to such conditioning; therefore He is described as self-illuminated. Consequently any c
onditioned soul within this material universe can remain completely perfect when he is u}{\cf1\insrsid8216104 nder the protection of V\'e4sudeva}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or when he is engaged in devotional service.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
