i ca bh\'fct\'e4ni\line m\'e4\'e0 tu veda na ka\'e7cana
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
"O Arjuna, as the Supreme Personality of Godhead, I know everything that has happened in the past, all that is happening in the present, and all things that are yet to come. I also know all living entities; but Me no one knows."}{\cf1\insrsid8457300  }{
\cs347\cf1\insrsid14315929\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid14315929 7.26) }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 K\'e5\'f1\'eba knows everything, but one cannot know K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a without being favored by Him. Thus for K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His representative there is no question of a theory of uncertainty. What K\'e5\'f1\'eba says is all perfect and certa
in and is applicable to the past, present and future. Nor is there any uncertainty for one who knows exactly what K\'e5\'f1\'eba says. The K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is based on }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  as it is, as spoken by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and for those who are engaged in this movement, there is no question of uncertainty.
\par Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is also addressed herein as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4\'e7i\'f1\'e4m \'e9\'e7a.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 The great saintly personalities, sages and demigods are able to offer benedictions to ordinary living entities, but they in turn are benedicted by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Without being benedicted by K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, one cannot offer benediction to anyone else. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 manave,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  meaning "unto the supreme Manu," is also significant. The supreme Manu in Vedic literature is Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, who is an incarnatio
n of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. All the Manus are empowered incarnations of K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 manvantara-avat\'e4ra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ). There are fourteen Manus in one day of Brahm\'e4, 420 in one month, }{\cf1\insrsid8457300 
5,040 in one year, and 504,000 Manus in the lifetime of Brahm\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid4618143  Since }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 all the Manus are directors of human society, ultimately K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the supreme director of human society. In another sense, the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 manave}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicates the perfection of all kinds of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantras.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  delivers the conditioned soul from his bondage; so simply by chanting the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5
\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare, one can gain deliverance from any condition.
\par }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 K\'e4ra\'eb\'e4tmane:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  everything has a cause. The theory of chance is repudiated in this verse. Because everything has its cause, there is n
o question of chance. Because so-called philosophers and scientists are unable to find the real cause, they foolishly say that everything happens by chance. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is described as the cause of all causes; therefore He is addressed herein as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4tmane.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 His very personality is the original cause of everything, the root of everything and the seed of everything. As described in the }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 , }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 janm\'e4dy asya yata
\'f9}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid4618143  }{\cf1\insrsid4618143 (1.1.2)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 :}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 the Absolute Truth is the supreme cause of all emanations.
\par The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4\'eckhya-yoge\'e7var\'e4ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is also significant herein, for K\'e5\'f1\'eba is described in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  as Yoge\'e7vara, the master of all mystic powers. Without possessing inconceivable mystic powers, one cannot be accepted as God. In this age of Kali, those who have a littl
e fragmental portion of mystic power claim to be God, but such pseudo Gods can only be accepted as fools, for only K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the Supreme Person who possesses all mystic and yogic perfections. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4\'eckhya-yoga}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  system popular at the present moment was propounded by the atheist Kapila, but the original }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4\'eckhya-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  system was propounded by an incarnation of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a also named Kapila, the son of Devah\'fcti. Similarly, Datt\'e4treya, another incarnation of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, also explained the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4\'eckhya-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  system. Thus K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the origin of all }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4\'eckhya-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  systems and mystic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  powers.
\par The words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid4618143 pur\'e4\'eb\'e4ya puru\'f1\'e4ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are also worthy of special attention. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  K\'e5\'f1\'eba is accepted as the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4di-puru\'f1a,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the original person, or the original enjoyer. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is also accepted as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pur\'e4\'eba-puru\'f1a,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the oldest person. Although He is the oldest of all personalities, He is also the youngest of all, or }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nava-yauvana.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Another significant word is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dharm\'e4ya.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Since K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the original propounder of all kinds of religious principles, it is said: 
}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dharma\'e0 tu s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d bhagavat-pra\'eb\'e9tam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . No one can introduce a new type of religion, for religion is already there, having been established by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. In }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  K\'e5\'f1\'eba informs us of the original }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dharma}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and asks us to give up a
ll kinds of religious principles. The real }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dharma}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is surrender unto Him. In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Mah\'e4bh\'e4rata,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  it is also said:
