V}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 eda-mantra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  it is said that the Supreme Absolute Truth is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sarva-k\'e4ma\'f9 sarva-gandha\'f9 sarva-rasa\'f9,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or, in other words, He is known as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 raso vai sa\'f9,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the source of all relishable relationships (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 rasas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ). We have various senses\emdash 
the powers of seeing, tasting, smelling, touching, etc.\emdash and all the propensities of our senses can be satisfied when the senses are engaged in the service of the Lord. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'eba h\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a-sevana
\'e0 bhaktir ucyate}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5380398  }{\cf1\insrsid5380398 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5380398 N\'e4rada-pa\'efcar\'e4tra}{\cf1\insrsid5380398 ).}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 "Bhakti}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  mea
ns engaging all the senses in the service of the master of the senses, H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a."  }{\insrsid5197105\charrsid13781628 These material}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 senses, however, cannot be engaged in the service of the Lord; therefore one has to become free from all designations. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Sarvop\'e4dhi-vinirmukta\'e0 tatparatvena nirmalam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 One has to become free from all designation or false egotism and thus become purified. When we engage our senses in the service of the Lord, the desires or the inclinations of the senses can be perfectly fulfilled. Lord \'c7iva therefore wants to see t
he Lord in a form }{\cf1\insrsid13781628 which is inconceivable to the Buddhist}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  philosophers, or the Buddhists.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
The impersonalists and the voidists also have to see the form of the Absolute. In Buddhist temples there are forms of Lord Buddha in meditation, but these are not worshiped like the forms of the Lord in Vai\'f1\'ebava temples (forms like R\'e4dh\'e4-K\'e5
\'f1\'eba, S\'e9t\'e4-R\'e4ma or Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba). Amongst the different }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 samprad\'e4yas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (Vai\'f1\'ebava sects) either R\'e4dh\'e4-K\'e5\'f1\'eba or Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a is worshiped. Lord \'c7iva wants to see that form perfectly, just as the devo}{\cf1\insrsid13781628 tees want to see it. T}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 he words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'fcpa\'e0 priyatama\'e0 sv\'e4n\'e4m}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are specifically mentioned here, indicating that Lord \'c7iva wants to see that form which is very dear to the devotees. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sv\'e4n\'e4m}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is especially significant because only the devotees
 are very, very dear to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s, yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karm\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are not particularly dear, for the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karm\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  simply want to see the Supreme Personality of Godhead as their order supplier. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  want to see Him to become one with 
Him, and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  want to see Him partially represented within their heart as Param\'e4tm\'e4, but the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhaktas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 or the devotees, want to see Him in His complete perfection. As stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahma-sa\'e0hit}{\cs347\cf1\insrsid14184656\charrsid14184656 \'e4 }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 ve\'ebu\'e0 kva\'ebantam aravinda-dal\'e4yat\'e4k\'f1a\'e0\line barh\'e4vata\'e0sam asit
\'e4mbuda-sundar\'e4\'ecgam\line kandarpa-ko\'f6i-kaman\'e9ya-vi\'e7e\'f1a-\'e7obha\'e0\line govindam \'e4di-puru\'f1a\'e0 tam aha\'e0 bhaj\'e4mi
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
"I worship Govinda, the primeval Lord, who is adept at playing on His flute, whose eyes are blooming like lotus petals, whose head is bedecked with peacock feathers
, whose beauty is tinged with the hue of blue clouds, and whose unique loveliness charms millions of Cupids." }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid9138202\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid9138202 5.30) }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 Thus Lord \'c7
iva's desire is to see the Supreme Personality of Godhead as He is described in this way}{\insrsid9138202 \emdash }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 that is, he wants to see Him as He appears to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bh\'e4gavatas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 the devotees. The conclusion is that Lord \'c7iva wants to see Him in complete perfection and not in the impersonalist or voidist way. Although the Lord is one in His various forms (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 advaitam acyutam an\'e4dim}{
