\'eba cannot be approached by the neophyte devotees; therefore temple worship according to regulative principles is offered to Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Although there may be a R\'e4dh\'e4-K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vigraha,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  or form, the worship of the neophyte devotees is acceptable as Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba worship. Worship according to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3491094 P\'e4\'efcar\'e4trika}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 -vidhi}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vidhi-m\'e4rga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and worship according to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3491094 Bh\'e4gavata}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 -vidhi}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  principles is called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The principles of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are especially meant for devotees who are elevated to the V\'e5nd\'e4vana platform.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid547208 The inhabitants of V\'e5nd\'e4vana, }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gop\'e9s,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  mother Ya\'e7od\'e4, Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the cowherd boys, the cows and everyone else\emdash are actually on the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid547208 B}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 h\'e4gavata-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  platform. }{\cf1\insrsid7435021 However, t}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 hey participate in five basic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 rasas}{\cf1\insrsid7435021 \emdash }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 d\'e4sya, sakhya, v\'e4tsalya, m\'e4dhurya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4nta.}{\cf1\insrsid7435021  A}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 lthough these five }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 rasas}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  are found in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid547208 Bh\'e4gavata}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 -m\'e4rga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid547208 Bh\'e4gavata}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 -m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is especially meant for }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4tsalya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4dhurya,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or paternal and conjugal relationships. Yet there is the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid7435021 p}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ralambha-sakhya,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the higher fraternal worship of the Lord especially enjoyed by the cowherd boys. Although there is friendship between K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and the cowherd boys, this friendship is different from the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ai\'e7varya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  friendship between K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Arjuna. When Arjuna saw the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'e7va-r\'fcpa,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  the gigantic universal form of the Lord, he was afraid for having treated K\'e5\'f1\'eba as an ordinary friend; therefore he begged K\'e5\'f1\'eba's pardon. However, the cowherd boys who are friends of K\'e5\'f1\'eba in V\'e5nd\'e4
vana sometimes ride on the shoulders of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. They treat K\'e5\'f1\'eba equally, just as they treat one another, and they are never afraid of Him, nor do they ever beg His pardon. Thus the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid547208 Bh\'e4gavata}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 -m\'e4rga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  friendship exists on a higher platform with K\'e5\'f1\'eba, namely the platform of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vipralambha}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  friendship. Paternal friendship, }{\cf1\insrsid7435021 conjugal }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 paternal service}{\cf1\insrsid7435021 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid7435021 as well as}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  conjugal service}{
\cf1\insrsid7435021 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are visible in the V\'e5nd\'e4vana }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  relationships.
\par Without serving K\'e5\'f1\'eba according to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vidhi-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  regulative principles of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid547208 P\'e4\'efcar\'e4trika}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 -vidhi,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 unscrupulous persons want to jump immediately to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  principles. Such persons are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sahajiy\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  There are also d
emons who enjoy depicting K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His pastimes with the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gop\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  taking advantage of K\'e5\'f1\'eba by their licentious character. These demons who print books and write lyrics on the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  principles are surely on the way to hell. Unfortunately, they lead others down with them. Devotees in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness should be very careful to avoid such demons. One should strictly follow the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vidhi-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  regulative principles in the worship of Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, although the Lord is present in the temple as R\'e4dh\'e4-K\'e5\'f1\'eba. R\'e4dh\'e4-K\'e5\'f1\'eba includes Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a; therefore when one worships the Lord according to the regulative principles, the Lord accepts the service in the role of Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105  Nectar of Devotion}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 full instructions are given about the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vidhi-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  worship of R\'e4dh\'e4-K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Although there are sixty-four kinds of offenses one can commit in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vidhi-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  worship, in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ga-m\'e4rga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 worship there is no consideration of such offenses because the devotees on that platform are very much elevated, and there is no question of offense. But if we do not follow the regulative principles on the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vidhi-m\'e4rga}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  platform and keep our eyes trained to spot offenses, we will not make progress.
\par In his description of K\'e5\'f1\'eba's beauty, Lord \'c7iva uses the words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 c\'e4rv\'e4yata-catur-b\'e4hu suj\'e4ta-rucir\'e4nanam,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicating the beautiful four-armed form of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, or Vi\'f1
\'ebu. Those who worship Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba describe Him as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 suj\'e4ta-rucir\'e4nanam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid2629474 V}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 i\'f1\'ebu-tattva}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 there are hundreds and thousands and millions of forms of the Supreme Lord, but of all these forms, the form of K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the most beautiful. Thus for those who worship K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 suj\'e4ta-rucir\'e4
nanam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is used.
\par The four arms of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu have different purposes. The hands holding a lotus flower and conchshell are meant for the devotees, whereas the other two hands, holding a disc and mac}{\cf1\insrsid2629474 e}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 or club, are meant for the demons. Actually all of the Lord's arms are auspicious, whether they are holding conchshells and flowers or clubs and discs. The demons killed by Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 cakra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  disc
 and club are elevated to the spiritual world, just like the devotees who are protected by the hands holding the lotus flower and conchshell. However, the demons who are elevated to the spiritual world are situated in the impersonal Brahman effulgence, wh
ereas the devotees are allowed to enter into the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha planets. Those who are devotees of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba are immediately elevated to the Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4vana planet.
\par The Lord's beauty is compared to rainfall because when the rain falls in the rainy season, it b
ecomes more and more pleasing to the people. After the scorching heat of the summer season, the people enjoy the rainy season very much. Indeed, they even come out of their doors in the villages and enjoy the rainfall directly. Thus the Lord's bodily feat
ures are compared }{\cf1\insrsid14099721 with}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the clouds of the rainy season. The devotees enjoy the Lord's beauty because it is a collection of all kinds of beauties. Therefore the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
sarva-saundarya-sa\'ecgraham}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is used. No one can say that the body of the Lord is wanting in beautiful parts. It is completely }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 p\'fcr\'ebam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 Everything is complete: God's creation, God's beauty and God's bodily features. All these are so complete that all one's desires can become fully satisfied when one sees the beauty of the Lord. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sarva-saundarya}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicates that there are different types of beauties in the material and spiritual worlds}{\cf1\insrsid14099721 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 and that the Lord contains all of them. Both materialists and spiritualists can enjoy the beauty of the Lord. Because the Supreme Lord attracts everyone, including demons and devotees, materialists and spiritualists, He is called K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. Similarly, His devotees also attract everyone. As mentioned in the }{\i\insrsid9459893\charrsid9459893 \'d1}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid9459893\charrsid9459893 a}{\i\insrsid9459893\charrsid9459893 \'f2}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 -gosv\'e4m\'e9-stotra:}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dh\'e9r\'e4dh\'e9ra-jana-priyau}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 \emdash the Gosv\'e4m\'e9s are equally dear to the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dh\'e9ra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (devotees) and }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 adh\'e9ra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (demons). Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba was not very pleasing to the demons when He was present in V\'e5nd\'e4vana, but the six Gosv\'e4m\'e9s were pleasing to the demons when they were present in V\'e5nd
\'e4vana. That is the beauty of the Lord's dealings with His devotees; sometimes the Lord gives more credit to His devotees than He takes for Himself. For instance, on the Battlefield of Kuruk\'f1etra, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a fought simply by giving directions. Yet it was Arjuna who took the credit for fighting. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Nimitta-m\'e4tra\'e0 bhava savyas\'e4cin}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid9459893  }{\cf1\insrsid9459893 (Bg. 11.33). "You, O Savyas\'e4cin}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  [Arjuna], can be but an instrument in the fight."  Everything was arranged by the Lord, but the credit of victory was given to Arjuna. Similarly, in the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement, everything is happening according to the predictions of Lord Caitanya, but the credit goes to Lord Caitanya's sincere servants. Thus the Lord is described herein as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sarva-saundarya-sa\'ecgraham.

