 the lotus feet of the Lord. When a devotee wants to see the transcendental form of the Lord, he begins his meditation on the Lord's body by first looking at the feet of the Lord. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  is considered to be the transcendental sound form of the Lord, and the twelve cantos are divided in accordance with the transcendental form of the Lord. The First and Second Cantos of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4
gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are called the two lotus feet of the Lord. It is therefore suggested by Lord \'c7iva that one should first try to see the lotus feet of the Lord. This also means that if one is serious about reading }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  he must begin by seriously studying the First and Second Cantos.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The beauty of the lotus feet of the Lord is compared to the petals of a lotus flower whi
ch grows in the autumn season. By nature's law, in autumn the dirty or muddy waters of rivers and lakes become very clean. At that time the lotus flowers growing in the lakes appear very bright and beautiful. The lotus flower itself is compared }{
\cf1\insrsid535446 with}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the lotus feet of the Lord, and the petals are compared }{\cf1\insrsid535446 with}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the nails of the feet of the Lord. The nails of the feet of the Lord are very bright, as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  testifies. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c4nanda-cinmaya-sad-ujjvala-vigrahasya:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  every limb of the transcendental body of the Lord is made of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4nanda-cinmaya-sad-ujjvala.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 Thus every limb is eternally bright. As sunshine dissipates the darkness of this material world, the effulgence emanating from the body of the Lord immediately dries up the darkness in the heart of the conditioned 
soul. In other words, everyone serious about understanding the transcendental science and seeing the transcendental form of the Lord must first of all attempt to see the lotus feet of the Lord by studying the First and Second Cantos of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  When one sees the lotus feet of the Lord, all kinds of doubts and fears within the heart are vanquished.
\par In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  it is said that in order to make spiritual progress, one must become fearless. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Abhaya\'e0 sattva-sa\'e0
\'e7uddhi\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (}{\cf1\insrsid535446 Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 16.1). Fearfulness is the result of material involvement. It is also said in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid14550478 :}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhaya\'e0 dvit\'e9y\'e4bhinive\'e7ata\'f9 sy\'e4t}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid535446  }{\i\cf1\insrsid535446\charrsid12064898 (Bh\'e4g. }{\cf1\insrsid535446\charrsid535446 1}{\cf1\insrsid535446 1.2.37).}{
\cf1\insrsid14550478  F}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 earfulness is a creation of the bodily conception of life. As long as one is absorbed in the thought that he is this material body, he 
