\cf1\insrsid15685442 eye}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . The word "meditation" is very popular in this age amongst the common people, but they do not know the actual meaning of meditation. However, from Vedic literature we learn that the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are always absorbed in meditation upon the lotus feet of the Lord. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Dhy\'e4n\'e4vasthita-tad-gatena manas\'e4 pa\'e7yanti ya\'e0 yogina\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid4348738 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid15149873\charrsid15149873 Bh\'e4g. }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid4348738 12.13.1)}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . This is the real business of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yog\'e9s:}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  to think of the lotus feet of the Lord. Lord \'c7iva therefore advises that one who is actually serious about purification must engage himself in this type of meditation or in the mystic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  system, which will help him not only to see the Lord within constantly but to see Him }{\cf1\insrsid4348738 eye}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  to }{\cf1\insrsid4348738 eye}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and become His associate in Vaiku\'eb\'f6
haloka or Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4vana.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sva-dharmam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (as in }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sva-dharmam anuti\'f1\'f6hat\'e4m}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) indicates that the system of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 \emdash which indicates the occupational duties of the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and which is the perfect institution for humanity\emdash must be supported by }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  if one at all wants security in life. Generally people think that simply by executing the occupational duties of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid4348738 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or the duty of a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmac\'e4r\'e9, g\'e5hastha, v\'e4naprastha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid4348738 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  one becomes fearless or securely attains liberation, but factually unless all these occupational duties are accompanied by }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
bhakti-yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  one cannot become fearless. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  there are descriptions of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-yoga, j
\'ef\'e4na-yoga, bhakti-yoga, dhy\'e4na-yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  etc., but unless one comes to the point of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  these other }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yogas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 cannot help one attain the highest perfection of life. In other words, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is the only means for liberation. We find this conclusion also in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5
ta}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  in a discussion between Lord Caitanya and R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya regarding a human being's liberation from this material world. In that discussion R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya referred to the execution of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and Lord Caitanya indicated}{\cf1\insrsid4348738  (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid4348738 eho b\'e4hya}{\cf1\insrsid4348738 )}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  that the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cf1\insrsid4348738  was simply external}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . Lord Caitanya wanted to impress upon R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya that simply by executing the duties of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var
\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  one is not guaranteed liberation. Finally R\'e4m\'e4nanda R\'e4ya referred to the process of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sth\'e4ne sthit\'e4
\'f9 \'e7ruti-gat\'e4\'e0 tanu-v\'e4\'ec-manobhi\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\i\cf1\insrsid16085486\charrsid16085486 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  10.14.3). Regardless of one's condition of life, if he practices }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
bhakti-yoga,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  which begins with hearing (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7ruti-gat\'e4m}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) the transcendental messages of the Lord through the mouths of devotees, he gradually conquers the unconquerable God.

\par God is known to be unconquerable, but one who submissively hears the words of a self-realized soul conquers the unconquerable. The conclusion is that if one is serious about liberation, he not only should execute the occupational duties of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  but should also engage in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 by beginning hearing from a realized soul. This process will help the devotee conquer the unconquerable Supreme Personality of Godhead and become His associate after giving up the material body.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
