\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11692357 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 It is clearly explained that Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba has multi}{\insrsid12873564 -energies}{
\insrsid5197105  }{\insrsid12873564 that}{\insrsid5197105  can be grouped into three: namely the external energy, the internal energy}{\insrsid12873564 ,}{\insrsid5197105  and the marginal energy. There are also different cosmic manifestations\emdash 
namely}{\insrsid12873564 ,}{\insrsid5197105  the spiritual world and the material world\emdash as well as different types of living entities. Some living entities are conditioned, an
d others are eternally free. The eternally free living entities are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nitya-mukta,}{\insrsid5197105 
 for they never come in contact with the material energy. However, some living entities are conditioned in this material world, and thus they think themselves separated 
from the Supreme Lord. Due to their contact with the material energy, their existence is always troublesome. Being always in distress, the conditioned soul considers the material energy to be very much disturbing. This fact is explained by a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 kavi,}{\insrsid11692357  or poet: }{\i\insrsid5197105\charrsid11692357 k\'e5\'f1\'eba bhuli' sei j\'e9va an\'e4di-bahir}{\i\insrsid11692357\charrsid11692357 -}{\i\insrsid5197105\charrsid11692357 mukha}{
\i\insrsid11692357\charrsid11692357 / }{\i\insrsid5197105\charrsid11692357 ataeva m\'e4y\'e4 t\'e4re deya sa\'e0s\'e4ra-du\'f9kha}{\insrsid11692357 . }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
When the living entity forgets the Supreme Lord and wants to enjoy himself independently, imitating the Supreme Lord, he is captured by the false notion that he is the
 enjoyer and is separated from the Supreme Lord. This material energy is therefore very much troublesome to the spiritual energy, the living entity, but the material energy is never troublesome to the Supreme Lord. Indeed, for the Supreme Lord, both mater
ial and spiritual energy are the same. In this verse Lord \'c7iva explains that the material energy is never troublesome to the Supreme Lord. The Supreme Lord is always independent, but because the living entities are not independent\emdash 
due to their false idea of becoming independently happy\emdash the material energy is troublesome. Consequently the material energy creates differentiation.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Because the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9
 philosophers cannot understand this, they want to be relieved from the material energy. However, because a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava philosopher is in full knowledge of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he finds no disturbance even in the material energy. This is because he knows how to utilize the material energy for the service of the Lord. In the government, the criminal depar
tment and civil department may appear different in the eyes of the citizens, but in the eyes of the government both departments are one and the same. The criminal department is troublesome for the criminal but not for the obedient citizen. Similarly, this
 material energy is troublesome for the conditioned soul, but it has nothing to do with the liberated souls who are engaged in the service of the Lord. Through the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 puru\'f1a-avat\'e4ra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Mah\'e4-Vi\'f1\'eb
u, the Supreme Personality of Godhead created the whole cosmic manifestation. Simply by breathing out all the universes, the Lord creates and maintains the cosmic manifestation as Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. Then as Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eb
a, He annihilates the cosmic manifestation. Yet despite the creation, maintenance and destruction of the cosmos, the
 Lord is not affected. The various activities of the Lord must be very disturbing to the tiny living entities, but since the Lord is supremely great, He is never affected. Lord \'c7
iva or any other pure devotee can see this clearly without being blinded by }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bheda-buddhi,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or differentiation. }{\cf1\insrsid13909368 For a devotee, the Lord is the S}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 upreme }{
\cf1\insrsid13909368 Spirit S}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 oul. Since He is supremely powerful, His various powers are also spiritual. For a devotee, there is nothing material, for material existence only means forgetfulness of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.

