\cf1\insrsid5197105  there are animal sacrifices in almost all religious rituals. However, one should not be satisfied simply by killing animals according to the directions of the scriptures. One should transcend the ritualistic ceremonie
s and try to understand the actual truth, the purpose of life. N\'e4rada Muni wanted to instruct the King about the real purpose of life and invoke a spirit of renunciation in his heart. Knowledge and the spirit of renunciation (}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na-vair\'e4gya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) are the ultima
te goal of life. Without knowledge, one cannot become detached from material enjoyment, and without being detached from material enjoyment, one cannot make spiritual advancement. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Karm\'e9s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are generally engaged in sense gratification, and for this end they are prepared to commit so many sinful activities. Animal sacrifice is but one such sinful activity. Consequently, by his mystic power N\'e4rada Muni showed King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1
at the dead animals which he had sacrificed.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.25.8
