unto you; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 kathayi\'f1ye}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash I shall speak; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 amum}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash on this subject matter; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 itih\'e4sam}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash history; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 pur\'e4tanam}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash very old; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjanasya}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash in the matter of Pura\'efjana; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 caritam}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash his character; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 nibodha}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash try to understand; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 gadata\'f9 mama}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash while I am speaking.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10101918 {\b\cf11\insrsid10101918\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid10101918 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 In this connection I wish to narrate an old history connected with the character
 of a king called Pura\'efjana. Please try to hear me with great attention.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid853019 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid853019\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The great sage N\'e4rada Muni turned toward another topic\emdash the history of King Pura\'ef
jana. This is nothing but the history of King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at told in a different way. In other words, this is an allegorical presentation. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 means "one who enjoys in a body." This is clearly explained in the next few chapters. Because a person entangled in material activities wants to hear stories of material activities, N\'e4rada Muni turned to the topics of King Pura\'ef
jana, who is none other than King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at. N\'e4rada Muni did not}{\cf1\insrsid10758692 , however,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 deprecate the value of performing sacrifices in which animals are sacrificed. Lord Buddha, however, directly rejected all animal sacrifice. \'c7r\'e9la Jayadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 has stated: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nindasi yaj\'efa-vidher ahaha \'e7
ruti-j\'e4tam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7ruti j\'e4tam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicates that in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 animal sacrifice is recommended, but Lord Buddha directly denied Vedic authority in order to stop animal sacrifice. Consequently Lord Buddha is not accepted by the followers of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 Because he does not accept the authority of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Lord Buddha is depicted as an agnostic or atheist. The great sage N\'e4rada cannot decry the authority of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}
{\cf1\insrsid5197105  but he wanted to indicate to King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at that the path of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is very difficult and risky.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Foolish persons accept the difficult path of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  for the sake of sense enjoyment, and those who are too much attached to sense enjoyment are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'fc\'f2has}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (rascals). It is very difficult for a }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m
\'fc\'f2ha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  to understand the ultimate goal of life. In the propagation of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement, we actually see that many people are not attracted because they are }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'fc\'f2has}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  engaged in fruitive activity. It is said: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 upade\'e7o hi m\'fcrkh\'e4\'eb\'e4\'e0 prakop\'e4ya na \'e7\'e4ntaye}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid13001469  (Hitopade\'e7a)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  If good instructions are given to a foolish rascal, he simply becomes angry and turns against the instructions instead of taking advantage of them. Because N\'e4rada Muni knew this very well, he indirectly in
structed the King by giving him the history of his entire life. In order to wear a gold or diamond nose pin or earring, one has to pierce the ear or nose. Such pain endured for the sake of sense gratification is endured on the path of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the path
 of fruitive activity. If one wishes to enjoy something in the future, he has to endure trouble in the present. If one wants to become a millionaire in the future and enjoy his riches, he has to work very hard at the present moment in order to accumulate 
money. This is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2\'e9ya.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Those who are too much attached to such a path undergo the risk anyway. N\'e4rada Muni wanted to show King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1
at how one undergoes great troubles and miseries in order to engage in fruitive activity. A person who is very much attached to material activity is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'f1ay\'e9.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  A }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
vi\'f1ay\'e9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is an enjoyer of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'f1aya,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  which means eating, sleeping, mating and defending. N\'e4rada Muni is indirectly indicating through the story of King Pura\'ef
jana that eating, sleeping, mating and defending are troublesome and risky.
\par The words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 itih\'e4sam}{\cf1\insrsid13001469  (history}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pur\'e4tanam}{\cf1\insrsid13001469  (old}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
) indicate that although a living entity lives within the material body, the history of the living entity within the material body is very old. In this regard, \'c7r\'e9la Bhaktivinoda \'d6h\'e4kura has sung}{\cf1\insrsid11166418 :}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }
{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 an\'e4di karama-phale, padi' bhav\'e4r\'ebav}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid11166418 a jale, tarib\'e4re n\'e4 dekhi up\'e4ya.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 "Due to my past fruitive activities I have fallen into the water of material existence, and I cannot find any way to get out of it." Every living entity is suffering in thi
s material existence from past activities; therefore everyone has a very old history. Foolish material scientists have manufactured their own theories of evolution, which are simply concerned with the material body. But actually this is not the real evolu
tion. The real evolution is the history of the living entity, who is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana,}{\cf1\insrsid11166418  living within the body.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  \'c7r\'e9 N\'e4
rada Muni will explain this evolutionary theory in a different way for the understanding of sane persons.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
