 "He does not die, even after the annihilation of the body." Thus the living entity transmigrates from one body to another and performs various activities. In each body the living entity performs so many acts. Sometimes he becomes a great hero\emdash 
just like Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and Ka\'e0sa}{\cf1\insrsid3162130 , or in the modern age}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 Napoleon or Hitler. The activities of such men are certainly very great, but as soon as their bodies are finished, everything else is finished. Then they remain in name only. Therefore a living entity may be called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 b\'e5
hac-chrav\'e4\'f9;}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  he may have a great reputation for various types of activities. Nonetheless, he has a friend whom he does not know. Materialistic persons do not understand that God is present as the Supersoul}{\cf1\insrsid3162130 
 and}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  situated within the heart of every living entity. Although the Param\'e4tm\'e4 sits beside the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  as a friend, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'e9v\'e4tm\'e4,
}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or living entity, does not know it. Consequently he is described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 avij\'ef\'e4ta-sakh\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  meaning "one who has an unknown friend." The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 avij
\'ef\'e4ta-ce\'f1\'f6ita\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is also significant because a living entity works hard under the direction of the Param\'e4tm\'e4
 and is carried away by the laws of nature. Nonetheless, he thinks himself independent of God and independent of the stringent laws of material nature. It is stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g
\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
