a also used his other senses in the service of the Lord. He engaged his eyes in seeing the Deity in the temple nicely decorated with flowers. He engaged his sense of smell by smelling the flowers, and he engaged his legs by walking to the
 temple. His hands were engaged in cleansing the temple, and his ears were engaged in hearing about K\'e5\'f1\'eba. His tongue was engaged in two ways: in speaking about K\'e5\'f1\'eba and in tasting }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pras\'e4da}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  offered to the Deity. Materialistic persons, who are under the ful
l control of material intelligence, cannot perform all these activities. Thus, consciously or unconsciously, they become entangled by the dictations of material intelligence. This fact is summarized in the following verse.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
