My dear King, once upon a time King Pura\'efjana took up his great bow, and}{\fs28\insrsid4659504 ,}{\fs28\insrsid5197105  equipped with golden armor and a quiver of unlimited arrows and accompanie
d by eleven commanders, he sat on his chariot driven by five swift horses and went to the forest named Pa\'ef
ca-prastha. He took with him in that chariot two explosive arrows. The chariot itself was situated on two wheels and one revolving axle. On the chario
t were three flags, one rein, one chariot driver, one sitting place, two poles to which the harness was fixed, five weapons and seven coverings. The chariot moved in five different styles, and five obstacles lay before it. All the decorations of the chari
ot were made of gold.
