These three verses explain how the material body of the living entity is under the control of the three qualities of the external energy. The body itself is the chariot, and the living entity is the owner of the body, as explained in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 : }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dehino 'smin yath\'e4 dehe}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid10095509  }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid10095509\charrsid14184656 
(Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid10095509 2.13)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The owner of the body is called the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 deh\'e9,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 and he is situated within this body, specifically within the heart. The living entity is driven by one chariot driver. The chariot itself is made of three }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gu\'ebas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 three qualities of material nature, as confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 : }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yantr\'e4r\'fc\'f2h\'e4ni m\'e4yay\'e4}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid10095509  }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid10095509\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid10095509 18.61)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yantra}{\cf1\insrsid10095509  means carriage.}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  The body is given by material nature, and the driver of that body is Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supersoul. The living entity is seated within the chariot. This is the actual position.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The living entity is always being influenced by the three qualities-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
sattva}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (goodness), }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 rajas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (passion) and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tamas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (ignorance). This is also confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
