\cs337\cf1\insrsid6643767 ,}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid10095509\charrsid10095509  who am above the modes and inexhaustible.}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid6643767 "}{\i\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid10095509  }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid6643767\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{
\cf1\insrsid6643767 7.13)}{\i\cf1\insrsid10095509\charrsid10095509 
\par }\pard \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf1\insrsid6643767 T}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 he living entity is bewildered
 by the three qualities of material nature. These three qualities are described in this verse as three flags. By a flag, one can come to know who the owner of the chariot is; similarly, by the influence of the three qualities of material nature, one can e
a
sily know the direction in which the chariot is moving. In other words, one who has eyes to see can understand how the body is being driven, influenced by the particular type of quality of material nature. In these three verses the activity of the living 
entity is described to prove how the body becomes influenced by the quality of ignorance, even when a person wants to be religious. N\'e4rada Muni wanted to prove to King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at that the King was being influenced by the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tamo-gu\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the quality of ignorance, even though the King was supposed to be very religious.
\par According to }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2\'e9ya,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the process of fruitive activities, a person performs various sacrifices directed by the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 and in all those sacrifices animal-killing, or experimenting on the life of animals to test the power of Vedic }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantras,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is enjoined. Animal-killing is certainly conducted under the influence of the mode of ignorance. Even though one may be religiously inclined, animal sacrifice is }{\cf1\insrsid6643767 nonetheless }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 recommended in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  not only in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 but even in the modern scriptures of other sects. These animal sacrifices are recommended in the name of religion, but actually animal sacrifice is meant for persons in the mode of ignorance. When such people kill animals, they can at lea
st do so in the name of religion. However, when the religious system is transcendental, like the Vai\'f1\'ebava religion, there is no place for animal sacrifice. Such a transcendental religious system is recommended by K\'e5\'f1\'eba in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya\line m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja\line aha\'e0 tv
\'e4\'e0 sarva-p\'e4pebhyo\line mok\'f1ayi\'f1y\'e4mi m\'e4 \'e7uca\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5263099 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
"Abandon all varieties of religion and just surrender unto Me. I shall deliver you from all sinful reaction. Do not fear." }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid5263099\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid5263099 18.66)
\par }\pard \s31\qj \fi397\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5263099 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Because King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at was engaged in performing various sacrifices in which animals were killed, N\'e4
rada Muni pointed out that such sacrifices are influenced by the mode of ignorance. From the very beginning of }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  it is said: }{\i\cf1\insrsid5263099\charrsid5263099 dharma\'f9}{
\cf1\insrsid5263099  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 projjhita-kaitavo 'tra}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5263099  (}{\cf1\insrsid5263099 1.1.2)}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  All kinds of r
eligious systems that are involved in cheating are completely kicked out of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhagavad-dharma,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 the religion dealing with one's relationship with the Supreme Personality of Godhead, animal sacrifice is not recommended. In the performance of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 \emdash Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare\emdash there is no recommendation for animal sacrifices.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 In these three verses, King Pura\'efjana's going to the forest to kill animals is symbolic of
 the living entity's being driven by the mode of ignorance and thus engaging in different activities for sense gratification. The material body itself indicates that the living entity is already influenced by the three modes of material nature and that he
 
is driven to enjoy material resources. When the body is influenced by the mode of ignorance, its infection becomes very acute. When it is influenced by the mode of passion, the infection is at the symptomatic stage. However, when the body is influenced by
 
the mode of goodness, the materialistic infection becomes purified. The ritualistic ceremonies recommended in religious systems are certainly on the platform of goodness, but because within this material world even the mode of goodness is sometimes pollut
ed by the other qualities (namely passion and ignorance), a man in goodness is sometimes driven by the influence of ignorance.
\par It is herein described that King Pura\'efjana once went to the forest to kill animals. This means that he, the living entity, came under the influence of the mode of ignorance. The forest in which King Pura\'efjana engaged in hunting was named Pa\'ef
ca-prastha. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pa\'efca}{\cf1\insrsid5263099  means five,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and this indicates the objects of the five senses. The body has five working senses, namely}{\cf1\insrsid5263099 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 the hands, the legs, the tongue, the rectum and the genitals. By taking full advantage of these working senses, the body enjoys material life. The chariot is driven by five horses, which represent the five sense organs\emdash 
namely the eyes, ears, nose, skin and tongue. These sense organs are very easily attracted by the sense objects. Consequently the horses are described as moving swiftly. On the chariot King Pura\'ef
jana kept two explosive weapons, which may be compared to }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 aha\'eck\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or false ego. This false ego is typified by two attitudes: "I am this body" (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ahant\'e4}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), and "Everything in my bodily relationships belongs to me" (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mamat\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ).
\par The two wheels of the chariot may be compared to the two moving facilities\emdash namely sinful life and religious life. The chariot is decorated with t
hree flags, which represent the three modes of material nature. The five kinds of obstacles, or uneven roads, represent the five kinds of air passing within the body. These are }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pr\'e4\'eba, ap\'e4na, ud\'e4na, sam\'e4na}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vy\'e4na.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The body itself is covered by seven coverings, namely}{\cf1\insrsid10487568 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  skin, muscle, fat, blood, marrow, bone and }{\cf1\insrsid10487568 
semen}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . The living entity is covered by three subtle material elements and five gross material elements. These are actually obstacles placed before the living entity on the path of liberation from material bondage.
\par The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ra\'e7mi}{\cf1\insrsid10487568  (rope}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) in this verse indicates the mind. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 n\'e9\'f2a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is also significant, for }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 n\'e9\'f2a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicates the nest where a bird takes rest. In this case }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 n\'e9\'f2a}{\cf1\insrsid10487568  is the heart}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 where the living entity is situated. The living entity sits in on
e place only. The causes of his bondage are two: namely lamentation and illusion. In material existence the living entity simply hankers to get something he can never get. Therefore he is in illusion. As a result of being in this illusory situation, the l
iving entity is always lamenting. Thus lamentation and illusion are described herein as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dvi-k\'fcbara,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the two posts of bondage.
\par The living entity carries out various desires through five different processes, which indicate the working of the five working senses. The golden ornaments and dress indicate that the living entity is influenced by the quality of }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 rajo-gu\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  passion. One who has a good deal of money or riches is especially driven by the mode of passion. Being influenced by the mode of passion, one desi
res so many things for enjoyment in this material world. The eleven commanders represent the ten senses and the mind. The mind is always making plans with the ten commanders to enjoy the material world. The forest named Pa\'ef
ca-prastha, where the King went to hunt, is the forest of the five sense objects: form, taste, sound, smell and touch. Thus in these three verses N\'e4rada Muni describes the position of the material body and the encagement of the living entity within it.

