\insrsid5197105 \emdash by this; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 r\'e4ja-indra}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash O King; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4nena}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash by advancement of knowledge; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 na}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash 
never; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 sa\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash he; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 lipyate}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash becomes involved.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10101918 {\b\cf11\insrsid10101918\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid10101918 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid5197105 N\'e4rada Muni continued to speak to King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at: }{
\fs28\insrsid5197105 My dear King, any person who works according to the directions of the Vedic scriptures does not become involved in fruitive activities.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid853019 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid853019\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Just as a government may issue trade licenses in order for its citizens to act in a certain way, the }
{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  contain injunctions that restrain and regulate all of our fruitive activities. All living entities have come into this material world to enjoy themselves. Consequently, the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are given to regulate sense enjoyment. One who enjoys his senses under the Vedic regulative principles does not become entangled in the actions and reactions of his activities. As stated in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8286382 :
\par }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid12918263 
\par }\pard \s124\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12918263 {\i\cf1\insrsid12918263\charrsid12918263 yaj\'ef\'e4rth\'e4t karma\'ebo 'nyatra
\par loko 'ya\'e0 karma-bandhana\'f9
\par tad-artha\'e0 karma kaunteya
\par mukta-sa\'ecga\'f9 sam\'e4cara
\par }\pard \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12918263 {\cf1\insrsid12918263 
\par }\pard \s124\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12918263 {\cf1\insrsid12918263 "}{\cf1\insrsid12918263\charrsid12918263 Work done as a sacrifice for Vi\'f1\'eb
u has to be performed, otherwise work binds one to this material world. Therefore, O son of Kunt\'e9, perform your prescribed duties for His satisfaction, and in that way you will always remain unattached and free from bondage.}{\cf1\insrsid12918263 " }{
\cs347\cf1\insrsid12918263\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid12918263 3.9)
\par }\pard \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
A human being is especially meant to attain liberation from the bondage of birth, death, old age and disease. He is therefore directed by the Vedic regulative principles to work in such a way that he may fulfill his d
esires for sense gratification and at the same time gradually become freed from material bondage. Action according to such principles is called knowledge. Indeed, the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 veda}{\cf1\insrsid9440223  means knowledge.}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  The words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4nena na sa lipyate}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicate that by following the Vedic principles, one does not become involved in the actions and reactions of his fruitive activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Everyone is therefore advised to act in terms of the Vedic injunctions and not irresponsibly. When a person within a state acts according to the laws a
nd licenses of the government, he does not become involved in criminal activities. Man-made laws, however, are always defective because they are made by men who are prone to committing mistakes, being illusioned, cheating and having imperfect senses. The 
Vedic instructions are different because they do not have these four defects. Vedic instructions are not subject to mistakes. The knowledge of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is knowledge received directly from God, and there is consequently no question of illusion, cheating, mistakes or imperfect senses. All Vedic knowledge is perfect because it is received directly from God by the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid9440223 parampar\'e4}
{\cf1\insrsid5197105  disciplic succession. In }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  it is said: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tene brahma h\'e5d\'e4 ya \'e4di-kavaye}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid9440223  }{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid9440223 (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid9440223 Bh\'e4g. }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid9440223\charrsid9440223 1.1.1}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid9440223 )}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The original creature of this universe, known as the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4di-kavi,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or Lord Brahm\'e4, was instructed by K\'e5\'f1\'eba through the heart. After receiving these Vedic instructions from Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself, Brahm\'e4 distributed the knowledge by the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 parampar\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  system to N\'e4rada, and N\'e4rada in turn distributed the knowledge to Vy\'e4
sa. In this way Vedic knowledge is perfect. If we act according to Vedic knowledge, there is no question of being involved in sinful activities.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.26.8
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 TEXT 8
