\par }\pard\plain \s268\qj \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 anyath\'e4}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash otherwise; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 karma}{
\insrsid5197105 \emdash fruitive activities; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 kurv\'e4\'eba\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash while acting; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 m\'e4na-\'e4r\'fc\'f2ha\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash being influenced by false prestige; }{
\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 nibadhyate}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash one becomes entangled; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 gu\'eba-prav\'e4ha}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash by the influence of the material qualities; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 patita\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 
\emdash fallen; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 na\'f1\'f6a-praj\'efa\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash bereft of all intelligence; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vrajati}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash thus he goes; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 adha\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash 
down.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10101918 {\b\cf11\insrsid10101918\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid10101918 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 Otherwise, a person who acts whimsically falls down due to fals
e prestige. Thus he becomes involved in the laws of nature, which are composed of the three qualities [goodness, passion and ignorance]. In this way a living entity becomes devoid of his real intelligence and becomes perpetually lost in the cycle of birth
 and death. Thus he goes up and down from a microbe in stool to a high position in the Brahmaloka planet.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid853019 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid853019\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 There are many important words in this verse. The first is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 anyath\'e4,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  "otherwise," which indicates one who does not care for the Vedic rules and regulations. The rules and regulations laid down in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7
\'e4stra-vidhi.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  clearly states that one who does not accept the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stra-vidhi,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  or rules and regulations mentioned in the Vedic scriptures, and acts whimsically or puffed up with false pride}{\cf1\insrsid6649929 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 never attains perfection in this life, nor does he attain happiness or liberation from the material condition.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 ya\'f9 \'e7\'e4stra-vidhim uts\'e5jya\line vartate k\'e4ma-k\'e4rata\'f9\line 
na sa siddhim av\'e4pnoti\line na sukha\'e0 na par\'e4\'e0 gatim
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "He who discards scriptural injunctions and acts according to his own whims attains neither perfection}{
\cf1\insrsid6649929 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  nor happiness}{\cf1\insrsid6649929 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  nor the supreme destination." (Bg. 16.23) }{\cf1\insrsid6649929 
\par }\pard \s31\qj \fi397\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6649929 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Thus one who is deliberately transgressing the rules and regulations of the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is simply involving himself more and more in material existence in the three modes of material nature. Human society should therefore follow the Vedic principles of life, which are summarized in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 .}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Otherwise life in material existence will continue. Foolish persons do not know
 that the soul is passing through 8,400,000 spieces of life. By the gradual process of evolution, when one comes to the human form of life, he is supposed to follow the rules and regulations laid down in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu says that the liv
ing entity, since time immemorial, is suffering the threefold miseries of material nature due to his demoniac attitude, which is his spirit of revolt against the Supreme Personality of Godhead. K\'e5\'f1\'eba also confirms this in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 mamaiv\'e4\'e0\'e7o j\'e9va-loke\line j\'e9va-bh\'fcta\'f9 san\'e4tana\'f9\line mana\'f9-
\'f1a\'f1\'f6h\'e4n\'e9ndriy\'e4\'ebi\line prak\'e5ti-sth\'e4ni kar\'f1ati
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
"The living entities in this conditioned world are My eternal, fragmental parts. Due to conditioned life, they are struggling very hard with the six senses, which include the mind." }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid3286642\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid3286642 
15.7) 
\par }\pard \s31\qj \fi380\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10227424 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Every living entity is part and parcel of God. There is no reason for the living entity's being put into the miserable threefold condition of material existence but that he voluntarily accepts material existence on the false pretext of becoming an 
enjoyer. To save him from this horrible condition, the Lord has given all the Vedic literatures in His incarnation of Vy\'e4sadeva. It is therefore said:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'e5\'f1\'eba bhuli' sei j\'e9va an\'e4di-bahirmukha\line ataeva m\'e4y\'e4 t\'e4
re deya sa\'e0s\'e4ra-du\'f9kha
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "By forgetting K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the liv
ing entity has become materialistic since time immemorial. Therefore the illusory energy of K\'e5\'f1\'eba is giving him different types of miseries in material existence." (}{\cs347\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid10227424 Cc}{
\cs347\cf1\insrsid10227424\charrsid10227424 .}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105  Mad}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid10227424 ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  20.117)
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4-mugdha j\'e9vera n\'e4hi svata\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-j\'ef\'e4na\line j\'e9vere k
\'e5p\'e4ya kail\'e4 k\'e5\'f1\'eba veda-pur\'e4\'eba
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "When a living entity is enchanted by the external energy, he cannot revive his original K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness independently. Due to such circumstances, K\'e5\'f1\'eba has kindly given him the Vedic literatures, such as the four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and eighteen }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Pur\'e4\'ebas.}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 " (}{\cs347\cf1\insrsid10227424\charrsid10227424 Cc.}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid10227424  Madya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  20.122) }{\cf1\insrsid10227424 
\par }\pard \s31\qj \fi397\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10227424 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Every human being should therefore take advantage of the Vedic instructions; otherwise one will be bound by his whimsical activities and will be without any guide.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4n\'e4r\'fc\'f2ha\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is also very significant in this verse. Under the pre
text of becoming great philosophers and scientists, men throughout the whole world are working on the mental platform. Such men are generally nondevotees, due to not caring for the instructions given by the Lord to the first living creature, Lord Brahm
\'e4. The }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  therefore says:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 har\'e4v abhaktasya kuto mahad-gu\'eb\'e4\line mano-rathen\'e4sati dh\'e4vato bahi\'f9}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10227424  }{\i0\cf1\insrsid10227424\charrsid10227424 (}{\cs347\cf1\insrsid10227424\charrsid10227424 Bh\'e4g. }{\i0\cf1\insrsid10227424\charrsid10227424 5.18.12)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
A person who is a nondevotee has no good qualifications because he acts on the mental platform. One who acts on the mental platform has to change 
his standard of knowledge periodically. We consequently see that one philosopher may disagree with another philosopher, and one scientist may put forward a theory contradicting the theory of another scientist. All of this is due to their working on the me
ntal platform without a standard of knowledge. In the Vedic instructions, however, the standard of knowledge is accepted, even though it may sometimes appear that the statements are contradictory. Because the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  are the standard of knowledge, even though they may appear contradictory, they should be accepted. If one does not accept them, he will be bound by the material conditions.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The material conditions are described in this verse as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gu\'eba-prav\'e4
ha,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the flowing of the three modes of material nature. \'c7r\'e9la Bhaktivinoda \'d6h\'e4kura therefore says in a song, }{\cf1\insrsid10227424 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 miche}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid10227424 )}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105  m\'e4y\'e4ra va\'e7e, y\'e4ccha bhese', kh\'e4ccha h\'e4bu\'f2ubu, bh\'e4i:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 "Why are you suffering? Why are you sometimes being drowned in the waves of material nature and sometimes coming to the surface?" }{\cf1\insrsid9722732 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 J\'e9va}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid9722732 )}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105  k
\'e5\'f1\'eba-d\'e4sa, ei vi\'e7v\'e4sa, karle ta' \'e4ra du\'f9kha n\'e4i:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  "Please therefore accept yourself as the servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Then you will be freed from all miseries." As soon as one surrenders to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and accepts the perfect standard of knowledge, which is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  as it is, 
he then comes out of the material modes of nature and does not fall down and lose his knowledge.
