\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
A materialistic person works throughout the whole week very, very hard. He is always asking, "Where is money? Where is money?" Then, at the end of the week, he wants to retire from these activities and go to some secluded place to rest. King Pura\'ef
jana returned to his home because he was very much fatigued from hunting animals in the forest. In this way his conscience came to stop him from committing further sinful activities and make him return home. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  materialistic persons are described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 du\'f1k\'e5tina\'f9,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 which indicates those who are always engaged in sinful activities. When a person comes to his senses and understands how he is engaging in sinful act
ivities, he returns to his conscience, which is herein figuratively described as the palace. Generally a materialistic person is infected by the material modes of passion and ignorance. The results of passion and ignorance are lust and greed. In the life 
of a materialist, activity means working in lust and greed. However, when he comes to his senses, he wants to retire. According to Vedic civilization, such retirement is positively recommended, and this portion of life is called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4naprastha.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Retirement is absolutely necessary for a materialist who wants to become free from the activities of a sinful life.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 King Pura\'ef
jana's coming home, taking bath and having an appropriate dinner indicate that a materialistic person must retire from sinful activities and beco
me purified by accepting a spiritual master and hearing from him about the values of life. If one would do this, he would feel completely refreshed, just as one feels after taking a bath. After receiving initiation from a bona fide spiritual master, one m
ust abandon all kinds of sinful activities, namely illicit sex, intoxication, gambling and meat-eating.
\par The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ucit\'e4h\'e4ra\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  used in this verse is important. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Ucita}{\cf1\insrsid14420271  means appropriate.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 One must eat appropriately and not take after food as hogs take after stool. For a human being there are eatables described in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs347\cf1\insrsid14184656\charrsid14184656  (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 17.8) as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4ttvika-\'e4h\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 or food in the mode of goodness. One should not indulge in eating food in the modes of passion and ignorance. This is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ucit\'e4h\'e4ra,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or appropriate eating. O
ne who is always eating meat or drinking liquor, which is eating and drinking in passion and ignorance, must give these things up so that his real consciousness may be awakened. In this way one may become peaceful and refreshed. If one is restless or fati
gued, one cannot understand the science of God. As stated in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid14420271\charrsid14420271 (}{\cf1\insrsid12064898\charrsid14420271 1}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid14420271 .}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 2.20):
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 eva\'e0 prasanna-manaso\line bhagavad-bhakti-yogata\'f9\line bhagavat-tattva-vij\'ef\'e4
na\'e0\line mukta-sa\'ecgasya j\'e4yate
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14420271 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Unless one can become free from the influence of passion and ignorance, he c
annot be pacified, and without being pacified, one cannot understand the science of God. King Pura\'efjana's returning home is indicative of man's returning to his original consciousness, known as K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness is absolutely necessary for one who has committed a lot of sinful activities, especially killing animals or hunting in the forest.
\par }\pard \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf1\insrsid14643438 
