When a man comes into good consciousness and accepts a saintly person as a spiritual master, he hears man
y Vedic instructions in the form of philosophy, stories, narrations about great devotees and transactions between God and His devotees. In this way a man becomes refreshed in mind, exactly like a person who smears scented sandalwood pulp all over his body
 and decorates himself with ornaments. These decorations may be compared to knowledge of religion and the self. Through such knowledge one becomes detached from a materialistic way of life and engages himself in always hearing }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and other Vedic literatures. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhv-ala\'eck\'e5ta}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  used in this verse indicates that one must be absorbed in knowledge gathered from the instructions of saintly persons. Just as King Pura\'efjana began to search out his better half, the Queen, one who is
 decorated with knowledge and instructions from saintly persons should try to search out his original consciousness, K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. One cannot return to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness unless he is favored by the instructions of a saintly person. Therefore \'c7r\'e9la Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura sings: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu-\'e7\'e4stra-guru-v\'e4kya, cittete kariy\'e4 aikya.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 If we want to become saintly persons, or if we want to return to our original K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, we must associate with }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4dhu}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (a saintly person), }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stra
}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (authoritative Vedic literature) and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 guru}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (a bona fide spiritual master). This is the process.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid14643438 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.26.13
