A neophyte devotee should neither eat too much nor collect more money than necessary. Eating too much or collecting too much is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 aty\'e4h\'e4ra.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  For such }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 aty\'e4h\'e4
ra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  one must endeavor very much. This is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pray\'e4sa.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Superficially one may show himself to be very much faithful to the rules and regulations}{\cf1\insrsid7942934  }{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 but at the same time not be fixed in the regulative principles. This is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 niyam\'e4graha.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  By mixing with undesirable persons, or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 jana-sa\'ecga,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  one becomes tainted with lust and greed and falls down from the path of devotional service.
