\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 In this verse the great sage N\'e4rada discloses that the character of Pura\'ef
jana was being described to give lessons to King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at. Actually the entire description was figuratively describing the activities of King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at. In this verse N\'e4rada frankly says "like you" (}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yath\'e4 bhav\'e4n}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), which indicates that King Pura\'efjana is none other than King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi\'f1at himself. Being a great Vai\'f1\'ebava, N\'e4rada Muni wanted to stop }{\cf1\insrsid1320245 
animal killing}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  in sacrifices. He knew that if he tried to stop the King from performing sacrifices, the King would not hear him. Therefore he is describing the life of Pura\'ef
jana. But in this verse he first discloses the intention, although not fully, by saying "like you." Generally the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karm\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 who are attached to increasing descendants, have to perform so many sacrifices and worship so many demigods for future generations, as well as to satisfy so many leaders, politicians, philosophers and scientists to make things go o
n properly for future generations. The so-called scientists are very eager to see that future generations will live very comfortably, and as such they are trying to find different means of generating energy to drive locomotives, cars, airplanes and so on.
 Now they are exhausting the petroleum supply. These activities are described in the }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid6057022 vyavas\'e4y\'e4tmik\'e4 buddhir}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 \line 
ekeha kuru-nandana\line bahu-\'e7\'e4kh\'e4 hy anant\'e4\'e7 ca\line buddhayo 'vyavas\'e4yin\'e4m
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6057022 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "Those who are on the spiritual path are resolute in purpose, and t
heir aim is one. O beloved child of the Kurus, the intelligence of those who are irresolute is many-branched."}{\cf1\insrsid11342287  }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid11342287\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid11342287 2.41)}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Actually, those who are in knowledge of everything are determined to execute K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, but those who are rascals (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), sinners (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 du\'f1k\'e5tina\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) and the lowest of mankind (}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nar\'e4dham\'e4\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), who are bereft of all intelligence (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid6057022 m\'e4yay\'e4pah\'e5ta-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
) and who take shelter of the demoniac way of life (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4sura\'e0 bh\'e4vam \'e4\'e7rit\'e4\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), are disinterested in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. As such they become im
plicated and take on so many activities. Most of these activities center around the killing of animals. Modern civilization is centered around }{\cf1\insrsid1320245 animal killing}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Karm\'e9s}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  are advertising that without eating meat, their vitamin value or vitality will be reduced;
 so to keep oneself fit to work hard, one must eat meat, and to digest meat, one must drink liquor, and to keep the balance of drinking wine and eating meat, one must have sufficient sexual intercourse to keep fit to work very hard like an ass.
\par There are two ways of }{\cf1\insrsid1320245 animal killing}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . One way is in the name of religious sacrifices. All the religions of the world\emdash except the Buddhists\emdash 
have a program for killing animals in places of worship. According to Vedic civilization, the animal-eaters are recommended to sacrifice a goat in the temple of}{\cf1\insrsid6057022  goddess}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  K\'e4l\'e9
 under certain restrictive rules and regulations and eat the flesh. Similarly, they are recommended to drink wine by worshiping the goddess Ca\'eb\'f2ik\'e4. The purpose is restriction. People have given up all this restr
iction. Now they are regularly opening wine distilleries and slaughterhouses and indulging in drinking alcohol and eating flesh. A Vai\'f1\'ebava }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4rya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  like N\'e4
rada Muni knows very well that persons engaged in such }{\cf1\insrsid1320245 animal killing}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  in the name of religion are cert
ainly becoming involved in the cycle of birth and death, forgetting the real aim of life: to go home, back to Godhead.
\par Thus the great sage N\'e4rada, while instructing }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  to Vy\'e4sa Muni, condemned the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 (fruitive) activities mentioned in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  N\'e4rada told Vy\'e4sa:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 jugupsita\'e0 dharma-k\'e5te 'nu\'e7\'e4sata\'f9\line sva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid6057022 -}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 bh\'e4va-raktasya mah\'e4n vyatikrama\'f9\line yad v\'e4kyato dharma it\'e9tara\'f9 sthito\line na manyate tasya niv\'e4ra\'eba\'e0 jana\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "The people in general are naturally inclined to enjoy, and you have encouraged them
 in that way in the name of religion. This is verily condemned and is quite unreasonable. Because they are guided under your instructions, they will accept such activities in the name of religion and will hardly care for prohibitions." }{
\i\cf1\insrsid16085486\charrsid16085486 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  1.5.15)
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9la N\'e4rada Muni chastised Vy\'e4
sadeva for compiling so many Vedic supplementary scriptures, which are all intended for guiding the people in general. N\'e4rada Muni condemned these scriptures because they do not mention direct devotional service. Under N\'e4rada's in
structions, direct worship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as described in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  was set forth by Vy\'e4sadeva. The conclusion is that neither the}{\cf1\insrsid4156016 
 Supreme Personality of Godhead Vi\'f1\'ebu}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  nor His devotee ever sanctions }{\cf1\insrsid1320245 animal killing}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  in the name of religion. Indeed, K\'e5\'f1\'eba incarnated Himself as Lord Buddha to put an end to 
}{\cf1\insrsid1320245 animal killing}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  in the name of religion. Animal sacrifice under the name of religion is conducted by the influence of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tamo-gu\'eba}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 (the mode of ignorance), as indicated in the Eighteenth Chapter of }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 yay\'e4 dharmam adharma\'e0 ca\line k\'e4rya\'e0 c\'e4k\'e4ryam eva ca\line ayath\'e4
vat praj\'e4n\'e4ti\line buddhi\'f9 s\'e4 p\'e4rtha r\'e4jas\'e9
\par adharma\'e0 dharmam iti y\'e4\line manyate tamas\'e4v\'e5t\'e4\line sarv\'e4rth\'e4n vipar\'e9t\'e4\'e0\'e7 ca\line buddhi\'f9 s\'e4 p\'e4rtha t\'e4mas\'e9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "That understanding which cannot
 distinguish between the religious way of life and the irreligious, between action that should be done and action that should not be done\emdash that imperfect understanding, O son of P\'e5th\'e4
, is in the mode of passion. That understanding which considers irreligion to be religion and religion to be irreligion, under the spell of illusion and darkness, and strives always in the wrong direction, O P\'e4rtha, is in the mode of ignorance."}{
\cf1\insrsid4156016  }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid4156016\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid4156016 18.31-32)}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
