\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
"The living entities in this conditioned world are My eternal, fragmental parts. Due to conditioned life, they are struggling very hard with the six senses, which include the mind."}{\cf1\insrsid6426960  }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid6426960\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }
{\cf1\insrsid6426960 15.7)}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The living entity is, after all, part and parcel of the Supreme Spirit, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. In other words, K\'e5\'f1\'eba's constitutional position and the living entity's constitutional position are the same qualitatively. The only difference is that the living entity is eternally an atomic particle of the Supreme Spirit. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Mamaiv\'e4\'e0\'e7o j\'e9va-loke j\'e9va-bh\'fcta\'f9 san\'e4tana\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 In this material world of conditional life, the fragmental portion of the Supreme Lord, the individual soul, is struggling due to his contaminated mind and consciousness. As part and parcel of the Supreme Lord, a living entity is supposed to think of K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, but here we see that King Pura\'efjana (the living entity) is thinking of a woman. Such mental absorption with some sense object brings about the living entity's struggle for existence in this material world. Since King Pura\'ef
jana is thinking of his wife, his struggle for existence in the material world will not be ended by death. As revealed in the following verses, King Pura\'efjana had to accept the body of a woman in his next life due to his being overly absorbed in
 thoughts of his wife. Thus mental absorption in social, political, pseudo}{\cf1\insrsid612672 -}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
religious, national and communal consciousness is cause for bondage. During one's lifetime one has to change his activities in order to attain release from bondage. This is confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
