\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 It is customary among }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriyas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 for a princess to be offered under certain conditions. For instance, Draupad\'e9 was offered in marriage to one who could pierce a fish with an arrow simply by seeing the reflection of that fish. K\'e5\'f1\'eba married one of His queens after conquering
 seven strong bulls. The Vedic system is for a daughter of a king to be offered under certain conditions. Vaidarbh\'e9
, the daughter of Vidarbha, was offered to a great devotee and powerful king. Since King Malayadhvaja was both a powerful king and great devo
tee, he fulfilled all the requirements. The name Malayadhvaja signifies a great devotee who stands as firm as Malaya Hill}{\cf1\insrsid10425500 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and, through his propaganda, makes other devotees similarly as firm. Such a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mah\'e4-bh\'e4gavata}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  can prevail over the opinions of all others. A strong devotee makes propaganda against all other spiritual conceptions\emdash namely }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 j\'ef\'e4na, karma}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yoga.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  With his devotional flag unfurled, he always stands fast to conquer other conceptions of transcendental realization. Whenever there is an argument be
tween a devotee and a nondevotee, the pure, strong devotee comes out victorious.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 p\'e4\'eb\'f2ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  comes from the word }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pa\'eb\'f2\'e4,}{\cf1\insrsid12010142  meaning knowledge.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Unless one is highly learned, he cannot conquer nondevotional conceptions. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 para}{\cf1\insrsid12010142 
 means }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 transcendent}{\cf1\insrsid12010142 al,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura}{\cf1\insrsid12010142  means city.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 para-pura}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 is Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha, the kingdom of God, and the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 jaya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 refers to one who can conquer. This means that a pure devotee, who is strong in devotional service and who has conquered all nondevotional conceptions, can also conquer the kingdom of God. In other words, one can conquer the kingdom of God, Vaiku\'eb\'f6
ha, only by rendering devotional service. The Supreme Personality of Godhead is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ajita,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  meaning that no one can conquer Him, but a devotee, by strong devotional service and 
sincere attachment to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, can easily conquer Him. Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is fear personified for everyone, but He voluntarily agreed to fear the stick of mother Ya\'e7od\'e4. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, God, cannot be conquered by anyone but His devotee. Such a devotee kindly married the daughter of King Vidarbha.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid2320539 
