n the material body, the Supersoul and the individual soul. There are two types of M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers\emdash the followers of the Buddhist philosophy and the followers of the \'c7a\'ec
kara philosophy. The followers of Buddha do not recognize that there is anything beyond the body; the followers of \'c7a\'eckara conclude that there is no separate existence of the Param\'e4tm\'e4, the Supersoul. The \'c7a\'ec
karites believe that the individual soul is identical with the Param\'e4tm\'e4 in the ultimate analysis. But the Vai\'f1\'ebava philosopher, who is perfect in knowledge, knows that the body is made of the external energy and that the Supersoul, the Param
\'e4tm\'e4, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is sitting with the individual soul and is distinct from him. As Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba states in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{
