\cf1\insrsid5197105  is very significant. In His Param\'e4tm\'e4 feature, K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the old friend of everyone. According to Vedic injunction, K\'e5\'f1\'eba is sitting with the living entity side by side. According to the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7ruti-mantra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dv\'e4 supar\'eb\'e4 sayuj\'e4 sakh\'e4y\'e4\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), the Lord is sitting within the heart of every living entity as }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 suh\'e5t,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the best friend. The Lord is always eager to have the living entity come home, back to Godhead. Sitting with the living entity as witness, the Lord gives him all chances to e
njoy himself materially, but whenever there is an opportunity, the Lord gives good counsel and advises the living entity to abandon trying to become happy through material adjustment and instead turn his face toward the Supreme Personality of Godhead and 
s
urrender unto Him. When one becomes serious to follow the mission of the spiritual master, his resolution is tantamount to seeing the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As explained before, this means meeting the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the instruc
tion of the spiritual master. This is technically called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4\'eb\'e9-sev\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura states in his }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  commentary on the verse }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vyavas\'e4y\'e4tmik\'e4 buddhir ekeha kuru-nandana}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 (Bg. 2.41) that one should serve the words of the spiritual master. The disciple must stick to whatever the spiritual master orders. Simply by following on that line, one sees the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Param\'e4tm\'e4, appeared before the Queen as a }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  but why didn't He appear in His original form as \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba? \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kura remarks that unless one is very highly elevated in loving the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one cannot see Him as He is. Nonetheless, if one sticks to the principles enuncia
ted by the spiritual master, somehow or other he is in association with the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Since the Lord is in the heart, He can advise a sincere disciple from within. This is also confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
