\cf1\insrsid5197105  from a realized soul.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 tad viddhi pra\'ebip\'e4tena\line paripra\'e7nena sevay\'e4\line upadek\'f1yanti te j\'ef
\'e4na\'e0\line j\'ef\'e4ninas tattva-dar\'e7ina\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "Just try to learn the truth by approaching a spiritual master. Inquire from him submissively an
d render service unto him. The self-realized soul can impart knowledge unto you because he has seen the truth." (}{\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid10758439 Bg.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  4.34)
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Thus one has to select a bona fide spiritual master and become enlightened to his original consciousness. In this way the individual 
soul can understand that he is always subordinate to the Supersoul. As soon as he declines to remain subordinate and tries to become an enjoyer, he begins his material conditioning. When he abandons this spirit of being an individual owner or enjoyer, he 
becomes situated in his liberated state. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sva-stha\'f9,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 meaning "situated in one's original position," is very significant in this verse. When one gives up his unwanted attitude of superiority, he becomes situated in his original position. The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tad-vyabhic\'e4re\'eba}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  is also significant, for it indicates that when one is separated from God due to disobedience, his real sense is lost. Again, by the grace of K\'e5\'f1\'eba and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 guru,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 he can be properly situated in his liberated position. These verses are spoken by \'c7r\'e9la N\'e4
rada Muni, and his purpose in speaking them is to revive our consciousness. Although the living entity and the Supersoul are one in quality, the individual soul has to pursue the instruction of the Supersoul. That is the state of liberation.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid2320539 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.28.65
\par }\pard\plain \s275\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 TEXT 65
\par }\pard\plain \s276\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s118\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f250\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 bihRZMa\'e0eTadDYaaTMa& Paarae+Yae<a Pa[diXaRTaMa( )\line 
YaTParae+aiPa[Yaae devae >aGavaNa( iv\'ec>aavNa" )) 65 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 barhi\'f1mann etad adhy\'e4tma\'e0
\par p\'e4rok\'f1ye\'eba pradar\'e7itam
\par yat parok\'f1a-priyo devo
\par bhagav\'e4n vi\'e7va-bh\'e4vana\'f9
\par }{\insrsid2320539 
\par }\pard\plain \s271\qj \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 SYNONYMS
\par }\pard\plain \s268\qj \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 barhi\'f1man}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash O King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 
etat}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash this; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 adhy\'e4tmam}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash narration of self-realization; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 p\'e4rok\'f1ye\'eba}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash indirectly; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 pradar\'e7itam}
{\insrsid5197105 \emdash instructed; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 yat}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash because; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 parok\'f1a-priya\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash interesting by indirect description; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 deva\'f9}{
\insrsid5197105 \emdash the Supreme Lord; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 bhagav\'e4n}{\insrsid10239684 \emdash }{\insrsid5197105 Personality of Godhead; }{\cs337\i\insrsid5197105 vi\'e7va-bh\'e4vana\'f9}{\insrsid5197105 \emdash the cause of all causes.
\par }\pard \s268\qc \li0\ri0\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10101918 {\b\cf11\insrsid10101918\charrsid3754542 TRANSLATION}{\insrsid10101918 
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s289\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid5197105 My dear King Pr\'e4c\'e9
nabarhi, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the cause of all causes, is celebrated to be known indirectly. Thus I have described the story of Pura\'efjana to you. Actually it is an instruction for self-realization.
\par }\pard \s289\qc \fi360\li0\ri0\sb36\sa36\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid853019 {\fs28\cf11\insrsid853019\charrsid3754542 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s280\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid5197105 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 There are many similar stories in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pur\'e4\'ebas}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  for self-realization. As stated in the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 parok\'f1a-priy\'e4 iva hi dev\'e4\'f9.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  There are many stories in the }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Pur\'e4\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  that are intended to interest ordinary men in transcendental subjects, but 
actually these refer to real facts. They are not to be considered stories without a transcendental purpose. Some of them refer to real historical facts. One should be interested, however, in the real purport of the story. Indirect instruction is quickly u
nderstandable for a common man. Factually the path of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti-yoga}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is the path of hearing directly about the pastimes of the Supreme Personality of Godhead (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid10239684 \'e7rava\'eba
\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), but those who are not interested in hearing directly about the activities of the Lord, or who cannot understand them, can very effectively hear such stories and fables as this one narrated by N
\'e4rada Muni.}{\cf1\insrsid10239684 
\par }{\fs96\cf1\insrsid10239684\charrsid10239684 _______________________________________________________________________________
\par }{\cf1\insrsid10239684 
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The following is a glossary of some of the important words in this chapter.
\par }\pard\plain \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10239684 \'c4de\'e7a}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'e4r\'e9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The actions resulting from sinful activities.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Agastya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The mind.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Am\'e4tya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The governor of the senses, the mind.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Arbuda-arbuda.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Various types of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7rava\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'e9rtana}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 of the Supreme Lord's name, quality, form and so on.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Ari.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Impediments like disease.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhoga.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Enjoyment. Herein this word refers to real enjoyment in spiritual life.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bh\'e5tya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The servants of the body, namely the senses.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Dravi\'f2a-r\'e4ja.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Devotional service or a person eligible to act in devotional service.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Dv\'e4ra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The doors of the body, such as the eyes and ears.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 G\'e5ha.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Home. For spiritual cultivation one requires an undisturbed place or the good association of devotees.

\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Idhmav\'e4ha.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The devotee who approaches the spiritual master. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Idhma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  refers to wood that is taken to burn as fuel for a fire. A }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  is supposed to take this }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 idhma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  to ignite the fire used in performing sacrifices. By spiritual instruction a }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmac\'e4ri}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  is trained to ignite a fire and offer oblations in the morning. He is supposed to go to the spiri
tual master to take lessons on transcendental subject matter, and the Vedic injunction is that when approaching the spiritual master one must carry with him fuel to perform }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 yaj\'efas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 or sacrifices. The exact Vedic injunction is as follows:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 tad-vij\'ef\'e4n\'e4rtha\'e0 sa gurum ev\'e4bhigacchet\line samit-p\'e4\'ebi\'f9 \'e7
rotriya\'e0 brahma-ni\'f1\'f6ham}{\cs337\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
"To learn transcendental subject matter, one must approach the spiritual master. In doing so, he should carry fuel to burn in sacrifice. The symptom of such a spiritual master is that he is expert in und}{\cf1\insrsid13265117 
erstanding the Vedic conclusion}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and therefore he constantly engages in the service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead." }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid13265117 (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid13265117\charrsid13265117 Mu\'eb\'f2aka Upani\'f1ad}{
\cf1\insrsid13265117  1.2.12) }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 By serving such a bona fide spiritual master, gradually a conditioned soul becomes detached from mat
erial enjoyment and invariably makes progress in spiritual realization under the direction of the spiritual master. Those who are misled by the illusory energy are never interested in approaching a spiritual master to make life successful.
\par }\pard\plain \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 J\'e4y\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Intelligence.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 J\'e9r\'eba-sarpa.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The fatigued air of life.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 K\'e4lakany\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The invalidity of old age.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 K\'e4ma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  A high fever.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Kul\'e4cala.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The place where there is no disturbance.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Ku\'f6umbin\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Intelligence.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Madirek\'f1a\'eb\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Madirek\'f1a\'eb\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 refers to one whose eyes are so attractive that one who observes them becomes maddened by her. In other words, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 madirek\'f1a\'eb\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  means a very beautiful young girl. According to J\'e9va Gosv
\'e4m\'e9, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 madirek\'f1a\'eb\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  means the personified deity of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  If one is attracted by the }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 bhakti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  cult, he becomes engaged in the service of the Lord and the spiritual master, and thus his life becomes successful. Vaidarbh\'e9
, the woman, became a follower of her husband. As she left her comfortable home for the service of her husband, }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid13265117 so }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 a serious student of spiritual understanding must give u
p everything for the service of the spiritual master. As stated by Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura, }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 yasy}{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid13265117 a pras\'e4d\'e4d bhagavat-pras\'e4da\'f9: }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  if one wants actual success in life, he must strictly follow the instructions of the spiritual master. By following such instructions, one is sure to make rapid progress in spiritual life. This statement by Vi\'e7van\'e4
tha Cakravart\'e9 is in pursuance of the following injunction from the }{\cs347\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c7vet\'e4\'e7vatara Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 yasya deve par\'e4 bhaktir\line yath\'e4 deve tath\'e4 gurau\line tasyaite kathit\'e4
 hy arth\'e4\'f9\line prak\'e4\'e7ante mah\'e4tmana\'f9}{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
"Only unto those great souls who have implicit faith in both the Lord and the spiritual master are all the imports of Vedic knowledge automatically revealed." }{\cf1\insrsid13265117 (}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5012641 \'c7vet. Up. }{\cf1\insrsid13265117 6.23)}
{\cf1\insrsid5012641  }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 In the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Ch\'e4ndogya Upani\'f1ad}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  it is said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4ryav\'e4n puru\'f1o veda:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 "One who approaches a bona fide spiritual master can understand everything about spiritual realization."
\par }\pard\plain \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Malayadhvaja.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  A nice devotee who is like sandalwood.

\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Pa\'efc\'e4la.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The five sense objects.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Paricchada.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The total aggregate of the senses.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Paura-jana.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The seven elements that constitute the body.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Pautra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Patience and gravity.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Prajv\'e4ra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  A kind of fever called }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'f1\'ebu jv\'e4ra.
\par Pratikriy\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Counteracting agents such as }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 mantras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  and medicines.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Pura-p\'e4laka.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The life air.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Putra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Consciousness.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Sainika.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The condition of threefold miseries.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Sapta-suta.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 The seven sons, namely hearing, chanting, remembering, offering prayers, serving the lotus feet of the Lord, worshiping the Deity}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5012641 ,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  and becoming a servant of the Lord.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Sauh\'e5dya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  Endeavor.
\par }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Suta.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The son of Vaidarbh\'e9, or, in 
other words, one who is somewhat advanced in fruitive activities and who comes in contact with a devotee spiritual master. Such a person becomes interested in the subject matter of devotional service.
\par }\pard \s159\ql \fi-1440\li1440\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0 {\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vaidarbh\'e9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  The woman who was formerly a man but took bi
rth as a woman in his next life because of too much attachment to woman. }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 Darbha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  means }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 ku\'e7a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  grass. In fruitive activities, or }{
\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2\'e9ya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  ceremonies, one requires }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 ku\'e7a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  grass. Thus }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 vaidarbh\'e9}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  refers to one who takes birth in a family of }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2\'e9ya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  understanding. However, if by }{\cs337\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105  activities one by chance comes in contact with a devotee, as Vaidarbh\'e9 did when she married Malayadhvaja, his life becomes successful. He then pursues the devotional service of the Lord. The conditioned soul becomes libe
rated simply by following the instructions of the bona fide spiritual master.
