\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 R
eal intelligence means linking with the Supreme Personality of Godhead. When this is done, the Supreme Personality of Godhead from within gives one the real intelligence by which one can return home, back to Godhead. Intelligence in the material world is 
described in this verse as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pramad\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  because in material existence the living entity falsely claims things to be his. He thinks, "I am the monarch of all I surve}{\cf1\insrsid4947349 
y." This is ignorance. Actually}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  nothing belongs to him. Even the body and the senses do not belong
 to him, for they are given to him by the grace of the Lord to satisfy his different propensities through the material energy. Nothing actually belongs to the living entity, but he becomes mad after everything, claiming, "This is mine. This is mine. This 
is mine." }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Janasya moho 'yam aha\'e0 mameti.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  This is called illusion. Nothing belongs to the living entity, but he claims that everything belongs to him. Lord Caitanya Mah\'e4
