\'f2a,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  fruitive activities and mental speculation. Being fixed in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, one can become free from the entanglement of birth and death and the vain struggle for existence. In these verses the words }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e5ga-t\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4\'e0 pradh\'e4vati}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 are very significant because the living entity is influenced by a thirst for sense enjoyment. He is like a deer that goes to the desert to search out water. In a desert an animal simply
