directly telling him, "Don't be interested in such temporary benefits." In modern civilization people are very much interested in exploiting the resources of material nature through the methods of science. Indeed, this is considered advancement. This is n
ot actually advancement, however, but is simply pleasing to hear. Although we are advancing according to such concocted methods, we are }{\cf1\insrsid3300742 nonetheless }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 forgetting our real purpose. Bhaktivinoda \'d6h\'e4
kura therefore says}{\cf1\insrsid3300742 :}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 ja\'f2a-vidy\'e4 yata m\'e4y\'e4ra vaib}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid3300742 hava tom\'e4ra bhajane b\'e4dh\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 "Materialistic studies are the glare of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  only, for they are an obstacle to spiritual progress."
