d unlimited desires for material enjoyment, and he has to transmigrate from one gross body to another until these desires are exhausted.
\par No living entity is free from the cycle of birth and death unless he takes to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness; therefore in this verse it is clearly stated (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sattvaika-ni\'f1\'f6he}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
) that when one is fully absorbed in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, in one stroke he is freed of past and future mental desires. Then, by the grace of the Supreme Lord, everything becomes simultaneously manifest within the mind. In this regard, Vi\'e7van
\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura cites the example of mother Ya\'e7od\'e4's seeing the whole cosmic manifestation within the mouth of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. By the grace of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, mother Ya\'e7od\'e4
 saw all the universes and planets within the mouth of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Similarly, by the grace of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, a K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious person can see all his dormant desires at one time and finish all his future transmigrations. This facility is especially given to the devotee to make his path clear for returning home, back to Godhead.
\par Why we see things not experienced in this life is explained herein. That which we see is the future expression of a gross body or is already stocked in our mental stockpile. Because a K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious person does not 
have to accept a future gross body, his recorded desires are fulfilled in a dream. We therefore sometimes find things in a dream never experienced in our present life.
