 is very important in this verse. When the saintly King Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi was induced by the great sage N\'e4
rada to leave home and take to the devotional service of the Lord, his sons had not yet returned from their austerities in the water. However, he did not wait for their return but simply left mes
sages to the effect that his sons were to protect the mass of citizens. According to V\'e9rar\'e4ghava \'c4c\'e4rya, such protection means organizing the citizens into the specific divisions of the four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'ebas}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  and four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4\'e7ramas.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  It was the responsibility of the royal order to see that the citizens were following the regulative principles of the four }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var
\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (namely }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid6899091 s}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 , k\'f1atriya}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid6899091 s}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 , vai\'e7ya}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid6899091 s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid6899091 s}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) and the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4\'e7ramas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  (namely }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 brahmacarya, g\'e5hastha, v\'e4naprastha}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sanny\'e4sa}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ). It is very difficult to rule citizens in a kingdom without organizing this }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  To rule the mass of citizens in a state and keep them in a complete progressive order is not possible simply by passing laws every year in a legislative assembly. The }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is essential in a good government. One class of men (the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
) must be intelligent and brahminically qualified, another class must be trained in administrative work (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), another in mercantile business (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vai\'e7ya}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) and another simply in labor (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ). These four class
es of men are already there according to nature, but it is the government's duty to see that all four of these classes follow the principles of their }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 var\'ebas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  methodically. This is called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 abhirak\'f1a\'eba,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or protection.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 It is significant that when Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Pr\'e4c\'e9
nabarhi was convinced of the goal of life through the instructions of N\'e4
rada, he did not wait even a moment to see his sons return, but left immediately. There were many things to be done upon the return of his sons, but he simply left them a message. He k
new what his prime duty was. He simply left instructions for his sons and went off for the purpose of spiritual advancement. This is the system of Vedic civilization.
\par \'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9 informs us that Kapil\'e4\'e7rama is located at the confluence of the Ganges and the Bay of Bengal, a place known now as Ga\'ecg\'e4-s\'e4
gara. This place is still famous as a place of pilgrimage, and many millions of people gather there every year on the day of Makara-sa\'eckr\'e4nti and take bath. It is called Kapil\'e4\'e7rama because of Lord Kapila's 
living there to perform His austerities and penances. Lord Kapila propounded the S\'e4\'eckhya system of philosophy.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid929492 
