"I worship Govinda, the primeval Lord, the first progenitor, who is tending the cows, yielding all desires, in abodes built with spiritual gems and surrounded by millions of purpose trees. He i
s always served with great reverence and affection by hundreds of thousands of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 lak\'f1m\'e9s,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gop\'e9s.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 " }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid4010281 (Bs. }{
\cf1\insrsid4010281 5.29) }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 Because this prayer was offered by Lord Brahm\'e4, we follow him by reciting this prayer. That is the easiest way to satisfy the Supreme Personality 
of Godhead. The pure devotee never attempts to reach the Supreme Lord directly. The most important way to worship the Lord is to go through the disciplic succession of devotees. The prayers offered by Lord \'c7
iva to the Supreme Personality of Godhead were thus repeated by the Pracet\'e4s, who were thus very successful in pleasing the Supreme Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Here the Supreme Personality of Godhead is described as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana.}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  According to Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya, the living entity is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  because he has become an inhabitant of this material world, and}{\cf1\insrsid9987393 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 under the influence of the three modes of material nature, he is forced to live within it. The Supreme Personality of Godhead creates this material world (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ), and He also enters within it. }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 A\'eb\'f2\'e4ntara-stha-param\'e4\'ebu-cay\'e4ntara-stham.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The Lord enters within the heart of the living entity and within the atom; therefore both the living entity and the Lord are called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  One }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the living entity, is subordinate to the supreme }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana;}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 therefore the duty of the subordinate }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  is to satisfy the supreme }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 pura\'efjana.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  That is devotional service. Lord Rudra, or Lord \'c7
iva, is the original }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e4c\'e4rya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  of the Vai\'f1\'ebava }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 samprad\'e4ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  called the Rudra-samprad\'e4ya. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Rudra-g\'e9tena}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  indicates that under the disciplic succession of Lord Rudra, the Pracet\'e4s achieved spiritual success.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid929492 
