Performing ten thousand years of severe austerities does not seem a happy endeavor. Yet the devotees, the serious students of spiritual life, undergo such austerities to attain the favor of the Supreme
 Personality of Godhead. At that time, when the duration of life was very long, people could undergo severe austerities for thousands of years. It is said that V\'e4lm\'e9ki, the author of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 R\'e4m\'e4ya\'eba,}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  underwent meditational austerities for }{\cf1\insrsid9987393 60,000}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  years. The Supreme Personality of Godhead appreciated the austerities undergone by the Pracet\'e4
s, and He finally appeared before them in a pleasing form. Thus they all became satisfied and forgot the austerities they underwent. In the material world, if one is successful af
ter hard labor, he is very pleased. Similarly, the devotee forgets all his labors and austerities as soon as he contacts the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Although Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was only a five-year-old boy, he underwent severe austerities by eating si
mply dry foliage, drinking only water and taking no food. In this way, after six months, he was able to see the Supreme Personality of Godhead face to face. When he saw the Lord, he forgot all his austerities and said, }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sv\'e4
min k\'e5t\'e4rtho'smi:}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  "My dear Lord, I am very pleased."
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Of course, these austerities were performed in the Satya-yuga, Dv\'e4para-yuga and Tret\'e4
