onsequently the devotee does not consider himself the proprietor of any occupation. The devotee always thinks of the Supreme Personality of Godhead as the proprietor; therefore the results of his business are offered to the Supreme Lord. One who thus l
ives in the material world with his family and children never becomes affected by the contaminations of the material world. This is confirmed in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs347\cf1\insrsid14184656\charrsid14184656  (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 3.9):
