\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The Third Chapter of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  specifically considers material activities for
 the purpose of sense gratification and material activities for the purpose of satisfying the Supreme Lord. The conclusion is that these are not one and the same. Material activities for sense gratification are the cause of material bondage, whereas the v
ery same activities for the satisfaction of K\'e5\'f1\'eba are the cause of liberation. How the same activity can be the cause of bondage and liberation can be explained as follows. One may get indigestion due to eating too many milk preparations\emdash 
condensed milk, sweet rice, and so on. But even though there is indigestion or diarrhea, another milk preparation\emdash yogurt mixed with black pepper and salt\emdash 
will immediately cure these maladies. In other words, one milk preparation can cause indigestion and diarrhea, and another milk preparation can cure them.
\par If one is placed in material opulence due to the special mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he should not consider that opulence a cause for bondage. When a mature devotee is blessed with material opulence, he doe}{\cf1\insrsid15229383 
s not become affected adversely}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid15229383 because}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 he knows how to employ material opulence in the service of the Lord. There are many such examples in the history of the world. There were kings like P\'e5thu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Janaka, Dhruva, Vaivasvata Manu and Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Ik\'f1v\'e4ku. All of these were great kings and were especially favored by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. If a devotee is not mature, the Supreme Lord will take away all his opulence. This principle is stated by the}{\cf1\insrsid15229383 
 Supreme Personality of Godhead: }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 yasy\'e4ham anug\'e5h\'eb\'e4mi hari\'f1ye tad-dhana\'e0 \'e7anai\'f9}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid15229383 .}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 "My first mercy shown to My devotee is to take away all his material opulence." Material opulence detrimental to devotional service is taken away by the Supreme Lord, whereas a person who is mature in devotional service is given all material facilities.

