A devotee is inspired by the Supersoul within the heart to advance in devotional service in a variety of ways. The devotee does not feel hackneyed or stereotyped, nor does he
 feel that he is in a stagnant position. In the material world, if one engages in chanting a material name, he will feel tired after chanting a few times. However, one can chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mah\'e4-mantra}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  all day and night and never feel tired. As chanting is increased, it will come out new and fresh. \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 said that if he could somehow get millions of ears and tongues, then he could relish spiritual bliss by chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 mah\'e4-mantra.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  There is really nothing uninspiring for a highly 
advanced devotee. In }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 the Lord says that He is situated in everyone's heart and that He helps the living entity forget and remember. By the grace of the Lord, the devotee gets inspiration.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 satata-yukt\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line bhajat\'e4\'e0 pr\'e9ti-p\'fcrvakam\line dad
