a-vigrah\'e4ya}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) that the Lord accepts three kinds of bodies (Vi\'f1\'ebu, Brahm\'e4 and \'c7
iva) for the purposes of creating, maintaining and annihilating the cosmic manifestation. The three predominating deities of the material universe (Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and \'c7iva) are called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 gu\'eba-avat\'e4ras.}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  There are many kinds of incarnations of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and the first incarnations within this material world are Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and Mahe\'e7vara (\'c7iva). Out of these three, Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva accept material bodies, but Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu does not accept a material body. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is therefore known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'e7uddha-sattva.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 His existence is completely free from the contamination of the material modes of nature. One should therefore not think that Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is in the same category with Lord Brahm\'e4 and \'c7iva. The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7\'e4stras}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  forbid us to think in this way.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 yas tu n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba\'e0 deva\'e0\line brahma-rudr\'e4di-daivatai\'f9\line 
samatvenaiva v\'e9k\'f1eta\line sa p\'e4\'f1a\'eb\'f2\'e9 bhaved dhruvam }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 One who considers Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu to be in the same category with }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 devas}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  like Lord Brahm\'e4 or Lord \'c7iva or who thinks Lord Brahm\'e4 and \'c7iva to be equal to Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is to be considered as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 p\'e4\'f1a\'eb\'f2\'e9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 (a faithless nonbeliever). Therefore in this verse Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is distinguished in the words }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 namo vi\'e7uddha-sattv\'e4ya.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Although a living entity like us, Lord Brahm\'e4
 is exalted due to his pious activities; therefore he is given the high post of Brahm\'e4. Lord \'c7iva is not actually like a living entity, but he is not the Supreme Personality of Godhead. His position is somewhere between Vi\'f1\'ebu, the Supreme Pe
rsonality of Godhead, and Brahm\'e4, the living entity. Lord \'c7iva is therefore explained in }{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahma-sa\'e0hit}{\cs347\cf1\insrsid14184656\charrsid14184656 \'e4 (Bg. }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 5.45) in this way:
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1\'e9ra\'e0 yath\'e4 dadhi vik\'e4ra-vi\'e7e\'f1a-yog\'e4t\line sa\'efj\'e4
yate na hi tata\'f9 p\'e5thag asti heto\'f9\line ya\'f9 \'e7ambhut\'e4m api tath\'e4 samupaiti k\'e4ry\'e4d\line govindam \'e4di-puru\'f1a\'e0 tam aha\'e0 bhaj\'e4mi
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Lord \'c7iva is considered to be like yogurt (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 dadhi}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
). Yogurt is nothing but transformed milk; nonetheless yogurt cannot be accepted as milk. Similarly, Lord \'c7iva holds almost all the powers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, and he is also above the qualities of the living entity, but he is not exactly like Vi\'f1
\'ebu, just as yogurt, although transformed milk, is not exactly like milk.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The Supreme Personality of Godhead is also described herein as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 v\'e4
sudev\'e4ya k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4ya.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the original Supreme Personality of Godhead, and all Vi\'f1\'ebu expansions are His plenary portions or portions of His plenary portions (known as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sv
\'e4\'e0\'e7a}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 kal\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ). The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sv\'e4\'e0\'e7a,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  or direct expansion, is also called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 a\'e0\'e7a.}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  All }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 vi\'f1\'ebu-tattvas}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 sv\'e4\'e0\'e7a,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  direct parts and parcels of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba. K\'e5
\'f1\'eba is known as V\'e4sudeva because He appeared in this material world as the son of Vasudeva. Similarly, He is known as Devak\'e9-nandana, Ya\'e7od\'e4-nandana, Nanda-nandana}{\cf1\insrsid11692057 ,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  and so on.
\par Again and again the Lord is very much interested in increasing the influence of His devotees. Therefore He is described herein as }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 prabhave sarva-s\'e4tvat\'e4m.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 s\'e4
tvata}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  community is a community of Vai\'f1\'ebavas, pure devotees of the Lord. The Supreme Personality of Godhead has unlimited powers, and He wants t
o see that His devotees are also entrusted with unlimited powers. A devotee of the Lord is always, therefore, distinguished from all other living entities.
\par The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 hari}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  means "one who takes away all miserable conditions," and }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 hari-medhase}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  means that the L
ord is always planning ways to deliver the conditioned soul from the clutches of }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 The Lord is so kind that He personally incarnates to deliver the conditioned souls, and whenever He comes, He makes His plans.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 paritr\'e4\'eb\'e4ya s\'e4dh\'fcn\'e4\'e0\line vin\'e4\'e7\'e4ya ca du\'f1k\'e5t\'e4m
