\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 There was no need for the Pracet\'e4s to ask any ben
ediction from the Supreme Lord because the devotees are simply satisfied by the presence of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja practiced severe austerities and penances to see the Supreme Lord, and his intention was to receive benediction from the Lord. He wanted to acquire the throne of his father\emdash or attain an even better position\emdash 
but when he was actually in the presence of the Supreme Lord, he forgot everything. He said, "My dear Lord, I do not wish to ask any benediction." This is the ac
tual position of the devotee. The devotee simply wants to be in the presence of the Supreme Lord\emdash either in this world or in the next\emdash and engage in His service. That is the ultimate goal and benediction for the devotees.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The Lord asked the Pracet\'e4s to pray 
for some benediction, and they said, "What kind of benediction should we pray for? The Lord is unlimited, and there are unlimited benedictions." The purport is that if one must ask for benediction, he must ask for unlimited benediction. The words }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 tvat parata\'f9}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  are very significant in this verse. The Supreme Personality of Godhead is }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 parata\'f9 par\'e4t.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 
para}{\cf1\insrsid10748191  means }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 transcendent}{\cf1\insrsid10748191 al, beyond this material world.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  The impersonal Brahman effulgence is beyond this material world, and this is called }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 para\'e0 padam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c4ruhya k\'e5cchre\'eba para\'e0 padam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid7677979 (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid15149873\charrsid15149873 Bh\'e4g. }{
\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid7677979 10.2.32)}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 . Merging into the impersonal effulgence of the Lord is called }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 para\'e0 padam,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 but there is a higher transcendental position, which is the association of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Brahmeti param\'e4tmeti bhagav\'e4n iti \'e7abdyate}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{
\i\cf1\insrsid16085486\charrsid16085486 (Bh\'e4g.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  1.2.11). The Absolute Truth is realized first as impersonal Brahman, then as Param\'e4tm\'e4, and finally as Bhagav\'e4n. Thus the Personality of Godhead, Bhagav\'e4n, is }{
\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 parata\'f9 par\'e4t,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  beyond Brahman and Param\'e4tm\'e4 realization. In this connection, \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9 points out that }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 parata\'f9 par\'e4t}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  means "better than the best." The best is the spiritual world, and it is known as Brahman. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, however, is known as Parabrahman. Therefore }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 parata\'f9 par\'e4t}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  means "better than Brahman realization."
\par As will be explained in the next verses, the Pracet\'e4s planned to ask the Lord for something that has no limit. The Lord's pastimes, qualities, forms and names are all unlimited. There is no limit to His name, forms, pastimes, creatio
n and paraphernalia. The living entity cannot conceive of the unlimitedness of the unlimited. However, if living entities are engaged in hearing about the unlimited potencies of the Supreme Lord, they are factually connected directly to the unlimited. Suc
h understanding of the unlimited becomes unlimited by hearing and chanting.
\par }{\cf1\insrsid929492 
\par }\pard\plain \s304\qr \li0\ri0\sb300\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 SB 4.30.32
