am:}{\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105  }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 the real perfection of life is pleasing the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9:}{\cf1\insrsid6239582  I}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
n understanding the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Vedas,}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  one has to understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead. One who has actually understood Him surrenders unto Him after many, many births. We find all these qualif
ications in the Pracet\'e4
s. They underwent severe austerities and penances within the water, and they did not take any food for a very long time. They practiced these austerities not for material benediction but for the satisfaction of the Supreme Lord. One 
may engage in any business\emdash material or spiritual\emdash 
but the purpose should be the satisfaction of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This verse presents a perfect picture of Vedic civilization. People training to become devotees should be respectful not only
 to the Supreme Personality of Godhead but also to those who are elderly in knowledge, who are \'c4ryans and actual devotees of the Lord. An }{\cf1\insrsid6239582 \'c4ryan is one who does not boast}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 but is an actual devotee of the Lord. }{\cs337\cf1\insrsid5197105\charrsid5340652 \'c4ryan}{\cf1\insrsid5340652  means advanced.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Formerly, those who claimed to be \'c4ryans had to be devotees of the Lord. For instance, in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs347\cf1\insrsid14184656\charrsid14184656  }{\cf1\insrsid5197105 K\'e5\'f1\'eba chastised Arjuna by saying that he was speaking like a non-\'c4ryan.
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'e7r\'e9-bhagav\'e4n uv\'e4ca\line kutas tv\'e4 ka\'e7malam ida\'e0\line vi\'f1
ame samupasthitam\line an\'e4rya-ju\'f1\'f6am asvargyam\line ak\'e9rti-karam arjuna
\par }\pard\plain \s31\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 "The Supreme Person [Bhagav\'e4
n] said: My dear Arjuna, how have these impurities come upon you? They are not at all befitting a man who knows the progressive values of life. They do not lead to higher planets, but to infamy." }{\cs347\cf1\insrsid5340652\charrsid14184656 (Bg. }{
\cf1\insrsid5340652 2.2)
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5340652 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid5197105 Arjuna, the }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 k\'f1atriya,}{\insrsid5197105 
 was refusing to fight despite being directly ordered by the Supreme Lord. He was thus chastised by the Lord as belonging to a non-\'c4
ryan family. Anyone who is advanced in the devotional service of the Lord certainly knows his duty. It does not matter whether his duty is violent or nonviolent. If it is sanctioned and ordered by the Supreme Lord, it must be performed. An \'c4
ryan performs his duty. It is not that the \'c4ryans are unnecessarily inimical to living entities. The \'c4ryans never maintain slaughterhouses, and they are never enemies of poor animals. The Pracet\'e4
s underwent severe austerities for many, many years, even within the water. Accepting austerities and penances is the avowed business of those interested in advanced civilization.
\par }\pard \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 The word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 nirandhas\'e4m}{\cf1\insrsid5340652  means without food.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 Eating voraciously and unnecessarily is not the business of an \'c4ryan. Rather, the eating process should be restricted as far as possible. When \'c4ryans eat, they eat only prescribed eatables. Regarding this, the Lord says in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
