\par }\pard\plain \s124\qj \fi360\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva, Manu (the father of mankind), great saintly persons a
nd also great sages who have elevated themselves to the transcendental platform through austerities and penance, as well as devotional service, are imperfect in knowledge compared to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is the case with anyone within 
this material world. No one can be equal to the Supreme Lord in anything, certainly}{\cf1\insrsid534708  not in knowledge. Consequently}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 anyone's prayer to the Supreme Personality of Godhead is never complete. It is not possible to measure the complete glories of the Supreme Lord, who is unlimited. Even the Lord Himse}{\cf1\insrsid534708 lf in His incarnation as Ananta}{
\cf1\insrsid5197105  or \'c7e\'f1a, cannot describe His own glories. Although Ananta has many thousands of faces and has been glorifying the Lord for many, many years, He could not find the limit of the glories 
of the Lord. Thus it is not possible to estimate the complete potencies and glories of the Supreme Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 
Nonetheless, everyone in devotional service can offer essential prayers to the Lord. Everyone is situated in a relative position, and no one is perfect in glorifying the Lord. Beginning with Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva down to ourselves, everyone is the servant of the Supreme Lord. We are all situated in relative positions according to our own }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 karma.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  Yet every one of us can offer prayers with heart and sou
l as far as we can appreciate the Lord's glories. That is our perfection. Even when one is in the darkest region of existence, he is allowed to offer prayers to the Lord according to his own capacity. The Lord therefore says in }{
\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 Bhagavad-}{\cs347\i\cf1\insrsid8601574\charrsid8601574 g\'e9t\'e4}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 :
\par }\pard\plain \s302\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid5197105 m\'e4\'e0 hi p\'e4rtha vyap\'e4\'e7ritya\line ye 'pi syu\'f9 p\'e4pa-yonaya\'f9\line 
