\cf1\insrsid876317  (}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 s}{\cf1\insrsid876317 imultaneously one and different}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ) propounded by Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu. The Supreme Personality of Godhead is simultaneously different and nondifferent from this cosmic manifestation. In }{\cf1\insrsid876317 the}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  previous verse it has been explained that the Supreme Personality of Godhead, }{
\cf1\insrsid876317 as}{\cf1\insrsid5197105  the root of a tree, is the original cause of 
everything. It was also explained how the Supreme Personality of Godhead is all-pervasive. He is present within everything in this material manifestation. Since the energy of the Supreme Lord is nondifferent from Him, this material cosmic manifestation is
 
also nondifferent from Him, although it appears different. The sunshine is not different from the sun itself, but it is simultaneously also different. One may be in the sunshine, but he is not on the sun itself. Those who live in this material world are l
iving on the bodily rays of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but they cannot see Him personally in the material condition.
\par }\pard\plain \s216\qj \fi357\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cf1\insrsid5197105 In this verse the word }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 padam}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 indicates the place where the Supreme Personality of Godhead resides. As confirmed in }{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 \'c9\'e7opani\'f1ad, \'e9\'e7\'e4v\'e4syam ida\'e0 sarvam.}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 The proprietor of a house may live in one room of the house}{\cf1\highlight7\insrsid876317\charrsid661063 .}{\cf1\insrsid661063 *}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 
 but the entire house belongs to him. A king may live in one room in Buckingham Palace, but the entire palace is considered his property. It is not necessary for the kin
g to live in every room of that palace for it to be his. He may be physically absent from the rooms, but still the entire palace is understood to be his royal domicile.
\par The sunshine is light, the sun globe itself is light, and the sun-god is also light. However, the sunshine is not identical with the sun-god, Vivasv\'e4n. This is the meaning of simultaneously one and different (}{\cs337\i\cf1\insrsid5197105 acintya-bhed
\'e4bheda-tattva}{\cf1\insrsid5197105 ). All the planets rest on the sunshine, and because of the heat of the sun, they all revolve in their orbits
. On each and every planet, the trees and plants grow and change colors due to the sunshine. Being the rays of the sun, the sunshine is nondifferent from the sun. Similarly, all the planets, resting on the sunshine, are nondifferent from the sun. The enti
re material world is completely dependent on the sun, being produced by the sun, and the cause, the sun, is inherent in the effects. Similarly, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is the cause of all causes, and the effects are permeated by the original cause. The entire cosmic manifestation should be understood as the expanded energy of the Supreme Lord.
\par When one sleeps, the senses are inactive, but this does not mean that the senses are absent. When one is awakened, the senses become active again. Similarly, this cosmic creation is sometimes ma}{\cf1\insrsid3157012 nifest and sometimes unmanifest. A}{
